<node id="ICD Category">
  <data key="d0">ICD Category</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ICD Category is indicated as “Various” for Acrocyanosis in the medical entry.&lt;SEP&gt;ICD Category groups congenital heart defects under various diagnostic codes for medical classification.&lt;SEP&gt;ICD Category indicates the medical coding classification applicable to Infertility Drugs.&lt;SEP&gt;ICD Category denotes that personality disorders fall under various International Classification of Diseases categories.&lt;SEP&gt;ICD Category indicates that postpolio syndrome falls under various ICD classifications.&lt;SEP&gt;ICD Category denotes that Qigong is associated with various categories in the International Classification of Diseases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8f16eabbb20e5fbb76381361fce2e83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56ef10afa5a5d842dfa90eafc05da760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d5f82c915dbc402d1fdeb23f98439f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71b04609b9999bd4f4017776dc567f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2da2e6ea84de29321c6bb6647758bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b20a7bdac3dcdeae955d7f5fcff8809</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426248</data>
</node>
<node id="Severity Level">
  <data key="d0">Severity Level</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Severity Level is a categorical attribute used in medical documentation to convey the assessed intensity or seriousness of a condition, procedure, drug class, or test result. It serves as a standardized way to indicate how severe or mild a health‑related issue is, supporting clinical decision‑making and data analysis.

In the provided records, Severity Level is assigned as follows: it is marked **Moderate** for both Acrocyanosis and immunosuppression, reflecting a middle‑range seriousness; it is designated **Severe** for Pickwickian syndrome, indicating a high level of clinical concern. For several other items the level is recorded as **Unknown**, showing that the seriousness could not be determined or was not specified. These items include alcoholism, anti‑hemorrhoid drug classifications, arthroscopy, the Immune Complex Test, and photosensitivity.

The mixture of specified (moderate, severe) and unknown entries illustrates that Severity Level can be explicitly defined when sufficient clinical information is available, but may remain indeterminate in cases where evidence is lacking, the condition is heterogeneous, or the assessment has not been performed.&lt;SEP&gt;Severity Level denotes that postpolio syndrome is classified as severe.&lt;SEP&gt;Severity Level indicates that the seriousness of Qigong as a condition is unknown.&lt;SEP&gt;Indicates the moderate severity associated with the Quadrantectomy procedure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8f16eabbb20e5fbb76381361fce2e83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b83572ef3bc13b6de1b3591b9a778c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b29429d857edf1192105634eda51b928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71b04609b9999bd4f4017776dc567f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2da2e6ea84de29321c6bb6647758bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afe775e3de6a2ede3813b294c2d7085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8049c6dc0f71e37cbd8d3611d0687a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b5b4ede4683a3be477e4527fbbb8cad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5479288509bdc5dc1bd82e1d305f9ed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b03362a1a14b83e88e498b918bc854</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426462</data>
</node>
<node id="Acrocyanosis">
  <data key="d0">Acrocyanosis</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f2da2e6ea84de29321c6bb6647758bc</data>
  <data key="d2">Acrocyanosis is classified under the ICD Category listed as Various.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372779</data>
</node>
<node id="Acoustic Neuroma">
  <data key="d0">Acoustic Neuroma</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acoustic Neuroma is a benign tumor involving cells of the myelin sheath that surrounds the vestibulocochlear nerve.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372986</data>
</node>
<node id="Myelin Sheath">
  <data key="d0">Myelin Sheath</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Myelin sheath is the insulating layer of cells surrounding nerve fibers, including those of the vestibulocochlear nerve.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372986</data>
</node>
<node id="Vestibulocochlear Nerve">
  <data key="d0">Vestibulocochlear Nerve</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Vestibulocochlear nerve is the eighth cranial nerve that connects the inner ear to the brain and consists of vestibular and cochlear branches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372986</data>
</node>
<node id="Inner Ear">
  <data key="d0">Inner Ear</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Inner ear is the auditory organ from which the vestibulocochlear nerve originates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372986</data>
</node>
<node id="Brain">
  <data key="d0">Brain</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Brain is the central organ of the nervous system that integrates and regulates a wide array of bodily functions. It receives sensory input from many cranial nerves, including signals from the vestibulocochlear nerve that convey balance and auditory information, and it processes visual data from the eyes, capable of suppressing input from an amblyopic eye to prioritize clearer visual signals. The brain also monitors sensory information originating in the diaphragm, adjusting neural messages that control diaphragm contraction and thereby influencing respiration.

Within the brain, the hypothalamus resides as a key regulatory hub, coordinating autonomic and endocrine activities throughout the nervous system. Chemical messengers produced in the brain govern fundamental drives such as hunger, and these pathways can be modulated by appetite‑suppressant drugs. The organ’s structure and function are vulnerable to various pathological conditions: chronic addiction can remodel neural circuits, leading to dependence and compulsive behavior; loss of myelin in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy damages white‑matter integrity; and neurodegenerative processes in Alzheimer’s disease cause neuron loss, resulting in brain atrophy and reduced size. Together, these roles and susceptibilities illustrate the brain’s essential position as the command center for sensory integration, physiological regulation, and behavioral control.&lt;SEP&gt;The brain is the organ in which ventricles, choroid plexus, and cerebrospinal fluid are located and where hydrocephalus occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;The brain is the central organ of the nervous system that houses the pituitary gland at its base.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df310a5eb710fa15878efbe7d25bc7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49690ebe88a03e6a7140692753a7c25a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd6df79e5db44ce548291f0e8d6d6cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9098e6c377264351e34498ab20d1d2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee26fc83e6a72a8d68824995539e61e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427a659d0ef51d2588b292e6329fb824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff53a187c372ebdee1b2526a7ad3f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-414a580eb00a7d0d58696314c2aa7dfe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410820</data>
</node>
<node id="Vestibular Nerve">
  <data key="d0">Vestibular Nerve</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Vestibular nerve is the vestibular branch of the vestibulocochlear nerve involved in balance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372986</data>
</node>
<node id="Cochlear Nerve">
  <data key="d0">Cochlear Nerve</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cochlear nerve is the cochlear branch of the vestibulocochlear nerve responsible for hearing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372986</data>
</node>
<node id="NF2 Gene">
  <data key="d0">NF2 Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">NF2 gene is a tumor suppressor gene whose loss or mutation can lead to development of acoustic neuroma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372986</data>
</node>
<node id="Hearing Loss">
  <data key="d0">Hearing Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hearing loss is a reduction in ability to hear, commonly the first symptom of acoustic neuroma.&lt;SEP&gt;Hearing loss is a potential consequence of untreated acute otitis media in Achondroplasia patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Any degree of impairment in the ability to apprehend sound, arising from hereditary factors, environmental exposure to loud sounds, obstructions, infections, and other causes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bafb2bd57a03b4eb45b6b85949d2efef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0df4e770c55ce326a53bf6ab0d1f1b74</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403702</data>
</node>
<node id="Unilateral Hearing Loss">
  <data key="d0">Unilateral Hearing Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unilateral hearing loss is hearing loss that is more severe in one ear than the other and may indicate acoustic neuroma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372987</data>
</node>
<node id="Tinnitus">
  <data key="d0">Tinnitus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tinnitus is a ringing sound in the ears often accompanying hearing loss in acoustic neuroma patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372987</data>
</node>
<node id="Pure Tone Audiometry">
  <data key="d0">Pure Tone Audiometry</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pure tone audiometry is a hearing test that measures ability to hear tones of different volume and pitch.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372987</data>
</node>
<node id="Speech Audiometry">
  <data key="d0">Speech Audiometry</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Speech audiometry is a hearing test that measures ability to understand spoken speech.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372987</data>
</node>
<node id="Surgery">
  <data key="d0">Surgery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Surgery is a medical intervention that encompasses a wide range of operative procedures used to treat various conditions. It can involve the operative removal of specific tumors, such as an acoustic neuroma, and is frequently employed to excise malignant growths in the head and neck region, particularly cancers of the lip and mouth. In oncology, surgery is often combined with anticancer drug therapy to enhance treatment efficacy.

In the gastrointestinal and anorectal fields, surgery is required for severe hemorrhoids and fissures, as well as for the management of anorectal abscesses and fistulas. These procedures aim to remove diseased tissue, relieve symptoms, and prevent complications.

Cardiovascular surgery includes corrective operations on the heart or its valves and is used as a treatment option for heart failure and related structural abnormalities. By restoring normal cardiac function, such interventions can improve patient outcomes.

While surgery offers therapeutic benefits, it also carries risks. Breaching natural barriers during operative procedures can increase the likelihood of anaerobic infections, necessitating careful aseptic technique and postoperative monitoring.

Overall, surgery is mentioned as a possible treatment across many medical specialties, serving as a cornerstone of modern therapeutic practice when non‑operative options are insufficient or when definitive removal of pathology is required.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical intervention that may be required to treat heart murmurs caused by structural defects.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgery is the primary treatment of choice for both hypospadias and epispadias, recommended to be performed early.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgical procedure to remove pinguecula or pterygium when it affects the cornea or causes discomfort, inflammation, or cosmetic concerns.&lt;SEP&gt;... description.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgery is the primary method used to treat ptosis, performed outpatient under local anesthetic.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgery is a medical method used to correct anatomical abnormalities such as pyloric stenosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c54bf8feacba012d420dc1bafe3e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3167aac9bbeb660fe5ef8b641759df31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1acfa8b3bcf6abb174b1db6c3878690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14488136ba3c8174aecc9163f5e16196&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cf07655a8780ee831372742398affa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf2a4a7521a933797a5c97cd08b21a3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-910d4bcf6932bd29fd1d161e11852b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f76892a4be4a69badd2654de9e4d916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7db5d994bc1563d4fe5ab322fe7f3808&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14cced56b63272cdcfcc286787f3aa8d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426471</data>
</node>
<node id="Radiation">
  <data key="d0">Radiation</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Radiation is a treatment option that uses targeted radiation to control acoustic neuroma growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation is a source that can cause increased formation of free radicals in the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd48b3d64142d95730163769979b3bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786386827</data>
</node>
<node id="Observation">
  <data key="d0">Observation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Observation is a treatment approach involving monitoring the acoustic neuroma without immediate intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;Observation of hiccup sounds is a diagnostic method for identifying hiccups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9098e6c377264351e34498ab20d1d2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405753</data>
</node>
<node id="Physician">
  <data key="d0">Physician</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Physician is a medical professional who, across a wide range of specialties, provides diagnostic, therapeutic, and advisory services to patients. In the context of neuro‑oncology, a physician discusses treatment options with individuals diagnosed with acoustic neuroma, helping patients understand the risks and benefits of surgery, radiation, or observation. In gastroenterology and colorectal care, the physician conducts a visual inspection of the perianal skin and may perform a rectal examination using a gloved finger to assess for pathology. 

Physicians are also the prescribers of systemic medications that require professional oversight, such as anticoagulant and antiplatelet agents, and they are consulted for detailed guidance on anti‑hemorrhoid drugs, including dosage instructions, potential complications, and patient counseling. Those physicians who have completed specialized surgical training are qualified to carry out general surgery procedures, applying operative techniques to treat a variety of intra‑abdominal and soft‑tissue conditions. In gynecology, a physician may perform hysteroscopy, inserting a hysteroscope through the vagina and cervix to directly visualize the uterine cavity for diagnostic or therapeutic purposes. 

Finally, physicians serve as the first point of evaluation for couples experiencing infertility; they are advised when a couple has not conceived after one year of regular, unprotected intercourse, and they coordinate further reproductive assessment and management.&lt;SEP&gt;Physician is the medical professional who may leave a tube in place after Paracentesis to allow slow fluid removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Physician is a medical professional who may guide the transducer during a pelvic ultrasound.&lt;SEP&gt;A physician is a medical doctor who may perform arterial blood collection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8bcf4112e39ea15ac243ebe48a81015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6407dc79c35579b5387abf2b05a97d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7a1c4e1372979af71be73cfdd576ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9b86e7fa3cdc49102c86215baa6da67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cf07655a8780ee831372742398affa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-405f3438c94303b670da4ac7ad2e23a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d89439564ae2dc33beae4237976b40b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed0aad3bf0cbd3eab10e7535f31d9a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b03362a1a14b83e88e498b918bc854</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420559</data>
</node>
<node id="Patient">
  <data key="d0">Patient</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patient is the individual who receives medical care, encompassing the full spectrum of physical, spiritual, emotional, and cognitive aspects addressed by both conventional and holistic medicine. In clinical practice the patient may present with a wide variety of health conditions, ranging from specific disorders such as acoustic neuroma (an inner‑ear tumor) and anaerobic infections that require targeted antimicrobial therapy, to chronic mental health issues like anxiety disorders or paranoid symptoms that necessitate psychiatric evaluation and psychotherapeutic intervention such as Gestalt therapy.  

When diagnostic or therapeutic procedures are needed, the patient may undergo preparations such as fasting after midnight, receive detailed briefings about the purpose, benefits, and risks of tests, and give informed consent. Examples of such procedures include angiography, pelvic ultrasound, and specialized examinations such as a penile exam for lumps or abnormalities. In surgical contexts the patient might be scheduled for operations like congenital heart defect repair, pneumonectomy, or organ transplantation, followed by postoperative monitoring of vital signs, administration of intravenous antibiotics, and comprehensive postoperative care aimed at recovery and long‑term health maintenance.  

Therapeutic regimens can also involve programs like PTHC (post‑traumatic health care), where the patient is instructed to fast, receives intravenous antibiotics when indicated, and is closely observed for complications. Across all settings, the patient remains the central focus of individualized assessment, treatment planning, and supportive care, with the overarching goal of restoring health, alleviating symptoms, and promoting overall well‑being.&lt;SEP&gt;A patient is an individual who undergoes Pyloroplasty and receives postoperative monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;A patient is an individual who undergoes a radical neck dissection and may require postoperative care such as hospital stay and drains.&lt;SEP&gt;Patient is the individual positioned for reflex testing and may be asked to perform muscle contractions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c5e751c6db20a49f7ca0a341eadc654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6407dc79c35579b5387abf2b05a97d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ee6af5422b0bedd83a764af83874c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75141ec103928f9f43bbc8f2d882b9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1acfa8b3bcf6abb174b1db6c3878690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56ef10afa5a5d842dfa90eafc05da760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b29429d857edf1192105634eda51b928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8ffed90e8805478f1786896b19a574a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c9e6467acd0c81d0621428aab938849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577fcfa5541668fe081689a4dcf7502f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b914f2eb8e464a9d70f7d72f05cc69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf6dff342e4acda4a389bc2338c84151&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f81367bc23721681b080e8e55f88ab71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f4ea3b1eb99b2409bd29d960ef8865e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b10aa104383eb3ba74165d13d525ae5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2056dc204f71f79fef28e7940fdf482f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786427080</data>
</node>
<node id="Name">
  <data key="d0">Name</data>
  <data key="d1">type</data>
  <data key="d2">Name is a personal identifier recorded as part of an individual’s personal data during a hospital admission. In the healthcare setting, this identifier functions as a key piece of information used to uniquely distinguish patients within medical records and to support the delivery of medical services. It is collected at the point of admission and stored alongside other personal and clinical data to ensure accurate patient management, billing, and communication among care providers. The identifier enables reliable linkage of diagnostic, treatment, and administrative information to the correct individual throughout the continuum of care.  

The remaining entries in the description list consist only of generic placeholders such as “description,” “Description,” or short truncated notes that do not provide additional substantive information about the entity. Consequently, the comprehensive understanding of Name rests on the detailed definition supplied in the first description.&lt;SEP&gt;Description". Should be okay.&lt;SEP&gt;Description". Looks correct.&lt;SEP&gt;description</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7294fc7c2531b2723bf6002b6e65eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427a659d0ef51d2588b292e6329fb824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afe775e3de6a2ede3813b294c2d7085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a09c28fcfc5857e1357740e308a5a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604d12edc178de2877cb886e122f1afb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566c344db40177f660ee8acadd6a0e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a3b3c33dc539d83724153cf8bd92691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d770964e720fab65211b3835a1fc2731&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd702733210b77bd85a84e3b0046cb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7e17cacaaf841bbb7b5d9df93877ea0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdce04fe6b7fc2f2383ff5401c7803f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a02576fa5e7cb9454806212014cc974e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad90a1c52c5adcfcef0c32801d2597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e49611e93e664f1f3b07223c8f1f46b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b80e7879bdadccc46c8e3487422dbd9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49690ebe88a03e6a7140692753a7c25a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1e4ccd0ac838eb947c64fb34bbe1307&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a94c4bf64c517d45cc23342217a0e34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a2507ab9e4fe1a49c0510793d8d0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afbff98c4c1d63870e1df4480f9167fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2887ebc17d5fa167b3627fd14696de82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786427056</data>
</node>
