<node id="Hormones">
  <data key="d0">Hormones</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hormones are chemical messengers whose interactions with skin proteins and bacteria influence the development of acne.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormones are substances produced by the adrenal cortex that affect water balance and metabolism in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormones are biochemical substances produced during pregnancy that may be related to nausea and vomiting.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormones are chemical messengers produced by endocrine glands that regulate various physiological functions throughout the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormones are biological chemicals that can worsen gingivitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormones are signaling molecules secreted by endocrine glands to regulate physiological processes.</data>
