<node id="Respiratory System">
  <data key="d0">Respiratory System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Respiratory System  

The Respiratory System is the body system responsible for breathing and gas exchange, delivering oxygen to the bloodstream and removing carbon dioxide from the body. It consists of the upper and lower airways—the nasal cavity, pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, and bronchioles—together with the lungs and the muscular apparatus that drives ventilation, chiefly the diaphragm and intercostal muscles. Oxygen inhaled through the airways binds to hemoglobin in circulating red blood cells, while carbon dioxide produced by cellular metabolism is transferred from the blood into the alveolar air and expelled on exhalation. By sustaining this oxygen‑delivery and carbon‑removal cycle, the system supports cellular metabolism throughout the organism.

Clinically, the Respiratory System can be affected by a wide array of disorders. Infectious diseases such as influenza and pneumonia commonly target the airways and lung parenchyma, and the system serves as the primary site where the pneumonia‑causing bacteria reside. Genetic conditions such as Alagille syndrome, structural anomalies, and environmental exposures like asbestos fibers (causing asbestosis) also involve the respiratory tract. High‑level alcohol intoxication may depress respiratory drive, leading to respiratory failure, while immunoglobulin‑deficiency syndromes increase susceptibility to respiratory infections. Additional, less typical influences that have been reported include hiatal hernia, hysteria‑related symptoms, an impacted tooth, cutaneous T‑cell lymphoma, and physiological phenomena such as hiccups, all of which can alter respiratory function.

Neuromuscular impairments are a notable source of respiratory compromise. Polio can paralyze the diaphragm and intercostal muscles, producing acute respiratory failure, and survivors may later develop post‑polio syndrome with further respiratory weakness. Premature birth is another risk factor, predisposing infants to chronic respiratory problems such as bronchopulmonary dysplasia.  

The Respiratory System is a frequent focus of diagnostic and therapeutic interventions. Laboratory assessments may include tests such as amylase and haptoglobin when respiratory involvement is suspected, and surgical procedures require careful airway management. Pulmonary function tests specifically evaluate respiratory performance, and the system is routinely listed among body systems in procedural documentation and medical references. Complementary and alternative approaches—including the Alexander Technique for posture and breathing mechanics, acupressure, hydrotherapy, and polarity therapy—are employed to support respiratory health. The system also features in educational contexts such as phlebotomy training and exercise modalities like Pilates, underscoring its central, integrative role in human physiology, pathology, and therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca4ee33fbe169b1bec7c819c96b35eb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afe775e3de6a2ede3813b294c2d7085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9098e6c377264351e34498ab20d1d2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ebc91deb19a2b42710150361b08958e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bcaad1542ea8e041fd9f427e13e25c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aaee80ad65e061c4dbd83e81542c322&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf9568ffc5d5bfc55e145a95f45cf030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc626b00afed53316810372730831c40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b6a561225b73fa4827b9e9a8a411e05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d89439564ae2dc33beae4237976b40b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31523ff9a2a651ce41cbc96e86cccd97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-011a30caa3696a5321ec2b965fba6473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c63f65bb800d3d7fae8a0864fc3cdf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56ef10afa5a5d842dfa90eafc05da760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f2eb90fc948c2cce9700f6264f9195a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a98908cc7f18fa4c5b0c4a45575393&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8123b7be7ff18b176f9e2f5778b3e2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a43117074cce1d59c31131832dfa007&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dcd996730cbdde5a41d3f86b16d8074&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcc52e74701dc594a5093895fbb8763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeb4dffb5ad505f4839faaa747910b3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b7e1ff6aefba50b9ab4cb48e8298cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47a3a83e48113d48f0a14a70afb7ebf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9b86e7fa3cdc49102c86215baa6da67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02740b694bb0616d4b4005a09fd946b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-012e85679bddc890f1489e743c060e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6ffae8f8f4f2414b3337df8e60bdabf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71b04609b9999bd4f4017776dc567f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9348993468d1735d7ee70858031d433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bca77605ecf717ab8187e9673827ff86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79234b86eefaf132e002bda9d70d7428&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f088a5c1c6bbd06f9b18f4580c46043&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
