<node id="Neurological System">
  <data key="d0">Neurological System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neurological System is the body system that comprises the central nervous system (the brain and spinal cord) and the peripheral nervous system (peripheral nerves and the muscles they innervate).  It serves as the primary regulator of sensory perception, motor coordination, autonomic activities, and overall nerve activity, integrating signals between the central nervous system and the rest of the organism to maintain physiological homeostasis.

Clinically, the Neurological System can be implicated in a wide spectrum of conditions.  It is a common site for abscess formation and is centrally involved in addiction, mediating the brain mechanisms underlying substance dependence.  Neurological dysfunction contributes to the symptomatology of Alagille syndrome, agoraphobia, ataxia‑telangiectasia, hereditary fructose intolerance, hypothyroidism, heat‑related disorders, and many personality and mood disorders.  Toxic exposures such as chronic alcohol use, as well as physical trauma—including amputation and prematurity‑related brain injury—can damage the brain, peripheral nerves, and associated muscles.  The system is a recognized cause of vomiting and can be adversely affected by several pharmacological classes, including antidepressants, selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors (SSRIs), antimigraine agents, and appetite‑suppressant drugs that act on central neurotransmitters.  Additional associations include hammertoe, reflex pathways that help maintain blood pressure, the pathophysiology of hiccups, insulin resistance, and hysteria symptoms.  The Neurological System also benefits from complementary approaches such as Animal‑Assisted Therapy and polarity therapy.

Specific neurological disorders and infectious agents highlight the system’s vulnerability.  Polio can damage the Neurological System, leading to lower‑limb paralysis and the later development of Post‑Polio Syndrome.  Progressive Supranuclear Palsy, rabies, and the neurodegeneration seen in prematurity‑related brain injury are also listed as affecting this system.  In reproductive health, the Neurological System is noted as relevant to prepregnancy counseling, underscoring the importance of neurological status before conception.

From a diagnostic and procedural perspective, the Neurological System appears in numerous laboratory and clinical evaluations.  It is considered during antidiuretic hormone (ADH) assays, aldolase tests that measure muscle enzyme activity, and allergy testing, reflecting its role in biochemical and immunological assessments.  Surgical references include craniotomy procedures and broader general‑surgery contexts.  The system is mentioned in relation to the Gleason Score entry, the Aston‑Patterning framework, and various psychological tests.  Reflexology and formal reflex tests specifically assess neurological function, illustrating its central place in both therapeutic and evaluative practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff53a187c372ebdee1b2526a7ad3f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca4ee33fbe169b1bec7c819c96b35eb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427a659d0ef51d2588b292e6329fb824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e261bddabf1598318602d5ab776f60c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-919116bb6efe3303887cfaa1a2474f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8c896b91f897e5bbbd177234ee62ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea87a42e2dfef284d8c503ac77656a7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe1b59b257b5d344c7de5181dbff9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96678691a6b9b46cb9e089fa58def217&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9098e6c377264351e34498ab20d1d2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e04fc4d9139221a4e00a150baf448e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6f6eb6351953e7ef79475828425af93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a3b3c33dc539d83724153cf8bd92691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aaee80ad65e061c4dbd83e81542c322&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31acc4fe9b37a7723a57b2cd84eb9d1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0562388bfd043886184b76d26796a668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36c53d0d3d0b154d1cafa4ae311eafc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189651eadb45a933adca499117c49ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cfffa1f33540095dd9f47cec4a53945&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df310a5eb710fa15878efbe7d25bc7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44b884468a26dc2957843352da600dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75141ec103928f9f43bbc8f2d882b9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a89a85dc3be8d37412b0c61ebf99cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-011a30caa3696a5321ec2b965fba6473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c63f65bb800d3d7fae8a0864fc3cdf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2408b24dbbf82011285a46aaece84afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f2eb90fc948c2cce9700f6264f9195a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-627b1597e2ff9fd7f303859f27a292f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b7ae47fed28c48dbd20bd5a3891afd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99238eefb790bd6f517ddd61b96753ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a43117074cce1d59c31131832dfa007&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-043b5eeeac66113551273095596cd117&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b20a7bdac3dcdeae955d7f5fcff8809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa850befaee3ce9863ec83a8dbb56b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9b86e7fa3cdc49102c86215baa6da67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02740b694bb0616d4b4005a09fd946b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1385133e299def4ed989633bdbd7168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71b04609b9999bd4f4017776dc567f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-097e88fc7e1ff542a919812e0d0d508a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f088a5c1c6bbd06f9b18f4580c46043</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
