<node id="Gastrointestinal System">
  <data key="d0">Gastrointestinal System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gastrointestinal System  

The Gastrointestinal System is a major human body system that encompasses the entire digestive tract, extending from the oral cavity through the esophagus, stomach, and small intestine (including the ileum) to the large intestine and anus. Its primary functions are the ingestion of food, mechanical and chemical digestion, and the absorption of nutrients, water, and small molecules such as alcohol across the mucosal lining, followed by the elimination of indigestible waste. Because of these essential roles, it is routinely listed among the fundamental anatomical and clinical systems of the body.  

Clinically, the Gastrointestinal System is implicated in a wide spectrum of conditions. It is a common site for abscess formation, contributes amylase used in laboratory assays of pancreatic and salivary function, and is involved in disorders ranging from inflammatory processes, ascites, and acute kidney failure to genetic diseases such as Alagille syndrome, hereditary fructose intolerance, and glycogen storage diseases. The system also participates in the pathophysiology of cutaneous T‑cell lymphoma, autoimmune hepatitis, hepatitis D, gestational diabetes, graft‑versus‑host disease, hiatal hernia, complications of high‑risk pregnancy, hypercholesterolemia, hypothyroidism, and historically described psychosomatic (“hysteria”) symptoms. It is considered in hospice‑care planning and in discussions of insulin resistance and other systemic metabolic disturbances.  

Infectious agents and neoplastic processes can affect the Gastrointestinal System. Influenza may produce gastrointestinal manifestations often termed “stomach flu,” poliovirus multiplies within the tract after infection, and conditions such as pneumonia, perinatal infections, pheochromocytoma, and endocrine pancreatic cancer have been reported to involve the gastrointestinal tract. The system is also listed among those affected by post‑polio syndrome, primary biliary cirrhosis, premature labor, and portal vein bypass procedures.  

Therapeutic management of gastrointestinal disorders includes both pharmacologic and non‑pharmacologic strategies. Common drug categories are anti‑hemorrhoid agents, anti‑emetics, and systemic corticosteroids. Non‑pharmacologic interventions range from the Alexander Technique and hydrotherapy to specific dietary regimens, such as clear‑liquid diets after hernia repair. Surgical procedures—including gastrostomy—and laboratory evaluations of growth‑hormone and haptoglobin levels are integral components of comprehensive care. The system can also be altered in form or function by protein‑energy malnutrition and is addressed in alternative modalities such as polarity therapy.  

Overall, the Gastrointestinal System is a central component of human physiology, essential for nutrition, metabolic regulation, and the manifestation or modulation of a broad array of infectious, genetic, endocrine, oncologic, and systemic disorders.&lt;SEP&gt;The gastrointestinal system is the bodily system responsible for digestion, encompassing the stomach, intestines, and related organs.&lt;SEP&gt;The gastrointestinal system is one of the body systems associated with Provenge.&lt;SEP&gt;The gastrointestinal system comprises the stomach, duodenum, and other parts of the digestive tract.&lt;SEP&gt;The gastrointestinal system is listed among body systems associated with rectal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The gastrointestinal system is a body system mentioned as being affected by radioactive implants.&lt;SEP&gt;The gastrointestinal system is a body system mentioned as involved with rectal polyps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-983b3f2e664e0a36b1b8ee3747b9cc69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7294fc7c2531b2723bf6002b6e65eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25a42943ad0f93e6631565dc2c851d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca4ee33fbe169b1bec7c819c96b35eb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-329ac66938be7de8f3fecbe3eafea694&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-696bd50fdda11571d3f3a3dd02534eb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe1b59b257b5d344c7de5181dbff9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a321ea72ebe4c42d67faa7f47af64c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ff1c28387bf5cdbd9396931e1ac3bd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e04fc4d9139221a4e00a150baf448e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0747cef262212b19792ffedcc3323ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2679367b0beba9113c18be86c1ebf3c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ebc91deb19a2b42710150361b08958e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d527eab17c7341eca433d361df1f72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bcaad1542ea8e041fd9f427e13e25c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aaee80ad65e061c4dbd83e81542c322&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cc9b041882b1ffceb3664e339701aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d95207e6b81b3dbdeace9390840bca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc626b00afed53316810372730831c40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf9568ffc5d5bfc55e145a95f45cf030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ccba52c964c301daf559927d7d7c5e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36c53d0d3d0b154d1cafa4ae311eafc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189651eadb45a933adca499117c49ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fced0eb999ac47a6953e79fd6a6ae9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdce04fe6b7fc2f2383ff5401c7803f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-170bf8fe0c421cc796fb1a155cc92877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-857d781bfe6e2b60c49450d61d8306db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c289af6c541d3d25ea977381740c2c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-011a30caa3696a5321ec2b965fba6473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97c12585544967d7c896d91a36a80447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f2eb90fc948c2cce9700f6264f9195a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8123b7be7ff18b176f9e2f5778b3e2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a43117074cce1d59c31131832dfa007&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2668ae388ce75891b60c313b7cab62b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb199a3e40198055fdd9a325ecd1aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c10b11558c17065dc27bd62ccb0fb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeb4dffb5ad505f4839faaa747910b3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcc52e74701dc594a5093895fbb8763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3978e5151245a8ce567b224992eabb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47a3a83e48113d48f0a14a70afb7ebf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07cc217c989e2af1a805d2ee5017b0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eff6cb4281c913c830bd641c706365c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6deb35c161bfdda7d3d14623d9a411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a94c4bf64c517d45cc23342217a0e34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e12a604aa907a1e42740edfcfafe2583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9b86e7fa3cdc49102c86215baa6da67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02740b694bb0616d4b4005a09fd946b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-012e85679bddc890f1489e743c060e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afbff98c4c1d63870e1df4480f9167fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd4e9159e066f72729a8b0e6c804cc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad7165a537192620d6a93befeffa64e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-380c6702cc605a3cfe1200c7e02a7fb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1385133e299def4ed989633bdbd7168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71b04609b9999bd4f4017776dc567f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9348993468d1735d7ee70858031d433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bca77605ecf717ab8187e9673827ff86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3519af09df48250c19cedc50f317f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f088a5c1c6bbd06f9b18f4580c46043&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b03362a1a14b83e88e498b918bc854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2056dc204f71f79fef28e7940fdf482f</data>
