  <data key="d2">Endoscopy is used to visually examine the interior of the esophagus.&lt;SEP&gt;Endoscopy is a medical procedure involving a thin, lighted instrument inserted into the interior of the body and is used to diagnose antibiotic-associated colitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Endoscopy is a key term associated with hernia repair, representing a minimally invasive diagnostic or therapeutic technique.&lt;SEP&gt;Endoscopy is a diagnostic medical procedure used to examine the upper gastrointestinal tract in patients with persistent indigestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Endoscopy is a direct visualization technique used in screening to view the lining of the colon and rectum.</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426767</data>
