<node id="Dizziness">
  <data key="d0">Dizziness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dizziness is a symptom that can arise in a variety of clinical contexts. It may occur as a sudden complication following invasive procedures that involve puncture, such as after a general puncture, an Aldolase test performed via puncture, or a hemoglobin test that requires blood sampling. In these situations, individuals often report a sensation of lightheadedness or vertiginous feeling shortly after the procedure.

Dizziness is also documented as a possible side effect of several pharmacologic agents. Patients taking the antihypertensive medication Accupril may experience dizziness, as can those receiving antinausea drugs such as prochlorperazine. Additionally, antiprotozoal medications have been associated with dizziness as a recognized adverse effect.

Beyond procedural and drug‑related causes, dizziness can manifest as a somatic symptom of anxiety. In this context, it is characterized by a subjective feeling of lightheadedness that reflects the physiological response to heightened anxiety.

Overall, dizziness encompasses a range of experiences—from procedural complications and medication side effects to anxiety‑related somatic sensations—each presenting as a notable, often transient, feeling of lightheadedness or loss of balance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8c8cde44ecd33ed261dcf8056e92cec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d527eab17c7341eca433d361df1f72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-380c6702cc605a3cfe1200c7e02a7fb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5922b682f2c38e37dd9bd7f8f614180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-919116bb6efe3303887cfaa1a2474f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80337a816ac74c4f4d818c5c4c8c74d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419756</data>
</node>
<node id="Bruising">
  <data key="d0">Bruising</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bruising is a symptom that may occur at the puncture site.&lt;SEP&gt;Bruising is a potential complication of the Aldolase Test occurring at the puncture site after blood collection.&lt;SEP&gt;A symptom that may occur at the puncture site after blood is drawn for the test.&lt;SEP&gt;Bruising is a skin discoloration caused by bleeding under the surface, possible after a puncture.&lt;SEP&gt;Bruising is listed as a possible risk associated with physical therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b2f2e3046d0f775744775822b8b1381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-380c6702cc605a3cfe1200c7e02a7fb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-919116bb6efe3303887cfaa1a2474f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8411522bdeb607aaa222e6502bca7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420958</data>
</node>
<node id="Discomfort">
  <data key="d0">Discomfort</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Discomfort is a symptom at the puncture site.&lt;SEP&gt;Discomfort is a sensation of pain or unease that may occur at the puncture site following blood collection for&lt;SEP&gt;Discomfort is a possible complication of the Aldolase Test, experienced at the puncture site and alleviated by warm packs.&lt;SEP&gt;A symptom that may occur at the puncture site after blood is drawn for the test.&lt;SEP&gt;Discomfort is a feeling of unease that may occur at the puncture site after a hemoglobin test.&lt;SEP&gt;Discomfort may occur following a prostate biopsy procedure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e10029ea7f3dfee7cdfc21bb655230a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b2f2e3046d0f775744775822b8b1381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-380c6702cc605a3cfe1200c7e02a7fb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abbfd6cbf4afd6662ba2707fbc17c147&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-919116bb6efe3303887cfaa1a2474f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786424846</data>
</node>
<node id="Bleeding">
  <data key="d0">Bleeding</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bleeding is a symptom that may occur at the puncture site.&lt;SEP&gt;Presence of bleeding in pancreatic tissue is used as a prognostic indicator in pancreatitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Complication involving continued bleeding after the procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;Bleeding is a symptom that treatment aims to prevent and is also listed as a potential complication of pleural biopsy.</data>
