6f9e2f5778b3e2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0db65915ac0fe12261f4142e959eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebfd4a7217e0e17b00a9c2caf49c2826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2668ae388ce75891b60c313b7cab62b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dcd996730cbdde5a41d3f86b16d8074&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c10b11558c17065dc27bd62ccb0fb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeb4dffb5ad505f4839faaa747910b3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b7e1ff6aefba50b9ab4cb48e8298cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed0aad3bf0cbd3eab10e7535f31d9a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a94c4bf64c517d45cc23342217a0e34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e12a604aa907a1e42740edfcfafe2583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9b86e7fa3cdc49102c86215baa6da67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b785ff55416d26c9c9d2574c29ca4711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02740b694bb0616d4b4005a09fd946b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd4e9159e066f72729a8b0e6c804cc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35c30232e67a5a9d2bf59484035c1a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d6c274f816e9066576ca6cf4bef367a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1385133e299def4ed989633bdbd7168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5922b682f2c38e37dd9bd7f8f614180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-910d4bcf6932bd29fd1d161e11852b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-097e88fc7e1ff542a919812e0d0d508a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79234b86eefaf132e002bda9d70d7428&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f088a5c1c6bbd06f9b18f4580c46043&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad30bf77e8797dcdced78f2e2465f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b03362a1a14b83e88e498b918bc854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42</data>
  <data key="d2">Cardiovascular System  

The cardiovascular system is the body system responsible for circulating blood throughout the organism. It consists of the heart and an extensive network of arteries, veins, and capillaries that deliver oxygen, nutrients, hormones, and other essential substances to tissues while removing carbon dioxide and metabolic waste, thereby maintaining physiological homeostasis and regulating blood pressure. Hormonal influences such as cortisol and antidiuretic hormone, as well as nutritional status—including adequate adult nutrient intake and proper hemoglobin function—directly affect vascular health and cardiac efficiency.

Clinically, the cardiovascular system is implicated in a wide spectrum of conditions. It is a core component of heart failure and can be compromised by congenital heart defects, prematurity‑related heart anomalies, and diseases such as Alagille syndrome, ataxia‑telangiectasia, and progressive supranuclear palsy. Systemic disorders that affect it include acute kidney failure, gestational diabetes, ascites, pheochromocytoma, hypothyroidism, hyperlipoproteinemia, hypercholesterolemia, and the inflammatory impact of infections such as *Haemophilus* species and pneumonia. Even seemingly unrelated issues—hiccups, hernia repair, alopecia, infertility, insulin resistance, peripheral vascular disease, and the systemic effects of an impacted tooth—can involve the cardiovascular system. It also appears in forensic and genetic contexts (e.g., parentage testing) and pharmacogenetic studies related to heart and blood‑vessel function.

Lifestyle factors and pharmacological agents exert significant influence on cardiovascular performance. Moderate alcohol consumption may lower blood pressure, whereas excessive intake can precipitate cardiovascular failure. Numerous drugs have documented adverse cardiovascular effects, including anticoagulants, anti‑hemorrhoid medications, antimigraine agents, aminoglycoside antibiotics, appetite‑suppressant drugs, anabolic steroids, and the physiological consequences of amputation. Adequate adult nutrition is emphasized as essential for preserving system health.

Beyond pathology, the cardiovascular system is a focus of various therapeutic, educational, and procedural domains. It is addressed in polarity therapy, Hatha Yoga postures, the Alexander Technique, and general surgery curricula. The system is relevant to animal‑assisted therapy, alopecia management, and is integral to phlebotomy procedures for blood collection and analysis. It is also listed as a system affected by polymyositis and dermatomyositis and is mentioned in surgical contexts such as portal vein bypass. Collectively, these structural, regulatory, and pathological dimensions illustrate the essential and pervasive role of the cardiovascular system across medical, pharmacological, lifestyle, and therapeutic contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;The cardiovascular system is a body system affected by the calcification of elastic fibers in Pseudoxanthoma Elasticum.&lt;SEP&gt;The cardiovascular system is one of the body systems listed for the procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;The cardiovascular system is one of the body systems listed in relation to pulmonary function tests.&lt;SEP&gt;The cardiovascular system, listed as a body system involved in rabies cases, includes the heart and blood vessels.&lt;SEP&gt;The cardiovascular system is listed among body systems associated with rectal cancer.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426767</data>
</node>
