<node id="Immunological System">
  <data key="d0">Immunological System</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7294fc7c2531b2723bf6002b6e65eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b83572ef3bc13b6de1b3591b9a778c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b29429d857edf1192105634eda51b928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b2f2e3046d0f775744775822b8b1381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8c896b91f897e5bbbd177234ee62ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30319cce70ff00cde3c2e324df5816f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1b905af9bb1602798ef23bcfc2818c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d76104bef49b3189628a31424cb580f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9338b75f511ec154e543f92f47f1080&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0747cef262212b19792ffedcc3323ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2679367b0beba9113c18be86c1ebf3c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ebc91deb19a2b42710150361b08958e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd702733210b77bd85a84e3b0046cb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189651eadb45a933adca499117c49ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31523ff9a2a651ce41cbc96e86cccd97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f2eb90fc948c2cce9700f6264f9195a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a98908cc7f18fa4c5b0c4a45575393&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3978e5151245a8ce567b224992eabb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b63fc7d102b55c2843666075d6ad7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07cc217c989e2af1a805d2ee5017b0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eff6cb4281c913c830bd641c706365c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11ea5690ed5971ad6fadd2d1b3e3450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afbff98c4c1d63870e1df4480f9167fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35c30232e67a5a9d2bf59484035c1a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebc93901c908c91f026b8f84613ebc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bca77605ecf717ab8187e9673827ff86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8049c6dc0f71e37cbd8d3611d0687a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3519af09df48250c19cedc50f317f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79234b86eefaf132e002bda9d70d7428&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b03362a1a14b83e88e498b918bc854</data>
  <data key="d2">Immunological System refers to the body’s immune system, a complex physiological network that detects and eliminates pathogens, damaged cells, and other threats to maintain health. It integrates cellular defenses such as white‑blood cells with humoral mechanisms including antibody production and inflammatory regulation, thereby protecting the organism from infection and disease and serving as a central component of many diagnostic and educational tests.

The system’s activity is modulated by several endogenous and exogenous factors. The glucocorticoid hormone cortisol helps regulate inflammation and immune‑cell function, while complementary‑medicine practices associate specific acupressure points with the Immunological System and employ pressure techniques to support immune health. Hydrotherapy is also cited as a possible modality that can benefit immune function. Pharmacologically, antibiotics influence immune‑related bacterial infections, and the system’s status can affect or be affected by protein‑energy malnutrition, immunosuppression, and various hormonal or nutritional states.

Clinically, the Immunological System is implicated in a wide range of disease conditions. It is weakened in Ataxia‑telangiectasia, can be altered by cutaneous T‑cell lymphoma and graft‑versus‑host disease, and participates in autoimmune attacks on the liver, primary biliary cirrhosis, and psoriatic arthritis. Autoimmune mechanisms involving the system contribute to alopecia, and immune disturbances are noted as potential causes of vomiting and complications in hemorrhoidal disease. The system also plays a role in the body’s response to pneumonia, perinatal infections, and foreign material exposure, and it may be impacted by an impacted tooth, infertility, Peyronie’s disease, and photosensitivity.

Beyond pathology, the Immunological System is recognized as a target for therapeutic interventions and supportive strategies. Animal‑assisted therapy is reported to have beneficial effects on immune function, reflecting the system’s broader role in overall well‑being and recovery. Overall, the Immunological System constitutes the body’s primary defense mechanism, interacting with numerous physiological, clinical, and lifestyle factors to maintain health and influence disease outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Im&lt;SEP&gt;The immunological system is a body system relevant to Provenge’s mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;The immunological system is listed among body systems related to rectal polyps.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786427055</data>
</node>
<node id="Acute Poststreptococcal Glomerulonephritis">
  <data key="d0">Acute Poststreptococcal Glomerulonephritis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute poststreptococcal glomerulonephritis (APSGN) is an inflammation of the kidney tubules that occurs after a streptococcal infection such as strep throat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373881</data>
</node>
<node id="Postinfectious Glomerulonephritis">
  <data key="d0">Postinfectious Glomerulonephritis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Postinfectious glomerulonephritis is another name for acute poststreptococcal glomerulonephritis, describing the same disease following infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373881</data>
</node>
<node id="Kidney Tubules">
  <data key="d0">Kidney Tubules</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Kidney tubules, also called glomeruli, are structures in the kidney that filter waste products from the blood and become inflamed in APSGN.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373881</data>
</node>
<node id="Streptococcal Infection">
  <data key="d0">Streptococcal Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Streptococcal infection is an infection caused by group A beta-hemolytic streptococci, affecting the skin or throat and preceding APSGN.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373881</data>
</node>
<node id="Strep Throat">
  <data key="d0">Strep Throat</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Strep throat is a streptococcal infection of the throat that can precede acute poststreptococcal glomerulonephritis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373881</data>
</node>
<node id="Group A Beta-Hemolytic Streptococci">
  <data key="d0">Group A Beta-Hemolytic Streptococci</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Group A beta-hemolytic streptococci are bacteria that cause streptococcal infections leading to APSGN.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373881</data>
</node>
<node id="Skin">
  <data key="d0">Skin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin is the body's outer covering and primary interface between the internal organism and the external environment. As an epidermal organ, it is continuously exposed to sunlight, environmental chemicals, and physical agents, making it vulnerable to ultraviolet radiation, various reactions, and the need for protective measures such as sunscreen or barrier garments.

Because of its exposure, the skin can serve as a portal for infectious agents. Streptococcal bacteria can colonise or infect the skin, contributing to the risk of acute post‑streptococcal glomerulonephritis (APSGN). Human papillomavirus also infects the skin, leading to warts and other lesions. In addition, the skin normally harbours anaerobic bacteria as part of its resident microbiota.

The skin is also a clinical site for several disease manifestations and therapeutic interventions. Red, itchy rashes characteristic of allergic purpura appear on the skin, and malignant T‑helper cells infiltrate the epidermis in cutaneous T‑cell lymphoma (CTCL). Moreover, the skin is a focal point for plastic, reconstructive, and cosmetic surgeries, where careful preparation of this outer tissue is essential for optimal functional and aesthetic outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Skin is the organ that contains sweat and oil glands and can develop rashes such as prickly heat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5b83572ef3bc13b6de1b3591b9a778c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1acfa8b3bcf6abb174b1db6c3878690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3da3e9ecf369a29de0664ed8a629a950&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5972068248f50904396788f92782210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6007bd886198fad2e92df82e7baf0b56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3c3c73e1fc719b81a2fc054715a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cef0181d6e65ea01360302ddd1f7b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786424550</data>
</node>
<node id="Throat">
  <data key="d0">Throat</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Throat is a body part that can be infected by streptococcal bacteria, leading to strep throat and subsequent APSGN.&lt;SEP&gt;The throat is examined by doctors for bleeding related to hemoptysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Part of the upper respiratory tract where Streptococcus pneumoniae is commonly found in healthy individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ebc91deb19a2b42710150361b08958e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786421957</data>
</node>
<node id="Children">
  <data key="d0">Children</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Children are a demographic group in which up to 95% fully recover from APSGN within weeks or months.&lt;SEP&gt;Children are a patient group who benefit from bone marrow transplantation for acute leukemias.&lt;SEP&gt;Children are a population group in which hypochondriasis is increasingly recognized.&lt;SEP&gt;Children are young human individuals who, especially in developing countries, suffer high mortality due to protein-energy malnutrition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-684465558da6f22c66a6b34b82cea78c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afbff98c4c1d63870e1df4480f9167fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07cc217c989e2af1a805d2ee5017b0b3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786424859</data>
</node>
<node id="Adults">
  <data key="d0">Adults</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adults are a demographic group in which up to 70% fully recover from APSGN, though some may develop chronic kidney problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Adults are a demographic group that Proctitis mainly affects.&lt;SEP&gt;Adults are a population group less likely to develop miliaria rubra compared to infants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dad561d3742857b36b06aba05376ddc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3da3e9ecf369a29de0664ed8a629a950</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786424551</data>
</node>
<node id="Kidney Failure">
  <data key="d0">Kidney Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Kidney failure is a severe complication that may result from APSGN in patients who do not fully recover.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney failure is a condition where the kidneys cannot filter waste, mentioned as a context for hemofiltration.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney Failure is severe loss of kidney function commonly resulting from progressive Alport syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney failure is a severe condition that can result from Hemolytic-Uremic Syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney failure is a possible consequence of fructose accumulation in the kidneys due to hereditary fructose intolerance.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney failure is a condition that can cause hypocalcemia and is mentioned as requiring specific treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney Failure is a severe outcome of Polycystic Kidney Disease resulting from progressive loss of healthy kidney tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-434d8d551fe8baa35b0eb7738c2dec25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab866fbd1bcab0eba4400418a2cf4f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d855036a34135250bf6b6942f08845d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36c53d0d3d0b154d1cafa4ae311eafc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bead2f9ad4273b49f336c30d5e85e2f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dfd51ae04f9e4cb50f69eb42e877763</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422503</data>
</node>
<node id="Chronic Kidney Problems">
  <data key="d0">Chronic Kidney Problems</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chronic kidney problems are progressive issues of kidney function that may occur after APSGN in patients with incomplete recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373882</data>
</node>
<node id="Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Treatment is a broad term that denotes any medical or therapeutic intervention intended to relieve symptoms, manage disease processes, prevent complications, or achieve cure. It encompasses a wide spectrum of actions—from pharmacologic agents and surgical procedures to behavioral programs and supportive care—chosen according to the nature and severity of the condition, as well as the patient’s overall health status.

Across diverse illnesses, treatment strategies are tailored to address the specific pathophysiology and clinical goals. For acute post‑streptococcal glomerulonephritis, care focuses on relieving edema and hypertension; asbestosis management aims to improve breathing, prevent respiratory infections, and control complications. Hemolytic anemia may be treated with splenectomy, corticosteroids, or transfusions depending on cause and severity, while hepatitis C therapy seeks a sustained virologic response through antiviral regimens. Hepatitis A, lacking a specific antiviral, is managed with hydration, nutrition, and avoidance of alcohol. Hypocalcemia is corrected with intravenous and oral calcium supplementation. Management of pancreatitis emphasizes fluid replacement, pain control, and fasting. For presbyopia, optical correction with glasses or contact lenses compensates for loss of near vision. Priapism is addressed through interventions such as aspiration, catheterization, and oxygen therapy.

Treatment also includes non‑pharmacologic and psychosocial components. Addiction treatment often requires long‑term, multimodal programs that combine medication, behavioral therapy, and social support. Personality disorders are now recognized as potentially responsive to targeted therapeutic approaches. Post‑polio syndrome symptom relief may involve anti‑inflammatory drugs, hot packs, and stretching exercises. Psoriatic arthritis treatment aims to control both cutaneous psoriasis lesions and joint inflammation, frequently using disease‑modifying antirheumatic drugs or biologics. Surgical correction is the primary treatment for ptosis, restoring normal eyelid position.

Overall, the common thread of treatment is the purposeful application of appropriate interventions—whether medical, surgical, behavioral, or supportive—to improve patient outcomes and quality of life.&lt;SEP&gt;Treatment of rat-bite fever involves antibiotic therapy with penicillins, erythromycin, or tetracycline&lt;SEP&gt;Treatment encompasses staging, biopsy, imaging, and therapeutic protocols applied after diagnosis of rectal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Treatment of rectal prolapse includes conservative measures for infants, dietary modifications, and addressing underlying causes to achieve resolution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0412c9964e570b59a9a74a4404773c0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2835448bb481a076c03436c11f787066&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df310a5eb710fa15878efbe7d25bc7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeeced344cdde493cb84ba3e9ab7759f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c10fb15c165fb1c6b20b0aa8847da7ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9787f8a8b14586557271753b09718b06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97bc31370eb8948b543aaf5f06eb9116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caa0df876843ee924756d881922e0a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf2a4a7521a933797a5c97cd08b21a3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd702733210b77bd85a84e3b0046cb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71b04609b9999bd4f4017776dc567f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ccba52c964c301daf559927d7d7c5e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab866fbd1bcab0eba4400418a2cf4f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d82066907ae788a5c895e3b1bededab3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b20a7bdac3dcdeae955d7f5fcff8809</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426920</data>
</node>
<node id="Prevention">
  <data key="d0">Prevention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prevention refers to the coordinated set of actions, interventions, and strategies designed to avert the onset, progression, or complications of diseases, disorders, and other harmful health conditions. In the medical domain, preventive efforts often begin with early detection and timely treatment; for example, prompt therapy for streptococcal infections can interrupt the cascade that leads to acute post‑streptococcal glomerulonephritis, and regular chest radiographs combined with personal protective equipment protect asbestos‑exposed workers from asbestosis. Rigorous blood‑screening protocols, vaccine development, and avoidance of hepatotoxic medications reduce the risk of blood‑borne infections such as hepatitis C and drug‑induced liver injury. Lifestyle and behavioral measures—abstinence from smoking, regular physical activity, balanced nutrition, and education programs targeting adolescent substance use—help lower the risk of neurological conditions, substance‑related disorders, and mental‑health problems. Genetic counseling serves as a preventive approach for hereditary conditions by explaining inheritance patterns and reproductive options, thereby aiming to reduce the occurrence of disorders such as albinism. In acute toxic exposures, techniques such as gastric lavage and prompt treatment of human‑bite injuries are employed to mitigate poisoning and infection.

Despite this broad repertoire, several conditions lack proven preventive measures. No established method exists to prevent Alzheimer’s disease, hypothyroidism, polydactyly, syndactyly, or to definitively reduce vomiting during pregnancy. Specific diseases also have no identified preventive strategies: post‑polio syndrome progression can only be managed by moderating exertion; psoriatic arthritis and psoriasis have no known actions that reliably prevent flare‑ups; ptosis cannot be prevented; and pyloric stenosis has no preventive method despite surgical interventions such as pyloroplasty. Prevention of rat‑bite fever relies on avoiding contact with infected animals and consuming only pasteurized milk and safe water, but no vaccine is available. For conditions with familial risk, such as certain gastrointestinal disorders, high‑fiber diets and early screening are recommended as risk‑reduction strategies.

These gaps underscore the ongoing need for research into early‑stage interventions, disease‑modifying therapies, and evidence‑based recommendations that can expand the scope of effective prevention across the entire spectrum of health conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Prevention is the method aimed at avoiding the occurrence of rashes by eliminating triggering factors such as allergens or improper hygiene.&lt;SEP&gt;Prevention strategies for rectal prolapse involve avoiding straining, maintaining a high‑fiber diet, and staying well hydrated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b12e63d79b206980d9b85d5beb720662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13d7186c36bc114fd063d81d9835a694&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2835448bb481a076c03436c11f787066&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd6df79e5db44ce548291f0e8d6d6cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd702733210b77bd85a84e3b0046cb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ccba52c964c301daf559927d7d7c5e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d82066907ae788a5c895e3b1bededab3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df310a5eb710fa15878efbe7d25bc7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27addf854956380fbaa2c0b20a96027b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3d1367f180f5cdbc9f3386cadd299a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b20a7bdac3dcdeae955d7f5fcff8809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adcf683ab3aafdf4309bc219710636d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1385133e299def4ed989633bdbd7168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caa0df876843ee924756d881922e0a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf2a4a7521a933797a5c97cd08b21a3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71b04609b9999bd4f4017776dc567f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56d4bbf8d05ae296dc53a12cb3d6bc91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2056dc204f71f79fef28e7940fdf482f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
