</node>
<node id="Infectious System">
  <data key="d0">Infectious System</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Infectious System is a medical classification that designates any bodily organ system that can be involved in infection processes. It functions as a catch‑all category used by clinicians to group together physiological systems susceptible to pathogenic organisms, thereby informing decisions such as antibiotic selection, diagnostic testing, risk assessment, and interpretation of laboratory results.

The Infectious System appears in a variety of condition‑specific listings. It is identified among the systems associated with acute post‑streptococcal glomerulonephritis (APSGN) and with ascites, indicating that infections can contribute to or complicate these states. It is also cited as a system that Haemophilus infections may involve, and as one of the systems relevant to high‑risk pregnancy management, reflecting the importance of monitoring infectious involvement in maternal‑fetal health. Additionally, the Infectious System is included in the set of systems considered during immune‑complex testing and is listed among those linked to infertility, underscoring the broad impact that infectious agents can have across diverse clinical scenarios.

Beyond these core medical contexts, the Infectious System is referenced in several ancillary domains. It is mentioned in relation to personality disorders, suggesting that infectious involvement may be considered when evaluating certain psychiatric presentations. It is listed as a body system affected by perinatal infections, highlighting its relevance to neonatal and maternal health. The category also appears in discussions of photosensitivity, Pilates, and cosmetic‑surgery infection risk, indicating that infection‑related considerations extend into dermatologic, fitness, and aesthetic procedures. Finally, the Infectious System is one of the body systems noted in the entry for pleural biopsy, emphasizing its role in procedural planning and interpretation of biopsy findings.

Overall, the Infectious System serves as a comprehensive reference point for clinicians across a wide spectrum of medical and related fields, enabling systematic assessment of how infections may influence organ function, disease etiology, treatment strategies, and outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;The infectious system is a body system listed as relevant to the prostate ultrasound.&lt;SEP&gt;The infectious system refers to bodily processes involved in response to infectious agents (as classified in the text).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2679367b0beba9113c18be86c1ebf3c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983b3f2e664e0a36b1b8ee3747b9cc69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-870bb1b70305260567e1654eccb86793&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b83572ef3bc13b6de1b3591b9a778c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5972068248f50904396788f92782210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086f817567ac7efd026aad0f965d640e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6ffae8f8f4f2414b3337df8e60bdabf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebc93901c908c91f026b8f84613ebc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5922b682f2c38e37dd9bd7f8f614180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1b905af9bb1602798ef23bcfc2818c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8049c6dc0f71e37cbd8d3611d0687a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b20a7bdac3dcdeae955d7f5fcff8809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d76104bef49b3189628a31424cb580f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0747cef262212b19792ffedcc3323ca</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786425570</data>
</node>
<node id="Hematological System">
  <data key="d0">Hematological System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hematological System  

The hematological system is the body system responsible for the production, maintenance, and regulation of blood and its constituent components—including red blood cells, white blood cells, platelets, plasma, hemoglobin, and the clotting factors required for coagulation. By transporting oxygen, nutrients, and metabolic waste, providing immune defense, and ensuring hemostasis, it underpins essential physiological processes such as metabolic health, nutrient delivery, and the body’s capacity to respond to infection, injury, and circulatory challenges. It is therefore central to oxygen transport, nutrient distribution, immune activity, and clot formation.  

Clinically, the hematological system is implicated in a wide spectrum of conditions and medical contexts. It features in acute post‑streptococcal glomerulonephritis, autoimmune hepatitis, high‑risk pregnancy, congenital defects, heart failure, gestational diabetes, orthopedic problems such as hammertoe, and metabolic disturbances like hyperlipoproteinemia and hypercholesterolemia. Specific disorders in which the system may be disturbed include Polycystic Ovary Syndrome, Progressive Supranuclear Palsy, and various phobias. It also appears in procedural and diagnostic settings such as portal vein bypass, prostate ultrasound, hernia repair, adult nutrition examinations, prepregnancy counseling, and genetic counseling. The system is routinely evaluated through laboratory tests (e.g., aldolase, amino‑acid disorder screening, haptoglobin, growth‑hormone assays) and is relevant to forensic applications like parentage testing and to routine practices such as phlebotomy.  

Pharmacologically, certain agents—such as antimigraine drugs—can produce hematologic side effects, and therapeutic monitoring often incorporates hematologic parameters to gauge safety and efficacy. Lifestyle interventions, notably practices such as Hatha Yoga, have been reported to favorably affect circulation and overall blood health, indicating that the hematological system responds to both preventive health measures and disease‑directed treatments.  

In biomedical ontologies the hematological system is classified as a natural body system, linked to blood‑pressure regulation and to the broader network of systems affected by metabolic and cardiovascular disturbances. Its pervasive role across physiology, pathology, diagnostics, therapeutics, and wellness underscores its importance as a core focus of medical evaluation, risk assessment, drug safety monitoring, and health‑promotion strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;The hematological system is a body system listed among those involved in Pseudoxanthoma Elasticum.&lt;SEP&gt;The hematological system is one of the body systems listed in relation to pulmonary function tests.&lt;SEP&gt;The hematological system is one of the body systems mentioned in relation to reflexology.&lt;SEP&gt;The hematological system is listed among body systems related to rectal polyps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-983b3f2e664e0a36b1b8ee3747b9cc69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7294fc7c2531b2723bf6002b6e65eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6ec3b15611dc7dd72a22a499011fa4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b2f2e3046d0f775744775822b8b1381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e261bddabf1598318602d5ab776f60c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efefc9a9914255b2db7998e6ff75be31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-919116bb6efe3303887cfaa1a2474f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bcf4112e39ea15ac243ebe48a81015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a3b3c33dc539d83724153cf8bd92691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cac3b15cf6eb4edf007b3be55fb814e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf9568ffc5d5bfc55e145a95f45cf030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0562388bfd043886184b76d26796a668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d89439564ae2dc33beae4237976b40b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdce04fe6b7fc2f2383ff5401c7803f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cfffa1f33540095dd9f47cec4a53945&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bace5728e2cd20cde6babfc53bd224f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c289af6c541d3d25ea977381740c2c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ac7fad90c3ef5bbb1366ea8a473928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-142d840737a92f2ba527c40fc2edcbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56ef10afa5a5d842dfa90eafc05da760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2408b24dbbf82011285a46aaece84afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af3b4b939a2aeb8a2dffe85570c09b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7913b0884240a87bdd0d8c498ec19f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebfd4a7217e0e17b00a9c2caf49c2826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2668ae388ce75891b60c313b7cab62b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dcd996730cbdde5a41d3f86b16d8074&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708af40669770fee42a9a9b052181fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb199a3e40198055fdd9a325ecd1aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c10b11558c17065dc27bd62ccb0fb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcc52e74701dc594a5093895fbb8763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3978e5151245a8ce567b224992eabb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-870bb1b70305260567e1654eccb86793&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e12a604aa907a1e42740edfcfafe2583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b785ff55416d26c9c9d2574c29ca4711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd4e9159e066f72729a8b0e6c804cc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-910d4bcf6932bd29fd1d161e11852b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42</data>
