<node id="Kidney">
  <data key="d0">Kidney</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The kidney is the organ containing tubules that filter waste and become inflamed in APSGN.&lt;SEP&gt;organ that filters urine; becomes swollen in hydronephrosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney is a vital organ that was attempted to be transplanted from a cadaver to a living patient in 1933.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney is a human organ that can become enlarged and damaged by cysts in Polycystic Kidney Disease.&lt;SEP&gt;The kidney is an organ affected by inflammation in pyelonephritis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b29429d857edf1192105634eda51b928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2600a22cecd1107559c673a4542b5d0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a51c332fdfaf8c96be6ab58c809b221&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d855036a34135250bf6b6942f08845d7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426588</data>
</node>
<node id="Sore Throat">
  <data key="d0">Sore Throat</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sore throat is a symptom of streptococcal infection that increases the risk of developing APSGN.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373883</data>
</node>
<node id="Antigens">
  <data key="d0">Antigens</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antigens are protein fragments from dead streptococci that bind to antibodies and contribute to kidney inflammation in APSGN.&lt;SEP&gt;Antigens are foreign proteins that trigger antibody binding in the immune response associated with Allergic Purpura.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e46cef0181d6e65ea01360302ddd1f7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377289</data>
</node>
<node id="Antibodies">
  <data key="d0">Antibodies</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibodies are immune proteins that bind to streptococcal antigens, forming complexes that become trapped in kidney tubules during APSGN.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibodies are immune proteins that bind to foreign antigens and form complexes in Allergic Purpura.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibodies are proteins produced by the immune system in response to antigens.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibodies are proteins that neutralize invading pathogens, synonymous with immunoglobulins.&lt;SEP&gt;Proteins produced by the immune system that can neutralize pathogens, listed as a key term related to pneumonia vaccination.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibodies are proteins produced by the immune system that can bind to specific antigens, including the body’s own tissues in autoimmunity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ebc91deb19a2b42710150361b08958e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551add173e0a688b46340efd695e578b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9348993468d1735d7ee70858031d433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8049c6dc0f71e37cbd8d3611d0687a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cef0181d6e65ea01360302ddd1f7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01a42939570e7d067a66881fea563910</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422229</data>
</node>
