<node id="Withdrawal">
  <data key="d0">Withdrawal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Withdrawal refers to unpleasant or life‑threatening symptoms that occur when abstaining from an addiction.&lt;SEP&gt;Withdrawal refers to the set of symptoms that occur when a person with alcoholism stops drinking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b5b4ede4683a3be477e4527fbbb8cad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df310a5eb710fa15878efbe7d25bc7d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377852</data>
</node>
<node id="Addictive Personality">
  <data key="d0">Addictive Personality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Addictive personality describes a set of traits that predispose individuals to develop addictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Addictive personality is a hypothesized trait suggesting individuals prone to one addiction may develop other addictions, including Internet addiction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4542d461496cd18b5417df49b1f50690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df310a5eb710fa15878efbe7d25bc7d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412468</data>
</node>
<node id="Mood Modification">
  <data key="d0">Mood Modification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mood modification is the initial effect of many addictions, providing a feeling of better mood or euphoria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2df310a5eb710fa15878efbe7d25bc7d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
