<node id="Lymphatic System">
  <data key="d0">Lymphatic System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The lymphatic system is a network of vessels and nodes that filters waste from organs and is affected by acute lymphangitis.&lt;SEP&gt;The lymphatic system is part of the immune system and the blood‑producing system, comprising lymph vessels, nodes, spleen, bone marrow, and thymus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d88b3e0c879cd2c524008f697f6859f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bead2f9ad4273b49f336c30d5e85e2f1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786408732</data>
</node>
<node id="Lymph Nodes">
  <data key="d0">Lymph Nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lymph nodes are small filtering organs within the lymphatic system where immune responses to infections such as acute lymphangitis are generated.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymph nodes are small, bean‑shaped structures of the lymphatic system that can swell in Hodgkin’s lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymph nodes are anatomical structures in the head and neck that are often removed during radical neck dissection because they may be malignant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bead2f9ad4273b49f336c30d5e85e2f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88b3e0c879cd2c524008f697f6859f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8ffed90e8805478f1786896b19a574a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426813</data>
</node>
<node id="Radical Mastectomy">
  <data key="d0">Radical Mastectomy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Radical mastectomy is a surgical removal of a breast and nearby lymph nodes that increases the risk of developing acute lymphangitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bead2f9ad4273b49f336c30d5e85e2f1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
