<node id="Good Hygiene">
  <data key="d0">Good Hygiene</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Good hygiene is a preventive measure that may help avoid acute lymphangitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Good hygiene refers to practices such as thorough hand washing before and after meals, toilet use, diaper changes, and handling animals to prevent infectious diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Good Hygiene refers to practices such as avoiding sharing drinks and close contact that help prevent infection with Epstein-Barr virus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf8d23aad485a31e434afa128d656202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cad90a1c52c5adcfcef0c32801d2597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bead2f9ad4273b49f336c30d5e85e2f1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412016</data>
</node>
<node id="Alternative Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Alternative Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alternative Therapy is an overarching category or entry‑type classification that groups together therapeutic practices and medical interventions which fall outside the scope of conventional Western medicine. It serves as a label for non‑conventional, non‑traditional, or complementary approaches that are not part of mainstream clinical protocols.

The category encompasses a wide variety of modalities, including body‑based techniques such as acupuncture and hyperbaric oxygen therapy; mind‑body and psychological methods like Gestalt therapy and polarity therapy; biologically oriented alternatives such as homeopathic medicine; and supportive or experiential interventions such as infant massage, pet therapy, and other complementary practices. In some classification schemes the term is also used to denote the entry type for specific health‑related therapies (e.g., HRT) that are considered alternative to standard treatment models.&lt;SEP&gt;Alternative Therapy is the entry type classification assigned to psychotherapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b6a8e48c9d8fbad2aa9b283c25def07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80bdc5e62cc3de9c461969117469e796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca4ee33fbe169b1bec7c819c96b35eb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1089fcdf26e7799dcc1972363c2c7c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8a323d4236a65c6a130c075aa9de815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4bfe90135432788559f3dd95da898ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b914f2eb8e464a9d70f7d72f05cc69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8c896b91f897e5bbbd177234ee62ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e03f4e63fc8716fd3ee8d9a8c4f4b983</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786425944</data>
</node>
<node id="Z-codes">
  <data key="d0">Z-codes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Z‑codes are a distinct category of codes within the International Classification of Diseases (ICD) system that is employed to record both specific health‑related services and broader determinants of health.  In the ICD framework, Z‑codes serve the dual purpose of classifying procedures, laboratory and psychological examinations, as well as factors influencing health status and contacts with health services.  This enables consistent documentation, reimbursement processing, epidemiological tracking, and quality‑of‑care initiatives across clinical and administrative settings.

The scope of Z‑codes encompasses a wide variety of diagnostic and therapeutic interventions.  Examples include alternative procedures such as acupuncture; surgical and endoscopic techniques such as arthroscopy, gastrostomy, hydrocelectomy, and hypophysectomy; and specialized therapies like hyperbaric oxygen therapy.  Laboratory and biochemical tests—such as the aldolase test, amylase test, immune‑complex test, and growth‑hormone assays—are also assigned Z‑codes, as are psychological assessments and genetic services such as parentage testing.  Specific clinical examinations, for instance a prostate ultrasound, fall under this category, as do health‑promoting activities like infant massage.

Beyond individual services, Z‑codes capture contextual health information, recording social, environmental, and preventive factors that affect a patient’s health status.  By providing a mechanism to document these broader determinants and the patient’s interactions with health‑care providers, Z‑codes function as a versatile component of the ICD taxonomy, supporting comprehensive health‑information management and facilitating analysis of both clinical care and the wider determinants of health outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5223cef84c6fa99549cfa09e03c4ddcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca4ee33fbe169b1bec7c819c96b35eb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4bfe90135432788559f3dd95da898ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-919116bb6efe3303887cfaa1a2474f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea87a42e2dfef284d8c503ac77656a7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a321ea72ebe4c42d67faa7f47af64c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96678691a6b9b46cb9e089fa58def217&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec2b081d8d4ebb2f1d50934b4b4d93dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6f6eb6351953e7ef79475828425af93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e03f4e63fc8716fd3ee8d9a8c4f4b983&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d89439564ae2dc33beae4237976b40b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-857d781bfe6e2b60c49450d61d8306db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b6a8e48c9d8fbad2aa9b283c25def07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb199a3e40198055fdd9a325ecd1aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-870bb1b70305260567e1654eccb86793&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edfaa9dba99a768f9ffcf5c77b2d0525&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b785ff55416d26c9c9d2574c29ca4711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9b86e7fa3cdc49102c86215baa6da67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-012e85679bddc890f1489e743c060e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a70a3ab31498f37b121780c8c0792259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8049c6dc0f71e37cbd8d3611d0687a1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786425231</data>
</node>
<node id="Traditional Chinese Medicine">
  <data key="d0">Traditional Chinese Medicine</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Traditional Chinese Medicine is a holistic medical system originating in China that includes practices such as acupuncture, shiatsu, and acupressure massage.&lt;SEP&gt;Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) is a medical system that has used Ginkgo biloba for about 5,000 years.&lt;SEP&gt;Traditional Chinese Medicine is a holistic medical system from China, studied by Randolph Stone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b6a8e48c9d8fbad2aa9b283c25def07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8be7372d8b44a9ef7b6fc0c394e699c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca4ee33fbe169b1bec7c819c96b35eb6</data>
