<node id="Hospital">
  <data key="d0">Hospital</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5a65a1c3cf6b8503607afdabf8b0202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6407dc79c35579b5387abf2b05a97d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e12a604aa907a1e42740edfcfafe2583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a321ea72ebe4c42d67faa7f47af64c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5972068248f50904396788f92782210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b29429d857edf1192105634eda51b928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d770964e720fab65211b3835a1fc2731&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99d14117824aa2b5637825772676446&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-097e88fc7e1ff542a919812e0d0d508a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d89439564ae2dc33beae4237976b40b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8ffed90e8805478f1786896b19a574a</data>
  <data key="d2">Hospital is a medical institution and facility that serves as the primary setting for a wide range of patient care activities, beginning with the admission process which takes place within the hospital organization itself.  

As a comprehensive health‑care center, a hospital provides surgical services that include amputations, gastrostomy procedures, and hernia repairs. It also houses specialized units such as an Intensive Care Unit (ICU) that delivers critical care for patients undergoing complex treatments.  

In addition to acute surgical and emergency care, hospitals support organ transplantation programs. They offer overall care for heart transplantation patients and provide aftercare services for individuals recovering from any type of organ transplant, ensuring continuous monitoring and support throughout the post‑operative period.  

Overall, a hospital functions as an integrated medical facility that combines admission, surgical, intensive, and post‑transplant care under one organizational umbrella.&lt;SEP&gt;Hospital is a healthcare institution where pelvic ultrasound examinations may be performed.&lt;SEP&gt;A hospital is a medical facility where phlebotomy procedures can be performed.&lt;SEP&gt;Hospitals are healthcare institutions where complex cosmetic surgeries may be performed.&lt;SEP&gt;The hospital is the medical facility where a patient stays for up to one week following a radical neck dissection.</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426813</data>
</node>
