<node id="Pituitary Gland">
  <data key="d0">Pituitary Gland</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pituitary Gland is an endocrine organ that produces the hormone ACTH, which regulates adrenal activity.&lt;SEP&gt;The pituitary gland is a small gland that regulates hormonal secretion, including stimulation of the thyroid gland.&lt;SEP&gt;The pituitary gland is a pea-sized endocrine organ located at the base of the brain that secretes hormones regulating various body functions.&lt;SEP&gt;The pituitary gland is a master endocrine organ located in the middle of the head, regulating various hormonal functions.&lt;SEP&gt;The pituitary gland, located deep in the brain, is considered the master gland that regulates many other endocrine glands.&lt;SEP&gt;The pituitary gland releases gonadotropins in response to Gn‑RH stimulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44b884468a26dc2957843352da600dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee26fc83e6a72a8d68824995539e61e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5223cef84c6fa99549cfa09e03c4ddcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6409c7c91c51d8723b72f6697dc5c8cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1385133e299def4ed989633bdbd7168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01a42939570e7d067a66881fea563910</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786423414</data>
</node>
<node id="ACTH">
  <data key="d0">ACTH</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ACTH (adrenocorticotropic hormone) is a hormone produced by the pituitary gland that stimulates the adrenal cortex.&lt;SEP&gt;ACTH (adrenocorticotropic hormone) is listed among key terms related to the condition.&lt;SEP&gt;ACTH (adrenocorticotropic hormone) is listed among key terms related to the condition.</data>
