<node id="Diagnostic Test">
  <data key="d0">Diagnostic Test</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnostic Test is a broad, entry‑type classification for medically sanctioned examinations and procedures whose primary purpose is to detect, confirm, monitor, or assess the presence, nature, severity, or progression of a health condition. As a category, it encompasses any test that measures physiological, biochemical, hormonal, genetic, or imaging parameters in order to support clinical decision‑making, disease screening, or organ‑function evaluation.

The scope of Diagnostic Test includes a wide variety of specialized assessments. Hormonal and biochemical assays such as general hormone panels, the antidiuretic hormone (ADH) test, alanine aminotransferase (ALT) test, alkaline phosphatase test, aldosterone assay, and aldolase test are typical examples that identify liver, adrenal, or muscular disorders. Metabolic monitoring can be performed with the Glycosylated Hemoglobin (HbA1c) test or a standard hemoglobin test, while endocrine and reproductive screening is represented by the hCG pregnancy test. Imaging studies like adrenal gland scans and disease‑specific markers such as the prostate‑specific antigen (PSA) test also fall under this umbrella. Genetic and forensic applications are covered by parentage testing, and immune‑system assessments include the Immune Complex test. Prenatal and obstetric screening is captured by antenatal testing, and the category even extends to psychological assessments, which are classified as diagnostic tests for mental‑health evaluation.

In summary, Diagnostic Test serves as the overarching classification that unifies diverse medical examinations—ranging from laboratory assays and imaging studies to genetic, immunologic, and psychological evaluations—each designed to diagnose, monitor, or guide treatment of disease conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic Test is a category of medical examinations that assess bodily functions, under which reflex tests fall.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6f6eb6351953e7ef79475828425af93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e10029ea7f3dfee7cdfc21bb655230a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44b884468a26dc2957843352da600dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75141ec103928f9f43bbc8f2d882b9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0f9060ec0c9f4ede431f09a4763b28e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b785ff55416d26c9c9d2574c29ca4711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a048e601dd7e1d6483996e8fa02d2546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7913b0884240a87bdd0d8c498ec19f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-919116bb6efe3303887cfaa1a2474f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9884cc6b8d6b0ac0b0a8e59dba54ef9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea87a42e2dfef284d8c503ac77656a7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8049c6dc0f71e37cbd8d3611d0687a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c289af6c541d3d25ea977381740c2c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96678691a6b9b46cb9e089fa58def217&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c3f104d4a00ee29290d4bff7ae1489&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42</data>
