  <data key="d3">chunk-62dcc63c88cff699f68208f0455773b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e1b300199e25407d954c8745371d3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3323f3fda2ab71ab254c2a21d7d535a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d2">Hospitalization is recommended for EKC to prevent blindness in patients with adenovirus infections.&lt;SEP&gt;Hospitalization is the practice of admitting patients with amebic liver abscess to a medical facility for care.&lt;SEP&gt;Hospitalization refers to inpatient medical care that may be required for severe primary genital herpes infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Hospitalization is often required when treating patients with Amphotericin B due to its toxic side effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Hospitalization is a medical treatment approach often required for severe cases of hyperemesis gravidarum.</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
