  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376277</data>
</node>
<node id="Alveolo-Capillary Junction">
  <data key="d0">Alveolo-Capillary Junction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The alveolo-capillary junction is the contact point where the smallest blood vessels (capillaries) meet the alveoli, allowing oxygen to pass from inhaled air to the blood; damage to this site permits fluid leakage into the alveoli in ARDS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-436bf04244acb1c38f4b291e7d30ec94</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376277</data>
</node>
<node id="Advance Directives">
  <data key="d0">Advance Directives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Advance Directives are written documents that allow individuals to specify how medical decisions should be made when they are unable to decide themselves.&lt;SEP&gt;A collection of legal documents, including health care proxy and living will, that specify a person's medical wishes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-366e84609f4da3f8c10c22b1688f408e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403105</data>
</node>
<node id="Instruction Directives">
  <data key="d0">Instruction Directives</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Instruction Directives are a category of advance directive that specify particular treatments or actions in writing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376361</data>
</node>
<node id="Agent-Driven Directives">
  <data key="d0">Agent-Driven Directives</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agent-Driven Directives are a category of advance directive that authorize a designated individual to make medical decisions on behalf of the patient.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376361</data>
</node>
<node id="Proxy">
  <data key="d0">Proxy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Proxy is an individual who makes medical decisions on behalf of another person under an agent-driven directive.&lt;SEP&gt;A role referred to in some states for the person authorized to make medical decisions on another's behalf.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-366e84609f4da3f8c10c22b1688f408e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403105</data>
</node>
<node id="Do Not Resuscitate Order">
  <data key="d0">Do Not Resuscitate Order</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Do Not Resuscitate Order is a directive that specifies that cardiopulmonary resuscitation should not be performed if the individual's heart stops.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376361</data>
</node>
<node id="Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation">
  <data key="d0">Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR) is a medical emergency procedure used to restore breathing and circulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR) is an emergency procedure that manually preserves brain function by maintaining circulation and breathing in a person whose heart has stopped.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-895c5e07d9ff1dcdf835a5d197d6cf8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404110</data>
</node>
<node id="Lung Injury">
  <data key="d0">Lung Injury</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lung Injury refers to damage to lung tissue that can impair oxygen exchange and lead to complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376361</data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen is a vital gas required for cellular respiration and the proper functioning of organs. It participates in numerous cellular reactions, serving as a key reactant in metabolic pathways while also contributing to the formation of free radicals that can affect cellular signaling and oxidative stress.

In the human body, oxygen is bound by hemoglobin in red blood cells and transported through the circulatory system to tissues throughout the body, where it is released to support aerobic metabolism. This transport mechanism ensures that oxygen reaches cells to sustain energy production and maintain physiological homeostasis.

Clinically, oxygen is administered as a therapeutic gas to support breathing in a variety of medical situations. It is provided during anaphylactic episodes to aid respiration, given after craniotomy to facilitate patient recovery, and supplied to patients for four to twenty‑four hours following heart transplantation to ensure adequate oxygenation during the critical postoperative period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd48b3d64142d95730163769979b3bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e59ab8338831484ea61486c70a6ad038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcc52e74701dc594a5093895fbb8763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99d14117824aa2b5637825772676446&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404828</data>
</node>
<node id="Kidneys">
  <data key="d0">Kidneys</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Kidneys are vital paired organs that filter blood, regulate fluid balance, and sit beneath the adrenal glands. By removing waste products and excess substances from the bloodstream, they maintain homeostasis and produce urine. Antidiuretic hormone (ADH) signals the kidneys to conserve water, concentrating urine and reabsorbing water as needed.

Kidneys also play a role in the excretion of specific enzymes; excess amylase in the blood can be transferred into urine, influencing urine amylase concentrations. They are capable of accumulating uric acid crystals, which can precipitate gout‑related complications. In addition, the kidneys are involved in the defective amino acid transport observed in Hartnup disease, linking renal function to certain metabolic disorders.

Various diseases can affect the kidneys. Alagille syndrome may involve renal abnormalities, and allergic purpura can influence kidney prognosis. Moreover, insufficient oxygen (hypoxia) makes the kidneys vulnerable to injury, underscoring the importance of adequate perfusion for their proper</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6f6eb6351953e7ef79475828425af93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-012e85679bddc890f1489e743c060e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7913b0884240a87bdd0d8c498ec19f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cef0181d6e65ea01360302ddd1f7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02740b694bb0616d4b4005a09fd946b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-737df0aafe22dcc66ba8fe8d61ceefec</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403298</data>
</node>
<node id="Bacterial Pneumonia">
  <data key="d0">Bacterial Pneumonia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bacterial Pneumonia is an infection of the lungs caused by bacteria, posing a risk for patients with lung injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376362</data>
</node>
<node id="Conservator">
  <data key="d0">Conservator</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Conservator is an individual appointed as a legal guardian to manage the personal and financial affairs of another person.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376362</data>
</node>
<node id="Legal Guardian">
  <data key="d0">Legal Guardian</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Legal Guardian is a person authorized by law to make decisions on behalf of another individual who is unable to do so.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc48729584254d74fcf981c77bc52930</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376362</data>
</node>
<node id="Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD)">
  <data key="d0">Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adrenoleukodystrophy is a rare genetic disease characterized by a loss of myelin surrounding nerve cells in the brain and progressive adrenal gland dysfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376379</data>
</node>
<node id="Myelin">
  <data key="d0">Myelin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Myelin is a protective layer that surrounds nerve cells and some axons, primarily composed of lipids and lipoproteins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376379</data>
</node>
<node id="Very Long Chain Fatty Acids (VLCFA)">
  <data key="d0">Very Long Chain Fatty Acids (VLCFA)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Very long chain fatty acids are fatty acid molecules that accumulate in various tissues due to a genetic defect in Adrenoleukodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376379</data>
</node>
<node id="Amniocentesis">
  <data key="d0">Amniocentesis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Amniocentesis is a procedure that collects amniotic fluid through a needle inserted through the abdomen to obtain fetal cells for genetic analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Amniocentesis is a prenatal testing method for Alagille Syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;Amniocentesis is a prenatal test that samples amniotic fluid to analyze fetal chromosomes for detecting Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02740b694bb0616d4b4005a09fd946b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419191</data>
</node>
<node id="Chorionic Villi Sampling">
  <data key="d0">Chorionic Villi Sampling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chorionic villi sampling is a technique used to collect placental tissue for genetic testing, mentioned as a sample source for the biochemical test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376380</data>
</node>
<node id="Plasma">
  <data key="d0">Plasma</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Plasma is the liquid component of blood and is listed as a sample type where very long chain fatty acids can be measured.&lt;SEP&gt;Plasma is the liquid portion of blood in which proteins such as prothrombin are dissolved.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-30ae64b33e92c1d03eab2e2ac4026629&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786424624</data>
</node>
<node id="Red Blood Cells">
  <data key="d0">Red Blood Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Red blood cells are cellular components of blood and are mentioned as a sample type for measuring very long chain fatty acids.&lt;SEP&gt;Red blood cells are mature blood cells that carry oxygen throughout the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Red blood cells are the cells whose increased destruction defines hemolytic anemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Red blood cells are cellular components that contain hemoglobin and circulate oxygen in the bloodstream.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells that contain hemoglobin and transport oxygen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19e4810245f812dff5d4b92e29c6f847&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2835448bb481a076c03436c11f787066&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cfde0612413cfdb92dc133bd235f120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405019</data>
</node>
<node id="Family History">
  <data key="d0">Family History</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Family history may indicate the likelihood of ALD because the disease is X‑linked and carried by the female lineage.&lt;SEP&gt;Family History is the recorded presence of genetic diseases within a family and is used in diagnosing Alport syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;Family history of diabetes is a risk factor highlighted for testing insulin resistance and type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Family history of acute porphyria indicates increased risk and prompts screening for the disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Family history refers to having close relatives who have been diagnosed with prostate cancer, identified as a risk factor for the disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ff9d306935e4afa9c10c819a28700dfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c10b11558c17065dc27bd62ccb0fb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e04fc4d9139221a4e00a150baf448e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dfd51ae04f9e4cb50f69eb42e877763</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786425029</data>
</node>
<node id="X‑chromosome">
  <data key="d0">X‑chromosome</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The X‑chromosome is the sex chromosome that carries the gene responsible for ALD, transmitted through female relatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376380</data>
</node>
<node id="Hypertonia">
  <data key="d0">Hypertonia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypertonia is a symptom of excessive muscular tone associated with Adrenoleukodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376380</data>
</node>
<node id="Ataxia">
  <data key="d0">Ataxia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ataxia is a loss of movement coordination listed as a symptom of Adrenoleukodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Ataxia is the lack of muscle control and balance that appears as a primary symptom of Ataxia‑telangiectasia.&lt;SEP&gt;Ataxia is a neurological symptom included in the key terms related to Gulf War Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b66d2f56572161b690b85278b6a11f68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786402898</data>
</node>
<node id="Neuropathy">
  <data key="d0">Neuropathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neuropathy refers to disease or abnormality of peripheral nerves and is mentioned as a symptom of Adrenoleukodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376380</data>
