<node id="Biochemical Test">
  <data key="d0">Biochemical Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The biochemical test detects elevated levels of very long chain fatty acids in various biological samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376380</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Draw">
  <data key="d0">Blood Draw</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood draw is the procedure of collecting blood, mentioned as having minimal risks such as slight bleeding or hematoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood draw is the procedure of collecting a blood sample from a vein for laboratory testing, such as the HLA test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59ae7c2e485dd251483e45f48ced8031</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409381</data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Values">
  <data key="d0">Normal Values</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Normal values are the reference ranges for the test, varying by time of day (morning 8–100 pg/mL, evening &lt;50 pg/mL).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376381</data>
</node>
<node id="Severity Level: Critical">
  <data key="d0">Severity Level: Critical</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Severity Level: Critical denotes that the disease condition is assessed as critical.&lt;SEP&gt;classification indicating the seriousness of infections treated by systemic antifungal drugs.&lt;SEP&gt;Severity Level: Critical indicates that Progressive Supranuclear Palsy is classified as a critical condition due to its progressive and debilitating nature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b6a561225b73fa4827b9e9a8a411e05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2408b24dbbf82011285a46aaece84afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1571076590b816bc3bb0de3b67b9a10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
