<node id="White Blood Cells (Lymphocytes)">
  <data key="d0">White Blood Cells (Lymphocytes)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">White blood cells (lymphocytes) are immune cells destroyed by HIV, especially T cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86d3c253b310c081f68af15bdade4f77</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376522</data>
</node>
<node id="T Cells">
  <data key="d0">T Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">T cells are a subset of white blood cells that carry the CD4 protein and are targeted by HIV.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86d3c253b310c081f68af15bdade4f77</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376522</data>
</node>
<node id="CD4 Protein">
  <data key="d0">CD4 Protein</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">CD4 protein is a surface protein on T cells used by HIV to infect them.&lt;SEP&gt;CD4 Protein is a surface receptor that characterizes CD4+ T‑helper cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86d3c253b310c081f68af15bdade4f77</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396553</data>
</node>
<node id="Opportunistic Infections">
  <data key="d0">Opportunistic Infections</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Opportunistic infections are severe infections that take advantage of the weakened immune system in AIDS patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86d3c253b310c081f68af15bdade4f77</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376522</data>
</node>
<node id="Certain Cancers">
  <data key="d0">Certain Cancers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Certain cancers are malignancies that occur more frequently in individuals with AIDS due to immune deficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86d3c253b310c081f68af15bdade4f77</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376522</data>
</node>
<node id="Central Nervous System">
  <data key="d0">Central Nervous System</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The central nervous system can be affected in AIDS, leading to neurological complications.&lt;SEP&gt;The central nervous system is the target of opioid analgesics' pharmacological action.&lt;SEP&gt;The central nervous system is the target of opioid analgesics' pharmacological action.&lt;SEP&gt;The central nervous system is a part of the body where antiemetics act on pathways to prevent vomiting.&lt;SEP&gt;The central nervous system is the part of the body that can be infected by syphilis, herpes, meningitis, encephalitis, or mumps, leading to hydrocephalus.&lt;SEP&gt;The central nervous system is the part of the nervous system consisting of the brain and spinal cord, which is affected by rabies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04a89a85dc3be8d37412b0c61ebf99cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52f3acaa7cdd3d59b760d2761a2fe751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-414a580eb00a7d0d58696314c2aa7dfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86d3c253b310c081f68af15bdade4f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189651eadb45a933adca499117c49ad</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426199</data>
</node>
<node id="Lymphoproliferative Disease">
  <data key="d0">Lymphoproliferative Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lymphoproliferative disease is a disorder of lymphocyte proliferation associated with AIDS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86d3c253b310c081f68af15bdade4f77</data>
