<node id="Alanine Aminotransferase Test (ALT)">
  <data key="d0">Alanine Aminotransferase Test (ALT)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The alanine aminotransferase test, also known as ALT, is a diagnostic test that can reveal liver damage and is widely used because ALT levels are elevated in most patients with liver disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a048e601dd7e1d6483996e8fa02d2546</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376645</data>
</node>
<node id="Liver Disease">
  <data key="d0">Liver Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Liver disease refers to various disorders of the liver for which ALT levels are typically elevated in most patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver disease impairs the liver's ability to produce haptoglobin, resulting in low haptoglobin levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver disease refers to various disorders of the liver, for which diuretics may be prescribed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8a0239df88721094e3c51f8a7373134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a048e601dd7e1d6483996e8fa02d2546</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410760</data>
</node>
<node id="Gastrointestinal">
  <data key="d0">Gastrointestinal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gastrointestinal denotes the body system associated with the alanine aminotransferase test.&lt;SEP&gt;Body system mentioned as relevant to antenatal testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Gastrointestinal is a body system listed for antihypertensive drug effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Gastrointestinal refers to the digestive system, listed as a body system relevant to pediatric surgery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec2b081d8d4ebb2f1d50934b4b4d93dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c3f104d4a00ee29290d4bff7ae1489&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a048e601dd7e1d6483996e8fa02d2546&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80337a816ac74c4f4d818c5c4c8c74d7</data>
