<node id="Aging">
  <data key="d0">Aging</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Aging is a disease/condition characterized by declining visual abilities, compromised vitamin D production, and other age-related changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Aging refers to the process of growing older, which is the primary focus of gerontology.&lt;SEP&gt;Aging is a condition that can lead to nondeliberate immunosuppression.&lt;SEP&gt;Aging is a process that affects the efficiency of glucose transport in the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b29429d857edf1192105634eda51b928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e04fc4d9139221a4e00a150baf448e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24b86a3178350e10dfda1ff35a2c715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412243</data>
</node>
<node id="Immunological">
  <data key="d0">Immunological</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Immunological refers to the body system affected by aging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376725</data>
</node>
<node id="Senescence">
  <data key="d0">Senescence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Senescence is a cause of aging, representing the natural aging process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376725</data>
</node>
<node id="Vata">
  <data key="d0">Vata</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vata is one of the three main constitutional types in Ayurvedic principles, considered a cause influencing aging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376725</data>
</node>
<node id="Programmed Senescence">
  <data key="d0">Programmed Senescence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Programmed senescence, also known as the aging clock theory, proposes that cellular aging is genetically programmed with a preset number of rejuvenations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376725</data>
</node>
<node id="Macular Degeneration">
  <data key="d0">Macular Degeneration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Macular degeneration is a disease that may result from age-related visual decline.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376725</data>
</node>
<node id="Painkillers">
  <data key="d0">Painkillers</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Painkillers are medications commonly prescribed to the elderly to control symptoms associated with aging.&lt;SEP&gt;Painkillers are medications administered after craniotomy to manage postoperative pain.&lt;SEP&gt;Painkillers are medications used to alleviate muscle aches in patients with paralytic Polio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a43117074cce1d59c31131832dfa007&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422232</data>
</node>
<node id="Diuretics">
  <data key="d0">Diuretics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diuretics, also called water pills, are medications used by older adults to manage conditions related to aging.&lt;SEP&gt;Diuretics, also called water pills, are medications used as a first-line treatment for hypertension.&lt;SEP&gt;Diuretics are drugs that remove excess water from the body and are used to manage aortic valve insufficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Diuretics are urine-producing drugs prescribed to treat ascites by increasing fluid excretion.&lt;SEP&gt;Diuretics are drugs that increase excretion of water and salts in urine, used to treat hypertension, congestive heart failure, liver disease, kidney disease, and can cause hypokalemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Diuretics are drugs mentioned as a key term for managing fluid balance in Polycystic Kidney Disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83aebc72b8b7f7141e25e88c35f39530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8428275c084088f8ee4bf166316b6e01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d855036a34135250bf6b6942f08845d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8a0239df88721094e3c51f8a7373134</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422503</data>
</node>
<node id="Sedatives">
  <data key="d0">Sedatives</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sedatives are drugs prescribed to the elderly to manage symptoms of aging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376725</data>
</node>
<node id="Cardiac Drugs">
  <data key="d0">Cardiac Drugs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cardiac drugs are medications used to treat heart-related conditions in older adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376725</data>
</node>
<node id="Mental Health Drugs">
  <data key="d0">Mental Health Drugs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Mental health drugs are medications used to address mental health issues in older adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376725</data>
</node>
<node id="Estrogen Replacement Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Estrogen Replacement Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Estrogen replacement therapy is a treatment commonly prescribed to postmenopausal women to mitigate aging-related symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376725</data>
</node>
<node id="Healthy Diet">
  <data key="d0">Healthy Diet</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Healthy diet is a preventive health practice that can lengthen lifespan and improve quality of life as people age.&lt;SEP&gt;A healthy diet is recommended for dieters using appetite suppressant drugs to ensure proper nutrition.&lt;SEP&gt;Healthy diet is a nutritional approach that may help reduce symptoms of hyperemesis gravidarum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff53a187c372ebdee1b2526a7ad3f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410003</data>
</node>
<node id="Daily Exercise">
  <data key="d0">Daily Exercise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Daily exercise is a preventive health practice that can improve appetite, bone health, and emotional well-being in aging individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376726</data>
</node>
<node id="Stress Management">
  <data key="d0">Stress Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stress management is a preventive practice that helps maintain health during aging.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress management involves controlling stress levels, which may help lessen hyperemesis gravidarum symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress management encompasses strategies to reduce psychological stress, which can alleviate indigestion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-696bd50fdda11571d3f3a3dd02534eb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786411745</data>
</node>
<node id="Smoking">
  <data key="d0">Smoking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Smoking is a lifestyle habit whose avoidance is recommended to prevent age-related health decline.&lt;SEP&gt;Smoking is a nasal irritant that can lead to rhinitis and exacerbate anosmia.&lt;SEP&gt;Smoking is a nasal irritant that can lead to rhinitis and exacerbate anosmia.&lt;SEP&gt;Smoking worsens the prognosis of asbestosis patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Smoking is a lifestyle risk factor that contributes to hyperlipoproteinemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Smoking is an aspect discussed in prepregnancy counseling as a behavior to avoid.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ac7fad90c3ef5bbb1366ea8a473928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0562388bfd043886184b76d26796a668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb501e7091ee5baf999ac62e451626a7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786423559</data>
</node>
<node id="Drinking">
  <data key="d0">Drinking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Drinking (alcohol consumption) is a lifestyle habit whose moderation is recommended for healthy aging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786376726</data>
</node>
<node id="Antioxidants">
  <data key="d0">Antioxidants</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antioxidants are key terms associated with aging, known for their role in combating oxidative stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Antioxidants are molecules that prevent oxygen molecules from interacting with other molecules in a process called oxidation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd48b3d64142d95730163769979b3bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786386826</data>
</node>
<node id="United States">
  <data key="d0">United States</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">United States is a nation that frequently appears in health‑related statistics and policy discussions, reflecting a broad spectrum of public‑health challenges and achievements. Approximately two‑thirds of Americans aged 65 and older take medications for a variety of age‑related complaints, and the country reports notable amputation rates, a relatively high prevalence of phenylketonuria (PKU), and a growing problem of childhood obesity. Undernutrition is more prevalent among the elderly than among children, and more than one out of ten infants are born prematurely. Giardiasis is increasingly recognized as a concern, particularly among children attending childcare centers, while an estimated 100 000 new hepatitis B infections occur each year; conversely, no hepatitis E outbreaks have been reported. The United States also experiences a substantial burden of sexually transmitted infections, with Chlamydia trachomatis causing more than four million infections annually, and an annual influenza death toll averaging about 20 000, accompanied by significant influenza‑related hospitalizations.

In preventive and clinical medicine, the United States conducts newborn screening for sickle‑cell anemia and administers Haemophilus influenzae type b vaccines as part of routine immunization schedules. The country maintains an extensive pharmaceutical market, having approved numerous anti‑angiogenic agents—including bevacizumab, sorafenib, sunitinib, thalidomide, and erlotinib—as well as a large array of antibiotics for bacterial infections. Public‑health initiatives have yielded measurable outcomes: mosquito‑control programs have contributed to the elimination of malaria within U.S. borders, and legislative actions have successfully reduced asbestos use, underscoring a broader commitment to mitigating environmental health hazards.

The United States’ healthcare system underwent a comprehensive restructuring through the passage of the Affordable Care Act, aiming to expand coverage and improve affordability. Occupational health concerns have also been highlighted, as military personnel and allied forces reported Gulf War Syndrome following combat deployments. Culturally, the United States is the country where Hatha Yoga is most widely practiced, reflecting a broad embrace of physical and mental exercise, and it was the nation where public bathhouses first appeared, marking the spread of hydrotherapy to America.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is the country where prostatitis prevalence data are reported.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is the country referenced for prostate cancer prevalence statistics.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is the country where puerperal infection affects an estimated 1–8% of new mothers.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is a country where rabies cases are infrequent, averaging one or two per year.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is a country where streptobacillary rat-bite fever is reported.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is the country where approximately 5,000–10,000 radical neck dissections are performed each year.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b14c26a47ca283ef7a5696f26a6c99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2679367b0beba9113c18be86c1ebf3c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cac3b15cf6eb4edf007b3be55fb814e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abbfd6cbf4afd6662ba2707fbc17c147&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19e4810245f812dff5d4b92e29c6f847&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc626b00afed53316810372730831c40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7496588525e64482c4ff86b39c6a814&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d82066907ae788a5c895e3b1bededab3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43384133dfe3fd1b2a03d01d15878f94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6564f0ba00e16734a472181bcd545e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a89a85dc3be8d37412b0c61ebf99cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c63f65bb800d3d7fae8a0864fc3cdf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3c89277f1dc142f48af64dbc9698621&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f49c33435524f5d8ed6badce93b4057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708af40669770fee42a9a9b052181fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edba73be60673b1668775ee43b5d8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee131fba1e9c2ffd9b0f33ae3d9ff27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b66d2f56572161b690b85278b6a11f68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9acb51065e727736eeeac34449f610b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a683508f811fbb08d10cc5a67bd08ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a62b13a067bbff6ba6a45d67ea3a11ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a31e273096780949be269771f5c7b3b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebc93901c908c91f026b8f84613ebc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bca77605ecf717ab8187e9673827ff86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-097e88fc7e1ff542a919812e0d0d508a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8ffed90e8805478f1786896b19a574a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426813</data>
</node>
<node id="Agoraphobia">
  <data key="d0">Agoraphobia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Agoraphobia is an irrational and often disabling fear of being out in public, characterized by anxiety about places where escape might be difficult or help unavailable, leading to avoidance and possible housebound state.&lt;SEP&gt;Agoraphobia is a phobia involving fear of open spaces, traffic, elevators, and escalators, making it harder to treat than other phobias.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af3b4b939a2aeb8a2dffe85570c09b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b7ae47fed28c48dbd20bd5a3891afd1</data>
