<node id="Complications">
  <data key="d0">Complications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Complications refer to possible adverse effects such as bruising, dizziness, and discomfort that may arise after the alkaline phosphatase test.&lt;SEP&gt;Complications are adverse effects such as pain, bleeding, and discomfort that can follow a prostate biopsy.&lt;SEP&gt;Potential postoperative issues such as discharge timing, hospital stay, incision care, and activity restrictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Complications refer to potential postoperative issues such as shallow breathing and the need for vital sign monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Complications are adverse outcomes following radical neck dissection, including hospital stay and the need for drains.</data>
