<node id="Pregnancy">
  <data key="d0">Pregnancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pregnancy is the physiological condition in which a woman carries a developing embryo or fetus in the womb.  It is a normal, hormonally driven state that marks the period from conception until birth, and it is the primary area of clinical expertise for gynecologists, who monitor fetal development and maternal health throughout this time.  

During pregnancy, hormone levels rise markedly, which can give rise to several medical conditions.  The increased hormonal milieu may trigger gestational diabetes, a form of glucose intolerance that appears only during pregnancy.  The expanding uterus can also exert pressure on surrounding structures, leading to ureteral obstruction in some cases.  Additionally, the physiological changes associated with pregnancy often cause elevated alkaline phosphatase levels in blood tests and may produce false‑positive results on HLA (human leukocyte antigen) testing.  

Pregnant women are also prone to certain mechanical and vascular issues.  The growing uterus can increase venous pressure in the pelvic region, contributing to the development of hemorrhoids.  These and other pregnancy‑related complications are routinely assessed and managed by obstetric care providers to ensure the health of both mother and child.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnancy is the gestational period during which the cervix normally stays closed until labor begins.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnancy is the condition of carrying a developing embryo or fetus, the desired outcome of Infertility Drugs.&lt;SEP&gt;The gestational period during which maternal infections can be transmitted to the fetus.&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnancy&lt;SEP&gt;Pregnancy is the condition of carrying a developing embryo or fetus within the woman's body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2679367b0beba9113c18be86c1ebf3c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c98e85575a0fbf6c6f4d4ea25dc15ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d5f82c915dbc402d1fdeb23f98439f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59ae7c2e485dd251483e45f48ced8031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cc9b041882b1ffceb3664e339701aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a51c332fdfaf8c96be6ab58c809b221&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a9a426a4bb2afd30f9a958bbb935d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdce04fe6b7fc2f2383ff5401c7803f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b03362a1a14b83e88e498b918bc854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cef0181d6e65ea01360302ddd1f7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422886</data>
</node>
