</node>
<node id="Headache">
  <data key="d0">Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Headache is a symptom that may precede the onset of Allergic Purpura.&lt;SEP&gt;Headache is a possible side effect of Accupril.&lt;SEP&gt;Headache is a somatic symptom of anxiety involving pain in the head.&lt;SEP&gt;Headache may occur after craniotomy due to stretching or irritation of scalp nerves.&lt;SEP&gt;Headache is a disorder characterized by pain in the head, which can arise from various primary or secondary causes.&lt;SEP&gt;Headache is a symptom of pain pain.&lt;SEP&gt;Headache is a possible symptom experienced by individuals with hypertension.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cef0181d6e65ea01360302ddd1f7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-540eabf6d4c3ae30f94409ef704b5804&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b4f1384d965014ddcabd93b7495e501&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80337a816ac74c4f4d818c5c4c8c74d7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410340</data>
</node>
<node id="Fever">
  <data key="d0">Fever</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fever is a symptom that may precede the onset of Allergic Purpura.&lt;SEP&gt;An elevated body temperature that can contribute to the occurrence of heart murmurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Fever is a common symptom experienced during hepatitis E infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Fever is an elevated body temperature that can act as a secondary cause of hyperhidrosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Fever is a rise in body temperature and a typical symptom of influenza.&lt;SEP&gt;Fever is the primary symptom of puerperal infection, defined as a temperature of 100.4 °F (38 °C) on two days or 101.6 °F (38.6 °C) within the first 24 hours postpartum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b14c26a47ca283ef7a5696f26a6c99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc626b00afed53316810372730831c40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ed665cb566f37b833eec31484ae9ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cef0181d6e65ea01360302ddd1f7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3167aac9bbeb660fe5ef8b641759df31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6564f0ba00e16734a472181bcd545e9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426141</data>
</node>
<node id="Loss of Appetite">
  <data key="d0">Loss of Appetite</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Loss of appetite is a symptom that may precede the onset of Allergic Purpura.&lt;SEP&gt;Loss of Appetite is a symptom of autoimmune hepatitis where patients feel reduced desire to eat.&lt;SEP&gt;Loss of appetite is a symptom associated with hepatitis E infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b14c26a47ca283ef7a5696f26a6c99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3978e5151245a8ce567b224992eabb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e46cef0181d6e65ea01360302ddd1f7b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405172</data>
</node>
<node id="Itchy Skin Rash">
  <data key="d0">Itchy Skin Rash</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Itchy skin rash is a common early symptom of Allergic Purpura, presenting as red patches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e46cef0181d6e65ea01360302ddd1f7b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377292</data>
</node>
