  <data key="d0">Illustration</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The illustration shows excessive mucus production in the nose after inhalation of airborne pollen, representing a symptom of allergic rhinitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60186ecba821e292a6f92302d8c6ca5e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377312</data>
</node>
<node id="Allergen">
  <data key="d0">Allergen</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An allergen is a substance that induces an allergic reaction, listed among key terms for allergic rhinitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Allergen is a foreign substance that can trigger an allergic reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Allergen is a substance that can cause allergic reactions, contributing to rhinitis and nasal polyps.&lt;SEP&gt;Allergen is a substance that can cause allergic reactions, contributing to rhinitis and nasal polyps.&lt;SEP&gt;Allergen is a key term representing substances that can trigger immune responses</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60186ecba821e292a6f92302d8c6ca5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb501e7091ee5baf999ac62e451626a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3978e5151245a8ce567b224992eabb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fea6119439079b171fb416dd0c1a0f6a</data>
