<node id="Perennial Allergic Rhinitis">
  <data key="d0">Perennial Allergic Rhinitis</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60186ecba821e292a6f92302d8c6ca5e</data>
  <data key="d2">Perennial allergic rhinitis is usually caused by exposure to home or workplace airborne substances.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377320</data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Cancer">
  <data key="d0">Skin Cancer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin cancer is a potential oncological condition that may develop later in life for individuals with albinism due to lack of pigment.&lt;SEP&gt;Skin cancer is a severe condition that may require surgical removal, mentioned in the treatment section.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6007bd886198fad2e92df82e7baf0b56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410478</data>
</node>
<node id="Eye Problems">
  <data key="d0">Eye Problems</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Eye problems refer to visual impairments such as nystagmus and strabismus commonly associated with albinism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377490</data>
</node>
<node id="Pigment">
  <data key="d0">Pigment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pigment, primarily melanin, provides color to skin, hair, and eyes; its deficiency characterizes albinism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377490</data>
</node>
<node id="Inheritance">
  <data key="d0">Inheritance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inheritance describes the genetic transmission of albinism from parents to offspring through flawed genes.&lt;SEP&gt;GSD is inherited; if both parents carry defective gene, 25% chance offspring inherit disorder.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25a42943ad0f93e6631565dc2c851d36</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786401780</data>
</node>
<node id="DNA">
  <data key="d0">DNA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DNA is the molecular carrier of genetic information that includes the genes responsible for melanin production.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA is a cellular component that can be damaged by free radicals if not protected by antioxidants.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is the genetic material analyzed in parentage testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b785ff55416d26c9c9d2574c29ca4711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd48b3d64142d95730163769979b3bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786418836</data>
</node>
<node id="DOPA">
  <data key="d0">DOPA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DOPA is a biochemical precursor in the melanin synthesis pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377491</data>
</node>
<node id="Amino Acids">
  <data key="d0">Amino Acids</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Amino acids are organic compounds that serve as building blocks for proteins and enzymes involved in melanin production.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic compounds that are the building blocks of proteins and are central to amino acid metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-708af40669770fee42a9a9b052181fce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786379487</data>
</node>
<node id="Astigmatism">
  <data key="d0">Astigmatism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Astigmatism is a refractive eye condition that can be present among individuals with albinism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377491</data>
</node>
<node id="Carrier">
  <data key="d0">Carrier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carrier denotes an individual who possesses one copy of a recessive albinism gene without manifesting the condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Carrier is an individual who possesses a defective gene for Alport syndrome without showing symptoms, capable of passing it to offspring.&lt;SEP&gt;Carrier refers to an individual who harbors the hepatitis B virus without showing symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dfd51ae04f9e4cb50f69eb42e877763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edba73be60673b1668775ee43b5d8dd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405096</data>
</node>
<node id="Hairbulb">
  <data key="d0">Hairbulb</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hairbulb refers to the follicular structure where hair pigment is produced and is affected in albinism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377491</data>
</node>
<node id="Albinism">
  <data key="d0">Albinism</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b83572ef3bc13b6de1b3591b9a778c3</data>
  <data key="d2">Albinism may lead to skin cancer later in life due to lack of protective pigment.&lt;SEP&gt;Albinism is the condition of lacking melanin pigment, leading to reduced protection against sunlight.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420750</data>
</node>
<node id="Genes">
  <data key="d0">Genes</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9102756028539b9228bf8362c3e96772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b20a7bdac3dcdeae955d7f5fcff8809</data>
  <data key="d2">Genes encode enzymes that direct melanin production; defects reduce melanin.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes are inherited biological factors that may partly determine temperament traits related to personality disorders.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes are hereditary units that influence drug responses and various body functions.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420263</data>
</node>
<node id="Melanin">
  <data key="d0">Melanin</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d028b3e3f4cefe67cb0e2fd00c4e75c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b83572ef3bc13b6de1b3591b9a778c3</data>
  <data key="d2">Genes encode enzymes that direct melanin production; defects reduce melanin.&lt;SEP&gt;Melanin is the skin pigment that provides natural protection against sunlight damage.</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420750</data>
</node>
<node id="Aldosterone Assay">
  <data key="d0">Aldosterone Assay</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Aldosterone Assay is a diagnostic test that measures the levels of aldosterone in blood or urine specimens.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7913b0884240a87bdd0d8c498ec19f82</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377737</data>
</node>
<node id="Adrenal Glands">
  <data key="d0">Adrenal Glands</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Adrenal Glands are a pair of endocrine organs located atop each kidney that produce aldosterone.&lt;SEP&gt;The adrenal glands, located on top of the kidneys, produce four separate kinds of hormones that regulate metabolism, stress response, and other bodily functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7913b0884240a87bdd0d8c498ec19f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01a42939570e7d067a66881fea563910</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422228</data>
</node>
<node id="Aldosteronism">
  <data key="d0">Aldosteronism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Aldosteronism is a medical condition caused by excess secretion of aldosterone from the adrenal glands.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7913b0884240a87bdd0d8c498ec19f82</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377737</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Blood Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Pressure is the physiological force exerted by circulating blood against the walls of blood vessels, particularly the arterial walls, as the heart pumps blood through the circulatory system. This force results from the interaction of cardiac output, blood volume, and vascular resistance, and it is influenced by factors such as water balance, blood volume, and the activity of the autonomic nervous system. Pharmacological agents such as alpha‑1‑adrenergic blockers can lower blood pressure by reducing peripheral vascular resistance.

Blood pressure is a standard vital sign that is routinely measured in clinical practice. It is expressed numerically as a systolic value (the pressure during cardiac contraction) over a diastolic value (the pressure during cardiac relaxation). Monitoring of blood pressure provides essential information about cardiovascular health and is used to assess the safety and recovery of patients after surgical procedures, including hydrocelectomy and other operations.

In research and therapeutic contexts, blood pressure is also tracked as a specific outcome measure. For example, it is a monitored physiological parameter in studies involving women receiving hormone replacement therapy (HRT), where changes in vascular dynamics may occur. Overall, blood pressure serves as a key indicator of circulatory function, reflecting the combined effects of heart performance, blood volume, and vascular tone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a3b3c33dc539d83724153cf8bd92691&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b4f1384d965014ddcabd93b7495e501&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1089fcdf26e7799dcc1972363c2c7c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8428275c084088f8ee4bf166316b6e01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a70a3ab31498f37b121780c8c0792259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7913b0884240a87bdd0d8c498ec19f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5922b682f2c38e37dd9bd7f8f614180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdce04fe6b7fc2f2383ff5401c7803f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422893</data>
</node>
<node id="Sodium">
  <data key="d0">Sodium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium is an electrolyte whose blood concentration is regulated by aldosterone.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium is an essential mineral element whose levels in the blood are regulated by aldosterone.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium is a chemical element whose intake is restricted to approximately 3 g per day before the PRA test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d56ee0cdfdf24e5c7abc6d2486262d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35c30232e67a5a9d2bf59484035c1a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7913b0884240a87bdd0d8c498ec19f82</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786421622</data>
</node>
<node id="Potassium">
  <data key="d0">Potassium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium is an electrolyte whose blood concentration is regulated by aldosterone.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium is an essential mineral element whose levels in the blood are regulated by aldosterone.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium is an essential electrolyte that facilitates nerve impulse conduction, contraction of skeletal and smooth muscles, cell membrane function, and enzyme activity; normally present at 3.5–5.0 mEq/L in serum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8a0239df88721094e3c51f8a7373134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7913b0884240a87bdd0d8c498ec19f82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d56ee0cdfdf24e5c7abc6d2486262d6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410760</data>
</node>
<node id="Water Balance">
  <data key="d0">Water Balance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Water Balance refers to the maintenance of appropriate body water levels, affected by sodium and potassium regulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7913b0884240a87bdd0d8c498ec19f82</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377738</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Volume">
  <data key="d0">Blood Volume</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Volume is the total amount of blood circulating in the body, influencing blood pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7913b0884240a87bdd0d8c498ec19f82</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377738</data>
</node>
