<node id="Alcohol Intoxication">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol Intoxication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol intoxication is a condition marked by talkativeness and positive mood when BAC rises and depression and mental impairment when it falls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b5b4ede4683a3be477e4527fbbb8cad</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377853</data>
</node>
<node id="Psychiatric">
  <data key="d0">Psychiatric</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Psychiatric refers to the body‑system category that encompasses mental health and the conditions, behaviors, and treatments associated with it. In this sense, the psychiatric system is the domain of the human body concerned with psychological well‑being, cognition, emotion, and related disorders.  

The psychiatric system is implicated in a range of clinical contexts. It is affected by substance‑related issues such as alcoholism, and it is the primary target of pharmacological interventions including antipsychotic medications as well as alternative approaches such as homeopathic remedies. In addition to medication, the system is central to various therapeutic modalities; it underlies the practice of psychotherapy broadly and includes specific approaches such as Gestalt therapy.  

The scope of the psychiatric system also extends to demographic and lifespan considerations. It is linked to gerontology, reflecting the importance of mental‑health care for older adults, and it integrates with the broader field of mental‑health research and practice. In all of these respects, “psychiatric” functions as a descriptor for the bodily and clinical domain that addresses mental health across pharmacological, psychotherapeutic, and demographic dimensions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80bdc5e62cc3de9c461969117469e796&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1259d33cdef2f40569e2a9b8ef612487&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8a323d4236a65c6a130c075aa9de815&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5e4b4100d5e6ad6ec77e0fab7182b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b914f2eb8e464a9d70f7d72f05cc69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24b86a3178350e10dfda1ff35a2c715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b5b4ede4683a3be477e4527fbbb8cad</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786425956</data>
</node>
<node id="Hematological">
  <data key="d0">Hematological</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hematological refers to the blood-related body system impacted by alcoholism.&lt;SEP&gt;Hematological relates to blood and its components.&lt;SEP&gt;Hematological relates to blood and its components.&lt;SEP&gt;Body system mentioned as relevant to antenatal testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Hematological is a body system mentioned as one of the systems addressed by radiology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b5b4ede4683a3be477e4527fbbb8cad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c190f7502921527346a5beaed7b2382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5e4b4100d5e6ad6ec77e0fab7182b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c3f104d4a00ee29290d4bff7ae1489</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426705</data>
</node>
<node id="Milk">
  <data key="d0">Milk</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Milk is a food allergen mentioned in the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fea6119439079b171fb416dd0c1a0f6a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377853</data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnostic and Statistical Manual">
  <data key="d0">Diagnostic and Statistical Manual</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnostic and Statistical Manual is a reference source used for diagnosing alcoholism (partial reference in text).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b5b4ede4683a3be477e4527fbbb8cad</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377853</data>
</node>
<node id="Eggs">
  <data key="d0">Eggs</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Eggs are a food allergen mentioned in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Eggs are the female reproductive cells removed from a woman's ovary for fertilization in IVF.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-929ba0da65b01f36a714e919c35cad8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fea6119439079b171fb416dd0c1a0f6a</data>
