<node id="Bed Rest">
  <data key="d0">Bed Rest</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bed rest is a prescribed method for patients with amebic liver abscess during hospitalization.&lt;SEP&gt;Bed rest is a treatment approach that reduces salt absorption by the kidneys, used in managing ascites.&lt;SEP&gt;A conservative treatment recommendation of up to 48 hours for herniated disk patients without serious neurologic symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Bed rest is a medical recommendation to limit activity, sometimes used to prevent premature labor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02e1b300199e25407d954c8745371d3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c63f65bb800d3d7fae8a0864fc3cdf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaa529cbf4202ca2218a48e019cb104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
