</node>
<node id="Anal Atresia">
  <data key="d0">Anal Atresia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anal atresia is a severe congenital disorder where the anus is absent or located incorrectly.&lt;SEP&gt;Anal atresia is a congenital condition affecting the anal opening, with varying severity levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Anal atresia is a congenital condition affecting the anal opening, with varying severity levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e8c9c7c02e8411303e8d4d577cb23c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-039b8130a20b6f937b48c9084aa01ee2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383938</data>
</node>
<node id="High Anal Atresia">
  <data key="d0">High Anal Atresia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High anal atresia is a form of anal atresia in which a fistulous channel may connect the large intestine to the urethra or bladder in boys, or to the vagina in girls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-039b8130a20b6f937b48c9084aa01ee2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786378855</data>
</node>
<node id="Low Anal Atresia">
  <data key="d0">Low Anal Atresia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low anal atresia is a form of anal atresia where the fistulous channel may open in front of the anal sphincter or, in boys, below the scrotum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-039b8130a20b6f937b48c9084aa01ee2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786378855</data>
</node>
<node id="Urethra">
  <data key="d0">Urethra</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The urethra is the tube that conveys urine from the bladder and can be joined to a fistula in high anal atresia in boys.&lt;SEP&gt;The urethra is a bodily passage where gonorrhea bacteria can grow.&lt;SEP&gt;The urethra is the tube that conveys urine from the bladder to the outside of the body, whose opening location defines hypospadias and epispadias.&lt;SEP&gt;The urethra is the tube that conducts urine from the bladder to the exterior of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The urethra is a tube that carries urine out of the bladder and is mentioned as a key term related to prostate ultrasound.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-870bb1b70305260567e1654eccb86793&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edfaa9dba99a768f9ffcf5c77b2d0525&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-039b8130a20b6f937b48c9084aa01ee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1a5a0f435acaf25e4ffe723e71d08b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14cced56b63272cdcfcc286787f3aa8d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786424961</data>
</node>
<node id="Amylase">
  <data key="d0">Amylase</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Amylase is a digestive enzyme made primarily by the pancreas and salivary glands that breaks down starches in food.&lt;SEP&gt;Amylase is an enzyme whose blood levels rise in amyloidosis while urine levels remain normal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-012e85679bddc890f1489e743c060e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08dacc20215db14b42730a5441dcba75</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786379169</data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreas">
  <data key="d0">Pancreas</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreas is an organ that produces amylase among other digestive enzymes.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas is an organ that secretes insulin, a hormone that helps regulate blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;A 6 to 8-inch slipper-shaped gland in the abdomen that produces digestive juices and plays a critical role in metabolic processes&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreas is the organ that releases enzymes, which can cause irritation during pancreatitis and lead to secondary peritonitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ecef8b1cb75d3c911d063994b3f226f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e04fc4d9139221a4e00a150baf448e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a3ecc34ed1c5383ab2125e8cf323393&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-012e85679bddc890f1489e743c060e63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419845</data>
</node>
<node id="Salivary Glands">
  <data key="d0">Salivary Glands</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Salivary Glands are organs that produce amylase for the initial digestion of starches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-012e85679bddc890f1489e743c060e63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786379023</data>
</node>
