</node>
<node id="Dental Infections">
  <data key="d0">Dental Infections</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dental infections are infections of the teeth, commonly caused by anaerobic bacteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c1acfa8b3bcf6abb174b1db6c3878690</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786379294</data>
</node>
<node id="Vagina">
  <data key="d0">Vagina</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The vagina is a body location where anaerobic bacteria are normally found.&lt;SEP&gt;The vagina is the female internal sexual organ into which the urethra may open in the female form of hypospadias.&lt;SEP&gt;Vagina is the canal where a speculum is inserted.&lt;SEP&gt;The vagina is the birth canal through which a physician accesses the cervix during hysteroscopy.&lt;SEP&gt;Vagina is the anatomical passage referenced as the route through which Culpocentesis removes ascitic fluid from the bottom of the abdominal cavity.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal canal into which a gloved finger is inserted for palpation during a pelvic exam.&lt;SEP&gt;The vagina is a female reproductive organ located anterior to the rectum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-506592426d0a0ade6d5d62f2ac15f607&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7a1c4e1372979af71be73cfdd576ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1acfa8b3bcf6abb174b1db6c3878690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ccba52c964c301daf559927d7d7c5e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9caaa60cd1726424ba3202fd3c2999a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-405f3438c94303b670da4ac7ad2e23a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14cced56b63272cdcfcc286787f3aa8d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426767</data>
</node>
