</node>
<node id="General Anesthesia">
  <data key="d0">General Anesthesia</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">General anesthesia induces unconsciousness and eliminates pain sensation throughout the entire body, used during certain medical and surgical procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;General anesthesia induces unconsciousness and eliminates pain sensation throughout the entire body, used during certain medical and surgical procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;General anesthesia is a method of anesthesia that may be used during a gastrostomy.&lt;SEP&gt;An anesthetic state induced in a patient before starting the transplant surgery.`&lt;SEP&gt;General anesthesia is a medically induced state of unconsciousness used during many cosmetic surgeries.&lt;SEP&gt;General anesthesia is a technique to render a patient unconscious and pain‑free during extensive surgeries such as pneumonectomy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5972068248f50904396788f92782210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b980f05326d81e805160717f42418e84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-924349d7f1e96f2f4001c672cc617820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f81367bc23721681b080e8e55f88ab71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a321ea72ebe4c42d67faa7f47af64c7</data>
