<node id="Antibody">
  <data key="d0">Antibody</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibody is an immunoglobulin protein produced by the immune system that specifically recognizes and binds to antigens.  As a class of proteins, antibodies include various isotypes such as IgE, which play a role in allergic responses.  By attaching to foreign molecules, antibodies can neutralize pathogens, mark them for destruction, or directly destroy invading viruses, including hepatitis B virus (HBV), hepatitis E virus, and hepatitis A virus (HAV).  In clinical practice, the presence and concentration of specific antibodies may be measured to aid in the diagnosis of infections such as aspergillosis.  Overall, antibodies function as targeted agents that bind to distinct antigens and facilitate the immune system’s effort to eliminate or control harmful microorganisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibody is a key term related to the immune system.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibody is a protein produced by the immune system that can neutralize pathogens like the rabies virus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b14c26a47ca283ef7a5696f26a6c99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a89a85dc3be8d37412b0c61ebf99cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97bc31370eb8948b543aaf5f06eb9116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59ae7c2e485dd251483e45f48ced8031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6007bd886198fad2e92df82e7baf0b56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edba73be60673b1668775ee43b5d8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e59ab8338831484ea61486c70a6ad038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeb4dffb5ad505f4839faaa747910b3c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426202</data>
</node>
