<node id="Anorectal Abscesses">
  <data key="d0">Anorectal Abscesses</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7cf07655a8780ee831372742398affa8</data>
  <data key="d2">Treatment for anorectal abscesses consists of cutting the abscess and draining the pus.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786381434</data>
</node>
<node id="Anorectal Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Anorectal Disorders</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7cf07655a8780ee831372742398affa8</data>
  <data key="d2">Anorectal disorders are a group of medical disorders that occur at the junction of the anal canal and the rectum.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786381434</data>
</node>
<node id="Hemorrhoids">
  <data key="d0">Hemorrhoids</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91b03362a1a14b83e88e498b918bc854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cf07655a8780ee831372742398affa8</data>
  <data key="d2">Most hemorrhoids will heal if the patient takes stool softeners to relieve the constipation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemorrhoids are bulges in the veins around the anus that can cause swelling, pain, and bleeding.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786385811</data>
</node>
<node id="Rectum">
  <data key="d0">Rectum</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7294fc7c2531b2723bf6002b6e65eee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cf07655a8780ee831372742398affa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abbfd6cbf4afd6662ba2707fbc17c147&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ccba52c964c301daf559927d7d7c5e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dad561d3742857b36b06aba05376ddc3</data>
  <data key="d2">Anorectal disorders are a group of medical disorders that occur at the junction of the anal canal and the rectum.&lt;SEP&gt;The rectum is the lower part of the large intestine where Proctitis causes inflammation.&lt;SEP&gt;The rectum is part of the digestive tract and can serve as a wall through which a needle is inserted for prostate biopsy.&lt;SEP&gt;The rectum is the portion of the large bowel located in the pelvis, extending from the colon to the anus and bounded by surrounding organs and bone.&lt;SEP&gt;The rectum is the final part of the large intestine where polyps develop."&lt;SEP&gt;The rectum is the final part of the large intestine where polyps develop.</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786427056</data>
</node>
