</node>
<node id="Childhood Obesity">
  <data key="d0">Childhood Obesity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Childhood obesity is a severe overweight condition affecting individuals aged two to nineteen years, noted as a public health concern in the United States.  `</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7496588525e64482c4ff86b39c6a814</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383895</data>
</node>
<node id="U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention">
  <data key="d0">U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention is a federal public health agency referenced in the definition of childhood obesity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7496588525e64482c4ff86b39c6a814</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383895</data>
</node>
<node id="Body Mass Index">
  <data key="d0">Body Mass Index</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Body Mass Index is a calculation comparing a person's weight and height, used by healthcare professionals to assess obesity, with adjustments for age and gender in children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7496588525e64482c4ff86b39c6a814</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383895</data>
</node>
<node id="Harvard School of Public Health">
  <data key="d0">Harvard School of Public Health</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Harvard School of Public Health conducted a 2006 study on calorie consumption among American children, linking excess intake to obesity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7496588525e64482c4ff86b39c6a814</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383895</data>
</node>
<node id="Pediatrics">
  <data key="d0">Pediatrics</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Pediatrics is a scientific journal that published the Harvard School of Public Health study on childhood calorie excess and obesity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7496588525e64482c4ff86b39c6a814</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383895</data>
</node>
<node id="Energy Gap">
  <data key="d0">Energy Gap</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Energy Gap refers to the difference between calorie intake and expenditure, identified as a simple cause of obesity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7496588525e64482c4ff86b39c6a814</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383895</data>
</node>
<node id="Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 2 Diabetes is a disease increasingly observed in adolescents and young adults, associated with increased risk for children with obesity.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 diabetes is a chronic condition that many women who had gestational diabetes may develop later in life.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 diabetes is a chronic metabolic disease characterized by high blood sugar, for which the NIDDK recommends screening in adults over 45 and at‑risk younger</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e04fc4d9139221a4e00a150baf448e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7496588525e64482c4ff86b39c6a814&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412244</data>
</node>
<node id="Healthcare Professionals">
  <data key="d0">Healthcare Professionals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Healthcare Professionals are the practitioners who calculate obesity using Body Mass Index and assess childhood obesity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7496588525e64482c4ff86b39c6a814</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383896</data>
</node>
<node id="Calories">
  <data key="d0">Calories</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Calories represent the unit of energy intake, with excess consumption identified as a cause of childhood obesity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7496588525e64482c4ff86b39c6a814</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383896</data>
</node>
<node id="Body Fat">
  <data key="d0">Body Fat</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Body Fat is the accumulation of adipose&lt;SEP&gt;Body fat is tissue where many lipophilic drugs are stored, influencing drug availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9102756028539b9228bf8362c3e96772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7496588525e64482c4ff86b39c6a814</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420263</data>
</node>
<node id="Labor">
  <data key="d0">Labor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Labor is the process of birth, a phase within childbirth that involves cervical dilation and uterine contractions.&lt;SEP&gt;Labor is the process of childbirth that is brought on or induced to deliver the baby.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8fa92ebcec8228939de0a7b767b729f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786411944</data>
</node>
<node id="Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Delivery is the birth itself, the final stage of childbirth when the infant exits the birth canal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383927</data>
</node>
<node id="Cervix">
  <data key="d0">Cervix</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cervix is the lower, neck-like portion of the uterus that forms the opening between the uterine cavity and the vagina in the female reproductive system. It serves as the conduit through which instruments such as catheters and hysteroscopes are inserted for procedures like hysteroscopy, and it is the site accessed during routine pelvic examinations and cervical cell sampling (e.g., Pap smears).  

During a normal pregnancy the cervix remains tightly closed, providing a barrier that protects the developing fetus. In the course of labor it undergoes dramatic dilation, expanding from essentially 0 cm to about 10 cm to allow passage of the baby. The cervix can be evaluated non‑invasively with pelvic ultrasound, which visualizes its length, thickness, and position.  

In addition to its mechanical functions, the cervix is susceptible to certain infections; for example, primary genital herpes infection may involve the cervical tissue as a complication. Overall, the cervix is a crucial anatomical structure that both protects the uterine environment and facilitates medical access to the upper reproductive tract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-506592426d0a0ade6d5d62f2ac15f607&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6407dc79c35579b5387abf2b05a97d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be7a1c4e1372979af71be73cfdd576ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cc9b041882b1ffceb3664e339701aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d126a4f2dfaa975afdfed278c2386bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9caaa60cd1726424ba3202fd3c2999a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419827</data>
</node>
<node id="Bloody Show">
  <data key="d0">Bloody Show</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bloody Show is a symptom indicating a small amount of blood-tinged mucus released from the cervix as it begins to dilate, signaling approaching childbirth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383927</data>
</node>
<node id="Mucus Plug">
  <data key="d0">Mucus Plug</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mucus Plug is the term for the mucus barrier that may be released during the bloody show as the cervix dilates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383927</data>
</node>
<node id="Contractions">
  <data key="d0">Contractions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Contractions are uterine muscle tightenings that signal the onset of labor and become stronger and longer over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383927</data>
</node>
<node id="True Labor Pains">
  <data key="d0">True Labor Pains</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">True Labor Pains are regular, progressively stronger uterine contractions that indicate genuine labor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383928</data>
</node>
<node id="False Labor Pains">
  <data key="d0">False Labor Pains</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">False Labor Pains are irregular uterine contractions that may be mistaken for true labor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383928</data>
</node>
<node id="Doppler Method">
  <data key="d0">Doppler Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Doppler method uses ultrasound with a handheld device to listen to fetal heart sounds during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383928</data>
</node>
<node id="Ultrasound">
  <data key="d0">Ultrasound</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultrasound is an imaging technique that employs high‑frequency sound waves to produce real‑time pictures of internal body structures. By transmitting sound pulses and interpreting the returning echoes, it enables clinicians to visualize organs, fluids, and blood flow without ionizing radiation, and it forms the basis of Doppler methods that assess vascular motion.

In obstetrics, ultrasound is routinely used for antenatal testing, allowing clinicians to monitor fetal development, confirm viability, and detect congenital abnormalities early in pregnancy. Its safety profile and portability make it a cornerstone of prenatal care.

In broader diagnostic practice, ultrasound is applied to evaluate cardiovascular and abdominal conditions. It can identify an enlarged aorta and assess valve function, aiding in the detection of aneurysms or valvular disease. In the abdomen, the modality readily detects ascitic fluid and characterizes renal abnormalities such as kidney enlargement and the cystic changes typical of Polycystic Kidney Disease. Neurologically, ultrasound can be employed to locate obstructions in the ventricular system of patients with hydrocephalus, providing guidance for therapeutic interventions.

Overall, ultrasound serves as a versatile, non‑invasive imaging method widely used in radiology to visualize internal structures across multiple organ systems, supporting diagnosis, monitoring, and procedural guidance in diverse clinical settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c190f7502921527346a5beaed7b2382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83aebc72b8b7f7141e25e88c35f39530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-414a580eb00a7d0d58696314c2aa7dfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d855036a34135250bf6b6942f08845d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b63fc7d102b55c2843666075d6ad7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07c3f104d4a00ee29290d4bff7ae1489</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426710</data>
</node>
<node id="Handheld Listening Device">
  <data key="d0">Handheld Listening Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A handheld listening device is used in the Doppler method to transmit fetal heart sounds to a speaker or ear piece.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383928</data>
</node>
<node id="Pain Relief">
  <data key="d0">Pain Relief</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pain relief encompasses various techniques and medications used to alleviate discomfort during childbirth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383928</data>
</node>
<node id="Relaxation and Imagery">
  <data key="d0">Relaxation and Imagery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Relaxation and imagery are non‑pharmacological pain relief methods involving mental techniques to reduce labor pain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383928</data>
</node>
<node id="Drugs">
  <data key="d0">Drugs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Drugs are pharmacological agents used for pain relief during childbirth, each with associated risks and benefits.&lt;SEP&gt;Drugs are chemical agents that can cause liver inflammation.&lt;SEP&gt;Drugs are used in the treatment of hypothyinroidism.&lt;SEP&gt;Drugs are chemical substances used for medical treatment, whose actions and reactions can vary based on genetic factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Drugs is an aspect discussed in prepregnancy counseling as a behavior to avoid.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9102756028539b9228bf8362c3e96772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1385133e299def4ed989633bdbd7168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0562388bfd043886184b76d26796a668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fe1b59b257b5d344c7de5181dbff9d0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786423559</data>
</node>
<node id="Regional Anesthetics">
  <data key="d0">Regional Anesthetics</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Regional anesthetics are pain relief techniques, such as epidurals and spinals, involving injection near spinal nerves.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383929</data>
</node>
<node id="Epidurals">
  <data key="d0">Epidurals</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Epidurals are a type of regional anesthetic involving medication injection into the epidural space for pain relief.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383929</data>
</node>
<node id="Spinals">
  <data key="d0">Spinals</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Spinals are a type of regional anesthetic involving medication injection into the spinal canal for pain relief.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786383929</data>
</node>
<node id="Woman">
  <data key="d0">Woman</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Woman refers to the pregnant individual experiencing labor and making choices about pain relief.&lt;SEP&gt;A woman is an adult female patient who may develop delta hepatitis during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Woman refers to the female partner whose fertility status may affect conception.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed0aad3bf0cbd3eab10e7535f31d9a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412230</data>
</node>
<node id="Doctor">
  <data key="d0">Doctor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Doctor denotes the medical professional providing recommendations and overseeing childbirth care.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctor is a medical professional who diagnoses and treats anxiety, categorizing it as emotion or affect and selecting therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctors supervise the use of appetite suppressant drugs and monitor progress and side effects.&lt;SEP&gt;A doctor is the medical professional who examines patients for sources of hemoptysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctor is a medical professional who can diagnose conditions such as reactive hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;medical professional who examines patient’s penis for lumps or abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;A doctor is a healthcare professional who may diagnose postpartum depression through clinical interview.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff53a187c372ebdee1b2526a7ad3f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc06a5f841f69dff2bacc579104fc30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7292edceea122082967a38e119e48dbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c9e6467acd0c81d0621428aab938849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32995d0e87b6ef1faa098707755b406f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422995</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot; then entity_name">
  <data key="d0">" then entity_name</data>
