<node id="Reproductive System">
  <data key="d0">Reproductive System</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The reproductive system is a body system that comprises the organs responsible for sexual reproduction, including the gonads—testes in males and ovaries in females—which synthesize the sex hormones essential for development, secondary sexual characteristics, and reproductive function. It governs key processes such as ovulation, fertilization, pregnancy, and the maintenance of fertility.

In clinical and medical contexts, the reproductive system is repeatedly cited as a central anatomical and physiological domain. It is listed among the systems associated with Gleason Score entries, reflecting its relevance to prostate cancer assessment, and it is highlighted in relation to hysterectomy procedures, indicating its involvement when the uterus is surgically removed. Historically, the system has also been mentioned in discussions of hysteria symptoms, illustrating past psychosomatic considerations.

The reproductive system is implicated in a wide range of reproductive health issues. It is identified as a primary system involved in infertility and in conditions such as an incompetent cervix. Perinatal infections can affect the reproductive system, and it is noted as a system assessable by pelvic ultrasound. Specific disorders linked to the system include Peyronie's disease in males and Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) in females, the latter causing anovulation and contributing to infertility. Additionally, the reproductive system is mentioned in relation to prematurity, underscoring its role in early‑life developmental outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;The reproductive system is a body system listed as relevant to the prostate ultrasound.&lt;SEP&gt;The reproductive system is listed among body systems related to Provenge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2679367b0beba9113c18be86c1ebf3c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a9a426a4bb2afd30f9a958bbb935d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-142d840737a92f2ba527c40fc2edcbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-870bb1b70305260567e1654eccb86793&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-011a30caa3696a5321ec2b965fba6473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c63f65bb800d3d7fae8a0864fc3cdf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5223cef84c6fa99549cfa09e03c4ddcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6407dc79c35579b5387abf2b05a97d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d5f82c915dbc402d1fdeb23f98439f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed0aad3bf0cbd3eab10e7535f31d9a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-627b1597e2ff9fd7f303859f27a292f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427a659d0ef51d2588b292e6329fb824&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cc9b041882b1ffceb3664e339701aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3519af09df48250c19cedc50f317f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d76104bef49b3189628a31424cb580f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b63fc7d102b55c2843666075d6ad7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c289af6c541d3d25ea977381740c2c8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786425689</data>
</node>
