</node>
<node id="Antibiotic-Associated Colitis">
  <data key="d0">Antibiotic-Associated Colitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibiotic-associated colitis is a moderate disease marked by inflammation of the intestines that can occur after antibiotic treatment and is caused by toxins produced by Clostridium difficile.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5a65a1c3cf6b8503607afdabf8b0202</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786384605</data>
</node>
<node id="Clostridium Difficile">
  <data key="d0">Clostridium Difficile</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Clostridium difficile is a bacterium that produces toxins responsible for antibiotic-associated colitis and is normally present in the intestines of a small percentage of healthy adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5a65a1c3cf6b8503607afdabf8b0202</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786384605</data>
</node>
<node id="Antibiotic Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Antibiotic Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibiotic treatment refers to the medical use of antibiotics, which can precede the development of antibiotic-associated colitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5a65a1c3cf6b8503607afdabf8b0202</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786384605</data>
</node>
<node id="Bacterial Toxin Laboratory Test">
  <data key="d0">Bacterial Toxin Laboratory Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The bacterial toxin laboratory test detects Clostridium difficile toxin in stool samples and is the preferred diagnostic test for antibiotic-associated colitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5a65a1c3cf6b8503607afdabf8b0202</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786384605</data>
</node>
<node id="Diarrhea">
  <data key="d0">Diarrhea</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diarrhea is a symptom that commonly appears in patients with antibiotic-associated colitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Diarrhea is a somatic symptom of anxiety characterized by frequent loose stools.&lt;SEP&gt;Diarrhea is a common gastrointestinal side effect associated with protease inhibitor therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Diarrhea is a symptom that can accompany certain rashes, especially when associated with systemic reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5a65a1c3cf6b8503607afdabf8b0202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a175dfbbb5bdb8e9c075eb55543a5a41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27addf854956380fbaa2c0b20a96027b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426862</data>
</node>
<node id="Intestines">
  <data key="d0">Intestines</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The intestines are the part of the gastrointestinal tract where Clostridium difficile normally resides and where inflammation occurs in antibiotic-associated colitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Intestines are organs involved in digestion and nutrient absorption, affected by Hartnup disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Intestines are part of the digestive system through which alcohol travels before reaching the liver.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fe1b59b257b5d344c7de5181dbff9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a65a1c3cf6b8503607afdabf8b0202</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405085</data>
</node>
<node id="Nursing Home">
  <data key="d0">Nursing Home</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Nursing home is a residential care facility where individuals can acquire Clostridium difficile bacteria, contributing to antibiotic-associated colitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Nursing homes are residential facilities for older people who should remain in bed until stool cultures are negative.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-434d8d551fe8baa35b0eb7738c2dec25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a65a1c3cf6b8503607afdabf8b0202</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404894</data>
</node>
<node id="General Health">
  <data key="d0">General Health</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">General health refers to overall well-being that can reduce the risk of bacterial infections and the severity of antibiotic-associated colitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5a65a1c3cf6b8503607afdabf8b0202</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786384606</data>
