<node id="Angiogenesis">
  <data key="d0">Angiogenesis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Angiogenesis is the biological process of forming new blood vessels, which antiangiogenic therapy seeks to inhibit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-43384133dfe3fd1b2a03d01d15878f94</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786384652</data>
</node>
<node id="Chemotherapy">
  <data key="d0">Chemotherapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chemotherapy is a cancer treatment modality listed among the key terms related to antiangiogenic therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a medical treatment referenced as a key term associated with the use of antiemetics.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a medical treatment for cancer that can suppress the immune system, raising risk of aspergillosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a medical treatment used to cure approximately 90% of Hodgkin’s lymphoma cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88b3e0c879cd2c524008f697f6859f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43384133dfe3fd1b2a03d01d15878f94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8189651eadb45a933adca499117c49ad</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786408733</data>
</node>
