<node id="Swelling">
  <data key="d0">Swelling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Swelling is a symptom that can occur when bacteria multiply in untreated wounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Swelling is a post‑operative risk associated with craniotomy that is managed with drugs.&lt;SEP&gt;Complication involving abnormal swelling of the puncture site.&lt;SEP&gt;Swelling is a symptom of preeclampsia characterized by fluid accumulation in tissues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3cdce04fe6b7fc2f2383ff5401c7803f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5922b682f2c38e37dd9bd7f8f614180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691c137b75421e29ad257ff721c4b853</data>
