<node id="Faverin">
  <data key="d0">Faverin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Faverin is a brand-name formulation of fluvoxamine." Then cut off. So missing many entities: "Paroxetine Hydrochloride", its brand names Paxil, Seroxat, Aropax, Deroxat, Rextin, Xetanor, Paroxat. Also "Fluoxetine" (though incomplete). Also disorders: "Generalized Anxiety Disorder", "Obsessive‑Compulsive Disorder (OCD)", "Panic Disorder", "Social Anxiety Disorder", "Premenstrual Dysphoric Disorder (PMDD)", "Post‑Traumatic Stress Disorder (PTSD)". Also "Antidepressant drugs" maybe as a class. Also "Body Systems: neurological; psychiatric". Also "Severity Level: Severe". Also "Entry Type: Drug/Medication". Also "Icd Category: Various". Also "Purpose: ...". Also "Entry: Antidepressant drugs, SSRI". Also "Method: selective serotonin reuptake inhibition". But we need to decide which are entities. The system types list includes "Concept, Method, Content, Data, Artifact, NaturalObject". So "Antidepressant drugs" could be "artifact" or "concept"? Probably "artifact" as drug class. "Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor" is a method? Actually it's a mechanism, could be "method". But we already have SSRI as artifact. The "Method" could be "Selective serotonin reuptake inhibition". Also "reabsorption" maybe not needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-043b5eeeac66113551273095596cd117</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786385036</data>
</node>
