<node id="Radiation Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Radiation Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Radiation therapy is a treatment method that can be combined with anticancer drug therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation Therapy is a treatment method that destroys cancerous cells in head and neck cancer patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation therapy is a treatment modality that, together with chemotherapy, cures most Hodgkin’s lymphoma patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation therapy for head or neck cancer can cause hypothyroidism.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation therapy is a medical method that can cause nondeliberate immunosuppression as a side effect.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14488136ba3c8174aecc9163f5e16196&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c54bf8feacba012d420dc1bafe3e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b29429d857edf1192105634eda51b928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88b3e0c879cd2c524008f697f6859f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1385133e299def4ed989633bdbd7168</data>
