<node id="Tuberculosis">
  <data key="d0">Tuberculosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tuberculosis is an infectious disease affecting the lungs and other organs, caused by Mycobacterium tuberculae.&lt;SEP&gt;Tuberculosis is a bacterial disease referenced for comparison with the skin test used for Histoplasmosis diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Tuberculosis is an infectious disease that can be a secondary cause of hyperhidrosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Tuberculosis is a bacterial infection that has been reported to transmit via ear piercing.&lt;SEP&gt;Tuberculosis is a specific infectious disease of the lungs that may cause pleural effusion as a secondary effect.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-448825a5baf21347c5a8fd84c362669b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3323f3fda2ab71ab254c2a21d7d535a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ed665cb566f37b833eec31484ae9ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8db2289714a65b14031455c87d3fc259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a09c28fcfc5857e1357740e308a5a0d</data>
