  <data key="d2">Abdominal aortic aneurysm repair requires extensive postoperative care in an intensive care unit.&lt;SEP&gt;The intensive care unit is a specialized hospital department where patients receive continuous cardiac monitoring after surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;Intensive Care Unit is a specialized hospital area where post‑surgical patients are closely monitored for 24–72 hours after Heart Transplantation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Intensive Care Unit (ICU) is a hospital unit where patients typically stay one to three days after heart valve replacement for monitoring.</data>
