<node id="Anxiety">
  <data key="d0">Anxiety</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anxiety is a multisystem response to a perceived threat, involving biochemical changes, personal history, memory, and social situation, and can be experienced as a feeling without constituting a disorder.&lt;SEP&gt;Anxiety is a pre‑operative emotional state that patients are given medication to ease before a craniotomy.&lt;SEP&gt;A psychological condition that can contribute to the occurrence of heart murmurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Anxiety is a possible symptom experienced by individuals with hypertension.&lt;SEP&gt;Anxiety is a symptom that may be relieved by medications prescribed in supportive treatment for hypochondriasis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-684465558da6f22c66a6b34b82cea78c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b4f1384d965014ddcabd93b7495e501&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3167aac9bbeb660fe5ef8b641759df31</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410603</data>
</node>
<node id="Anxiety Disorder">
  <data key="d0">Anxiety Disorder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anxiety disorder is a psychiatric diagnosis distinct from the ordinary feeling of anxiety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388041</data>
</node>
<node id="Fear">
  <data key="d0">Fear</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fear is a direct, focused response to a specific event or object, consciously recognized by a person.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388041</data>
</node>
<node id="Anxious Affect">
  <data key="d0">Anxious Affect</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anxious affect describes the external observable nervous or anxious behavior of a patient as perceived by an observer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388041</data>
</node>
<node id="Somatic Symptoms">
  <data key="d0">Somatic Symptoms</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Somatic symptoms are physical manifestations of anxiety such as headaches, dizziness, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, tingling, pale complexion, sweating, numbness, difficulty breathing, chest tightness, and neck tightness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388041</data>
</node>
<node id="Tingling">
  <data key="d0">Tingling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tingling is a somatic symptom of anxiety describing abnormal prickling sensations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388042</data>
</node>
<node id="Pale Complexion">
  <data key="d0">Pale Complexion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pale complexion is a somatic symptom of anxiety indicating reduced blood flow to the skin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388042</data>
</node>
<node id="Sweating">
  <data key="d0">Sweating</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sweating is a somatic symptom of anxiety involving excess perspiration.&lt;SEP&gt;Sweating is a symptom that may appear after PTHC.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c5e751c6db20a49f7ca0a341eadc654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be</data>
