  <data key="d5">1786388043</data>
</node>
<node id="Emotion">
  <data key="d0">Emotion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Emotion refers to the internal biochemical changes and feeling state that underlie a person's sense of anxiety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388043</data>
</node>
<node id="Affect">
  <data key="d0">Affect</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Affect is the external emotional state as perceived by an observer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aecb82b4c17b2ce7e9445ff42d2200be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388043</data>
</node>
<node id="Artery">
  <data key="d0">Artery</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">An artery is a blood vessel that carries oxygen-rich blood away from the heart; the aorta is identified as an artery in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Arteriovenous Malformation consists of tangled arteries as part of its structure.&lt;SEP&gt;An artery is a blood vessel that may be accessed for specific blood tests during phlebotomy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d89439564ae2dc33beae4237976b40b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc1f798899ffec9a01bfa1aa437f649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45f05d7c26e4d3fdd9cc182e8964493</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420560</data>
</node>
<node id="Aorta">
  <data key="d0">Aorta</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2178c16160f72fcce4eafd8e4952fe8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc1f798899ffec9a01bfa1aa437f649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83aebc72b8b7f7141e25e88c35f39530</data>
  <data key="d2">The aorta is described as an artery because it carries oxygen-rich blood to the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The aorta is the main arterial vessel that carries blood away from the heart.&lt;SEP&gt;A major blood vessel that carries oxygenated blood from the heart to the systemic circulation, connected to the ductus arteriosus during fetal development."&lt;SEP&gt;The aorta is the main artery that carries oxygenated blood from the heart to the body and connects to the ductus arteriosus in fetal circulation.</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419023</data>
</node>
<node id="Aneurysm">
  <data key="d0">Aneurysm</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf2a4a7521a933797a5c97cd08b21a3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc1f798899ffec9a01bfa1aa437f649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c</data>
  <data key="d2">The aneurysm entry lists the cardiovascular system as one of the body systems involved.&lt;SEP&gt;Aneurysm is a vascular condition listed as a key term related to hemoptysis.&lt;SEP&gt;An aneurysm is a vascular condition that can be a cause of acquired ptosis.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786425872</data>
</node>
<node id="Apgar Testing">
  <data key="d0">Apgar Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Apgar Testing is an assessment of the newborn that rates color, heart rate, stimulus response, muscle tone, and respirations on a zero-to-two scale for each, yielding a maximum score of 10 and is performed at one minute and five minutes after birth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af3262684a537f83a047b77ed5ae0b70</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388396</data>
</node>
<node id="Virginia Apgar">
  <data key="d0">Virginia Apgar</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Virginia Apgar was an early‑20th‑century physician, one of the first women to graduate from a medical school in York, who shifted from surgery to anesthesiology and created the Apgar Testing method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af3262684a537f83a047b77ed5ae0b70</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388396</data>
</node>
<node id="Aortic Valve">
  <data key="d0">Aortic Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The aortic valve is a heart valve whose position is referenced in a medical entry concerning disease/condition classification.&lt;SEP&gt;The aortic valve is a heart valve that normally closes to prevent blood from flowing back into the left ventricle.&lt;SEP&gt;The Aortic Valve is one of the four heart valves that direct blood flow and may malfunction, requiring replacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83aebc72b8b7f7141e25e88c35f39530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67802df86489f08c4cf899e4cdd599e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af3262684a537f83a047b77ed5ae0b70</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404586</data>
</node>
<node id="Color">
  <data key="d0">Color</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Color is one of the five Apgar test categories, assessing the newborn’s skin coloration for signs of pallor or normal perfusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af3262684a537f83a047b77ed5ae0b70</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388396</data>
</node>
<node id="Heart Rate">
  <data key="d0">Heart Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Heart Rate is an Apgar test category that evaluates the newborn’s pulse frequency&lt;SEP&gt;Heart rate is the number of heartbeats per minute, referenced as a function of the heart's electrical system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-566c344db40177f660ee8acadd6a0e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af3262684a537f83a047b77ed5ae0b70</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404235</data>
</node>
<node id="York">
  <data key="d0">York</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af3262684a537f83a047b77ed5ae0b70</data>
  <data key="d2">Virginia Apgar graduated from a medical school in York.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388397</data>
</node>
<node id="Stimulus Response">
  <data key="d0">Stimulus Response</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af3262684a537f83a047b77ed5ae0b70</data>
  <data key="d2">Stimulus Response is a scoring category in Apgar Testing.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388398</data>
</node>
<node id="Medical School">
  <data key="d0">Medical School</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af3262684a537f83a047b77ed5ae0b70</data>
  <data key="d2">Virginia Apgar attended a medical school that was among the first to graduate women.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786388399</data>
</node>
