</node>
<node id="Appetite Suppressant Drugs">
  <data key="d0">Appetite Suppressant Drugs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Appetite suppressant drugs are medications that decrease desire for food, leading to reduced calorie consumption and weight loss, intended for use under doctor supervision with regular exercise and a healthy diet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff53a187c372ebdee1b2526a7ad3f69</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389545</data>
</node>
<node id="Weight Loss">
  <data key="d0">Weight Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Weight loss is the reduction in body weight achieved when dieters consume fewer calories due to appetite suppressant drugs.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight loss is a symptom reported in women with a hydatidiform mole.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight loss is a symptom of starvation that can occur in hyperemesis gravidarum.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight Loss is a therapeutic approach mentioned for treating Pickwickian Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03146cdc1f2091b67696466e08fc65db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff53a187c372ebdee1b2526a7ad3f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8db2289714a65b14031455c87d3fc259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420900</data>
</node>
<node id="Calorie Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Calorie Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Calorie consumption refers to the intake of calories from food, which is reduced by appetite suppressant drugs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff53a187c372ebdee1b2526a7ad3f69</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389545</data>
</node>
<node id="Regular Exercise">
  <data key="d0">Regular Exercise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Regular exercise is recommended for dieters using appetite suppressant drugs to support health and weight loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff53a187c372ebdee1b2526a7ad3f69</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389546</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Pressure Elevation">
  <data key="d0">Blood Pressure Elevation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood pressure elevation is a possible side effect of appetite suppressant drugs, indicating increased blood pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff53a187c372ebdee1b2526a7ad3f69</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389546</data>
</node>
<node id="Desire for Food">
  <data key="d0">Desire for Food</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Desire for food is the feeling of wanting to eat, which is reduced by appetite suppressant drugs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff53a187c372ebdee1b2526a7ad3f69</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389546</data>
</node>
<node id="Stroke">
  <data key="d0">Stroke</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Stroke is a key term linked to appetite suppressant drugs, representing a possible severe cardiovascular complication.&lt;SEP&gt;Stroke is a cerebrovascular event linked to high homocysteine concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Stroke is a medical event that can lead to the diagnosis of hypercholesterolemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fff53a187c372ebdee1b2526a7ad3f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cd4e9159e066f72729a8b0e6c804cc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3046439ce6fa1d6d5f63b57269a3f9b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409959</data>
</node>
<node id="Aston-Patterning">
  <data key="d0">Aston-Patterning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Aston-Patterning is an integrated system of movement education, bodywork, ergonomic adjustments, and fitness training that links body and mind to improve well‑being and reduce acute or chronic pain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa850befaee3ce9863ec83a8dbb56b00</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389628</data>
</node>
<node id="Aston">
  <data key="d0">Aston</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Aston is the individual who introduced the three‑dimensional spinal pattern concept and created the Aston-Patterning method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa850befaee3ce9863ec83a8dbb56b00</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389628</data>
</node>
<node id="Rolfing">
  <data key="d0">Rolfing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rolfing is a movement therapy that strives for linear symmetry, contrasted with Aston-Patterning’s focus on asymmetry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa850befaee3ce9863ec83a8dbb56b00</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389628</data>
</node>
<node id="Rolf">
  <data key="d0">Rolf</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Rolf is the individual associated with the development of the Rolfing method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa850befaee3ce9863ec83a8dbb56b00</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389628</data>
</node>
<node id="Three-Dimensional Spinal Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Three-Dimensional Spinal Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A conceptual framework introduced by Aston that describes working with spinal alignment in three dimensions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa850befaee3ce9863ec83a8dbb56b00</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389628</data>
</node>
<node id="Asymmetry">
  <data key="d0">Asymmetry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The condition of non‑symmetrical structure or movement that Aston-Patterning embraces rather than correcting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa850befaee3ce9863ec83a8dbb56b00</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389628</data>
</node>
<node id="Linear Symmetry">
  <data key="d0">Linear Symmetry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A principle of perfect symmetry that Rolfing aims to achieve, contrasted with Aston-Patterning’s focus on asymmetry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa850befaee3ce9863ec83a8dbb56b00</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389629</data>
</node>
<node id="Movement Education">
  <data key="d0">Movement Education</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the four components of Aston-Patterning, involving teaching individuals optimal movement patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa850befaee3ce9863ec83a8dbb56b00</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389629</data>
</node>
<node id="Bodywork">
  <data key="d0">Bodywork</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A therapeutic component of Aston-Patterning that involves hands‑on manipulation to improve body function.&lt;SEP&gt;Bodywork is a therapeutic technique involving manipulation of the body, included as a component of polarity therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa850befaee3ce9863ec83a8dbb56b00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca4ee33fbe169b1bec7c819c96b35eb6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422315</data>
</node>
<node id="Ergonomic Adjustments">
  <data key="d0">Ergonomic Adjustments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A component of Aston-Patterning that modifies everyday setups to reduce strain and improve posture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa850befaee3ce9863ec83a8dbb56b00</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389629</data>
</node>
<node id="Bronchial Walls">
  <data key="d0">Bronchial Walls</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Bronchial walls are the tissue surrounding the bronchi that contain mast cells involved in asthma inflammation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa5b9c93d92f286edbd8518809c07cae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389771</data>
</node>
<node id="Airway Inflammation">
  <data key="d0">Airway Inflammation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Airway inflammation is the immune-mediated swelling and irritation of the bronchial passages that occurs during asthma attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa5b9c93d92f286edbd8518809c07cae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389771</data>
</node>
<node id="Bronchoconstriction">
  <data key="d0">Bronchoconstriction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bronchoconstriction is the narrowing of the airways caused by contraction of the bronchial smooth muscle in asthma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa5b9c93d92f286edbd8518809c07cae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389771</data>
</node>
<node id="Allergic Sensitization">
  <data key="d0">Allergic Sensitization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Allergic sensitization describes the state of hypersensitivity to specific inhaled allergens that predisposes individuals to asthma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa5b9c93d92f286edbd8518809c07cae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389771</data>
</node>
<node id="Supplemental Oxygen">
  <data key="d0">Supplemental Oxygen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplemental oxygen is a medical device that delivers extra oxygen to patients during severe asthma attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Supplemental Oxygen – Artifact – oxygen supplied to patients to raise blood oxygen levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa5b9c93d92f286edbd8518809c07cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf9568ffc5d5bfc55e145a95f45cf030</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412089</data>
</node>
<node id="Mechanical Ventilation">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Ventilation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mechanical ventilation is a medical procedure that assists or replaces spontaneous breathing in critical severe asthma attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Mechanical Ventilation – Method – equipment-based respiratory support that may require weaning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa5b9c93d92f286edbd8518809c07cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf9568ffc5d5bfc55e145a95f45cf030</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412090</data>
</node>
<node id="Smooth Muscle Tissue">
  <data key="d0">Smooth Muscle Tissue</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Smooth muscle tissue lines the airway walls and contracts during bronchoconstriction in asthma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa5b9c93d92f286edbd8518809c07cae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389772</data>
</node>
<node id="Asthma">
  <data key="d0">Asthma</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa5b9c93d92f286edbd8518809c07cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b66d2f56572161b690b85278b6a11f68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dcd996730cbdde5a41d3f86b16d8074</data>
  <data key="d2">Asthma triggers inflammation of the airway lining, leading to swelling and irritation.&lt;SEP&gt;Asthma is a respiratory condition listed as a symptom of Gulf War Syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;Asthma is a lung disease that can be diagnosed with pulmonary function tests and peak flow meters.</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786425953</data>
</node>
<node id="Allergens">
  <data key="d0">Allergens</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa5b9c93d92f286edbd8518809c07cae</data>
  <data key="d2">Inhalation of allergens can lead to allergic sensitization, increasing susceptibility to asthma.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389772</data>
</node>
<node id="Severe Asthma Attack">
  <data key="d0">Severe Asthma Attack</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa5b9c93d92f286edbd8518809c07cae</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplemental oxygen is administered to patients during severe asthma attacks to improve oxygenation.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389772</data>
</node>
<node id="Ataxia-Telangiectasia">
  <data key="d0">Ataxia-Telangiectasia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ataxia-telangiectasia (A‑T), also called Louis‑Bar syndrome, is a rare genetic neurological disorder of childhood that progressively destroys part of the brain’s motor control area, causing loss of balance, coordination, immune deficiencies, and increased risk of leukemia and lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;..." No extra hyphens, proper case for type (lowercase? The examples used lower-case for type: example "person". So type should be lower-case. Also entity_name should be title case. Should not include hyphens in entity name; it's "Ataxia-Telangiectasia". Good.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389781</data>
</node>
<node id="Louis-Bar Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Louis-Bar Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Louis‑Bar syndrome is an alternate name for Ataxia‑telangiectasia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389781</data>
</node>
<node id="ATM Gene">
  <data key="d0">ATM Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The ATM gene is an autosomal recessive gene whose defective copies inherited from both parents cause Ataxia‑telangiectasia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389781</data>
</node>
<node id="Purkinje Cells">
  <data key="d0">Purkinje Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Purkinje cells are large branching neurons in the cerebellum whose death underlies the ataxia observed in Ataxia‑telangiectasia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389781</data>
</node>
<node id="Cerebellum">
  <data key="d0">Cerebellum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The cerebellum is the brain region that contains Purkinje cells and coordinates motor control, and it is damaged in Ataxia‑telangiectasia.&lt;SEP&gt;Cerebellum is the part of the brain involved in coordination of movement, walking, and balance, and is affected by Progressive Supranuclear Palsy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2408b24dbbf82011285a46aaece84afd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786424338</data>
</node>
<node id="Leukemia">
  <data key="d0">Leukemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Leukemia is a blood cancer whose incidence is increased in people with Ataxia‑telangiectasia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389781</data>
</node>
<node id="Lymphoma">
  <data key="d0">Lymphoma</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lymphoma is a blood cancer whose incidence is increased in people with Ataxia‑telangiectasia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389781</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Cancer">
  <data key="d0">Blood Cancer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood cancer refers to malignancies such as leukemia and lymphoma that are more common in Ataxia‑telangiectasia patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389781</data>
</node>
<node id="Radiation Sensitivity">
  <data key="d0">Radiation Sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Radiation sensitivity denotes the extreme sensitivity to ionising radiation observed in individuals with Ataxia‑telangiectasia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389781</data>
</node>
<node id="Gamma Globulin">
  <data key="d0">Gamma Globulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gamma globulin is a preparation of human blood antibodies injected to strengthen the weakened immune system in Ataxia‑telangiectasia treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Gamma Globulin is an immune chemical derived from donated blood used in the treatment of graft-versus-host disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-07cc217c989e2af1a805d2ee5017b0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786401941</data>
</node>
<node id="High-Dose Vitamin Administration">
  <data key="d0">High-Dose Vitamin Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">High‑dose vitamin administration is a therapeutic approach sometimes prescribed for patients with Ataxia‑telangiectasia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389781</data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Physical Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical therapy is a rehabilitation method used to help individuals with Ataxia‑telangiectasia manage ataxia and improve motor function.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical therapy is a treatment modality designed to meet the specific needs of persons with Parkinson’s disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical therapy is a rehabilitative method applied to improve motor function in children with Patau Syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical therapy is described as an essential component of successful treatment, relying on physiological understanding to avoid risks such as pain, falls, bruising, or injury.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical therapy is a treatment method used to restore muscle strength in paralytic Polio patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2887ebc17d5fa167b3627fd14696de82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a43117074cce1d59c31131832dfa007&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8411522bdeb607aaa222e6502bca7dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422232</data>
</node>
<node id="Speech Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Speech Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Speech therapy is a rehabilitation method used to address speech difficulties in individuals with Ataxia‑telangiectasia.&lt;SEP&gt;Speech therapy is a therapeutic approach used to address communication challenges in patients with Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419191</data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Researchers">
  <data key="d0">Medical Researchers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical researchers are investigators studying screening, prevention, and treatment strategies for Ataxia‑telangiectasia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389782</data>
</node>
<node id="Carrier Screening">
  <data key="d0">Carrier Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Carrier screening is a genetic test aimed at identifying individuals who carry defective copies of the ATM gene.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389782</data>
</node>
<node id="Telangiectasia">
  <data key="d0">Telangiectasia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Telangiect&lt;SEP&gt;Term referring to spot formed by dilated capillary or artery, appears as small red spots on skin, mouth, nose, etc.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2668ae388ce75891b60c313b7cab62b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb8410ab80dc1278656666cc6ce9a2b7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405557</data>
</node>
<node id="Asbestosis">
  <data key="d0">Asbestosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Asbestosis is a chronic, progressive inflammation of the lung caused by prolonged inhalation of asbestos fibers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389850</data>
</node>
<node id="Asbestos">
  <data key="d0">Asbestos</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Asbestos is a mineral fiber historically used in construction, insulation, and manufacturing, whose inhalation can cause lung disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Asbestos is a fibrous material whose exposure is associated with an increased risk of developing laryngeal cancer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c54bf8feacba012d420dc1bafe3e309</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403384</data>
</node>
<node id="Automobile Brake Shoe Linings">
  <data key="d0">Automobile Brake Shoe Linings</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Automobile brake shoe linings are products that may contain asbestos and expose workers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389850</data>
</node>
<node id="Boiler Insulation">
  <data key="d0">Boiler Insulation</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Boiler insulation is a product that may contain asbestos and expose workers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389850</data>
</node>
<node id="Ceiling Acoustic Tiles">
  <data key="d0">Ceiling Acoustic Tiles</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ceiling acoustic tiles are products that may contain asbestos and expose workers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389850</data>
</node>
<node id="Electrical Equipment">
  <data key="d0">Electrical Equipment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Electrical equipment is a product that may contain asbestos and expose workers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389850</data>
</node>
<node id="Fire-Resistant Materials">
  <data key="d0">Fire-Resistant Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fire-resistant materials are products that may contain asbestos and expose workers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389850</data>
</node>
<node id="Workers">
  <data key="d0">Workers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Workers are individuals who may be exposed to asbestos in occupational settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389850</data>
</node>
<node id="Occupational Exposure">
  <data key="d0">Occupational Exposure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Occupational exposure is the most common cause of asbestosis, involving inhalation of asbestos fibers at work.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389850</data>
</node>
<node id="Family Members">
  <data key="d0">Family Members</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Family members can develop asbestosis through secondary exposure to asbestos dust on workers' clothing.&lt;SEP&gt;Family Members are the relatives of patients who often provide Home Care services.&lt;SEP&gt;Family members of an individual with hyperlipoproteinemia are advised to have their blood lipids assessed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08f81c821ddcf514260191db4522a7a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ac7fad90c3ef5bbb1366ea8a473928</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409944</data>
</node>
<node id="Waste Products from Plants">
  <data key="d0">Waste Products from Plants</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Waste products from plants near homes can contain asbestos fibers, posing a risk of exposure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389851</data>
</node>
<node id="Lung">
  <data key="d0">Lung</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The lung is the organ affected by asbestosis, where inflammation and scarring occur.&lt;SEP&gt;The lung is the organ that becomes infected during pneumonia.&lt;SEP&gt;The lung is a vital organ involved in respiration, targeted for removal in pneumonectomy procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47a3a83e48113d48f0a14a70afb7ebf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f81367bc23721681b080e8e55f88ab71</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422129</data>
</node>
<node id="X Rays">
  <data key="d0">X Rays</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">X rays are imaging tests used to detect shadows or spots on lungs indicative of asbestosis.&lt;SEP&gt;X rays are a diagnostic imaging method that can help confirm the bony deformity of hammertoe.&lt;SEP&gt;X rays are imaging tools that may reveal characteristic joint damage in psoriatic arthritis patients.&lt;SEP&gt;X rays are imaging tests used in diagnosing the cause of ptosis.&lt;SEP&gt;X Rays are an indirect visualization technique used in screening to view the lining of the colon and rectum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf2a4a7521a933797a5c97cd08b21a3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd702733210b77bd85a84e3b0046cb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ccba52c964c301daf559927d7d7c5e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426768</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Tests">
  <data key="d0">Blood Tests</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood tests measure oxygen and carbon dioxide concentrations in patients with asbestosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood tests are laboratory analyses used to rule out clotting disorders and detect food particles or gastrointestinal blood.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood tests can be part of the diagnostic work‑up for intractable hiccups.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood tests are laboratory analyses used to identify underlying conditions causing ptosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood tests are diagnostic procedures used to help rule out other causes after rabies symptom onset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-04a89a85dc3be8d37412b0c61ebf99cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf2a4a7521a933797a5c97cd08b21a3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9098e6c377264351e34498ab20d1d2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426202</data>
</node>
<node id="Pulmonary Function Tests">
  <data key="d0">Pulmonary Function Tests</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pulmonary function tests assess lung capacity and function in asbestosis patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Pulmonary function tests are clinical assessments that can reveal decreased lung function associated with aspergillosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Pulmonary Function Tests – Method – tests performed to verify treatment success or monitor adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Pulmonary function tests are a group of procedures that measure the function of the lungs, revealing problems in breathing and helping diagnose lung diseases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dcd996730cbdde5a41d3f86b16d8074&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf9568ffc5d5bfc55e145a95f45cf030</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786425953</data>
</node>
<node id="Ultrasonic Cool-Mist Humidifiers">
  <data key="d0">Ultrasonic Cool-Mist Humidifiers</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultrasonic cool-mist humidifiers help loosen bronchial secretions in asbestosis treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389851</data>
</node>
<node id="Protective Mask">
  <data key="d0">Protective Mask</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Protective masks are recommended for workers handling asbestos to prevent inhalation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389851</data>
</node>
<node id="Legislation">
  <data key="d0">Legislation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Legislation has reduced asbestos use in the United States.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389852</data>
</node>
<node id="Asbestos Fibers">
  <data key="d0">Asbestos Fibers</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Asbestos fibers are microscopic particles inhaled that cause lung tissue irritation and scarring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389852</data>
</node>
<node id="Asbestos Dust">
  <data key="d0">Asbestos Dust</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Asbestos dust consists of fine particles that can cling to clothing and cause secondary exposure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389852</data>
</node>
<node id="Asbestos-Related Industries">
  <data key="d0">Asbestos-Related Industries</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Asbestos-related industries include sectors where workers handle asbestos-containing materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d5f8eb7b45a1ef3316ab36b4d963198</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786389852</data>
</node>
<node id="Mucus">
  <data key="d0">Mucus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Mucus is a thin, slippery film secreted by mucous membranes and glands, which can form plugs that obstruct airways and cause atelectasis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390006</data>
</node>
<node id="Chest">
  <data key="d0">Chest</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The chest is the part of the body overlying the lungs, examined by percussion and auscultation when diagnosing atelectasis.&lt;SEP&gt;The chest is examined for bleeding and trauma in patients with hemoptysis.&lt;SEP&gt;The upper portion of the body that contains the thoracic cavity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bcaad1542ea8e041fd9f427e13e25c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405603</data>
</node>
<node id="Airways">
  <data key="d0">Airways</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Airways are the passages that conduct air to the lungs and can become obstructed, leading to atelectasis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390006</data>
</node>
<node id="Atelectasis">
  <data key="d0">Atelectasis</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d2">A computed tomography (CT) scan of the chest visualizes collapsed lung tissue to diagnose atelectasis.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390007</data>
</node>
<node id="Computed Tomography Scan">
  <data key="d0">Computed Tomography Scan</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-448825a5baf21347c5a8fd84c362669b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-414a580eb00a7d0d58696314c2aa7dfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d855036a34135250bf6b6942f08845d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d2">A computed tomography (CT) scan of the chest visualizes collapsed lung tissue to diagnose atelectasis.&lt;SEP&gt;Computed tomography (CT) scan is an imaging method that can detect even small amounts of ascitic fluid.&lt;SEP&gt;Computed tomography (CT) scan is an imaging study used to assess the presence and location of obstructions in hydrocephalus.&lt;SEP&gt;Computed tomography (CT) scan is an imaging modality employed to diagnose intestinal obstruction.&lt;SEP&gt;Computed Tomography Scan is an advanced imaging method that provides detailed cross‑sectional images of the chest and is helpful for evaluating pleural effusion when lung disease is present.&lt;SEP&gt;Computed Tomography Scan is an imaging method that can highlight cyst‑damaged areas of kidneys in Polycystic Kidney Disease.</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422502</data>
</node>
<node id="Stethoscope">
  <data key="d0">Stethoscope</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3167aac9bbeb660fe5ef8b641759df31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b4f1384d965014ddcabd93b7495e501</data>
  <data key="d2">A stethoscope is used to listen to lung sounds, helping identify atelectasis.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical instrument used by physicians to listen to heart sounds, including murmurs.&lt;SEP&gt;A stethoscope is placed over the artery during cuff deflation to listen for the sounds of blood returning, aiding in blood‑pressure assessment.</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410340</data>
</node>
<node id="Percussion">
  <data key="d0">Percussion</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d2">Percussion of the chest is performed to assess for signs of atelectasis.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390010</data>
</node>
<node id="Coughing">
  <data key="d0">Coughing</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d2">Coughing helps remove airway blockages that cause atelectasis.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390011</data>
</node>
<node id="Suctioning">
  <data key="d0">Suctioning</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d2">Suctioning removes mucus or other material from the airways to treat atelectasis.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390012</data>
</node>
<node id="Bronchoscopy">
  <data key="d0">Bronchoscopy</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f57760db433207b2438ded5229d83be6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c</data>
  <data key="d2">Bronchoscopy is performed to remove airway obstructions causing atelectasis.&lt;SEP&gt;Bronchoscopy is an endoscopic procedure used to directly visualize the airways in hemoptysis cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Bronchoscopy is a medical procedure that obtains lung samples for microscopic identification of Pneumocystis carinii.</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786421792</data>
</node>
<node id="Postural Drainage">
  <data key="d0">Postural Drainage</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d2">Postural drainage helps clear airway secretions in patients with atelectasis.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390016</data>
</node>
<node id="Repositioning">
  <data key="d0">Repositioning</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d2">Frequent repositioning in bed helps prevent atelectasis after surgery.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390018</data>
</node>
<node id="Deep Breathing">
  <data key="d0">Deep Breathing</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af3b4b939a2aeb8a2dffe85570c09b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d2">Deep breathing is recommended to prevent atelectasis postoperatively.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep Breathing is a technique taught in cognitive-behavioral therapy to lessen anxiety associated with phobias.</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420675</data>
</node>
<node id="Breathing Exercises">
  <data key="d0">Breathing Exercises</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d2">Breathing exercises are performed regularly to prevent atelectasis.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390020</data>
</node>
<node id="Breathing Devices">
  <data key="d0">Breathing Devices</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3061512333f2d3b557a0b433544fa7</data>
  <data key="d2">Breathing devices are used to assist deep breathing and help prevent atelectasis.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390022</data>
</node>
<node id="Aspergillosis">
  <data key="d0">Aspergillosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Aspergillosis is a severe disease caused by the fungus Aspergillus, affecting respiratory, neurological, immunological, and infectious systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Aspergillosis is a fungal infection listed as a key term related to hemoptysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404945</data>
</node>
<node id="Aspergillus">
  <data key="d0">Aspergillus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Aspergillus is a genus of fungus that produces airborne spores capable of causing aspergillosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390042</data>
</node>
<node id="Aspergilloma">
  <data key="d0">Aspergilloma</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Aspergilloma is a specific form or manifestation of aspergillosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390042</data>
</node>
<node id="Allergic Bronchopulmonary Aspergillosis">
  <data key="d0">Allergic Bronchopulmonary Aspergillosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis (ABPA) is a subtype of aspergillosis associated with asthma and allergic reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390042</data>
</node>
<node id="Bronchial Asthma">
  <data key="d0">Bronchial Asthma</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bronchial asthma is a respiratory condition that can be worsened by allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390042</data>
</node>
<node id="HIV">
  <data key="d0">HIV</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HIV is a virus that compromises the immune system, increasing susceptibility to aspergillosis.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV is listed as a key term associated with the discussion of immune‑related conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV is a systemic infection identified as a risk factor for developing infectious arthritis.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV is a viral infection that, while theoretically transmissible by piercing and tattooing, has no documented cases from professional artists.&lt;SEP&gt;Human immunodeficiency virus is a virus whose infection weakens the immune system, increasing susceptibility to Pneumocystis pneumonia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7a69ca28e7676455bc1dd105b09f56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f57760db433207b2438ded5229d83be6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8db2289714a65b14031455c87d3fc259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88b3e0c879cd2c524008f697f6859f7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786421792</data>
</node>
<node id="Antifungal Drugs">
  <data key="d0">Antifungal Drugs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Antifungal drugs are medications intended to treat fungal infections but are not reliably effective against Aspergillus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390042</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Cultures">
  <data key="d0">Blood Cultures</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood cultures are laboratory tests used to detect fungal presence in the bloodstream for diagnosing aspergillosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390043</data>
</node>
<node id="Sputum Cultures">
  <data key="d0">Sputum Cultures</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sputum cultures are laboratory tests used to detect fungal organisms in respiratory secretions for diagnosing aspergillosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390043</data>
</node>
<node id="Centers For Disease Control And Prevention">
  <data key="d0">Centers For Disease Control And Prevention</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention is a public health agency that provides information and guidance on aspergillosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390043</data>
</node>
<node id="MedlinePlus">
  <data key="d0">MedlinePlus</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">MedlinePlus is an online health information resource that offers details about aspergillosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390043</data>
</node>
<node id="National Institute Of Child Health And Human Development">
  <data key="d0">National Institute Of Child Health And Human Development</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Institute of Child Health and Human Development is a research institute referenced for related health topics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390043</data>
</node>
<node id="Asperweb">
  <data key="d0">Asperweb</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Asperweb is a website that provides information and resources concerning aspergillosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390044</data>
</node>
<node id="Ear Canal">
  <data key="d0">Ear Canal</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The ear canal is a body location where aspergillus spores can lodge and cause infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390044</data>
</node>
<node id="Eyes">
  <data key="d0">Eyes</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The eyes are a body location where aspergillus spores can lodge and cause infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390044</data>
</node>
<node id="Nose">
  <data key="d0">Nose</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The nose is a body location where aspergillus spores can lodge and cause infection.&lt;SEP&gt;The nose is examined by doctors for bleeding that could indicate the source of hemoptysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404943</data>
</node>
<node id="Sinus Cavities">
  <data key="d0">Sinus Cavities</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The sinus cavities are body locations where aspergillus spores can lodge and cause infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390044</data>
</node>
<node id="Immunocompromised">
  <data key="d0">Immunocompromised</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Immunocompromised describes individuals with weakened immune systems who are at higher risk for aspergillosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390044</data>
</node>
<node id="Spores">
  <data key="d0">Spores</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Spores are airborne reproductive particles produced by Aspergillus that can be inhaled and cause infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Spores are microscopic reproductive units of Histoplasma capsulatum that are inhaled and cause infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3323f3fda2ab71ab254c2a21d7d535a1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786408341</data>
</node>
<node id="Meningitis">
  <data key="d0">Meningitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Meningitis is an inflammation of the membranes covering the brain and spinal cord that can arise as a complication of aspergillosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Meningitis is an inflammation of the membranes surrounding the brain and spinal cord that can be caused by H. influenzae infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Meningitis is an infection of the central nervous system that can cause hydrocephalus.&lt;SEP&gt;Meningitis is a severe infectious disease that can be life‑threatening according to the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Inflammation of the membranes covering the brain and spinal cord, listed as a key term related to pneumococcal disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ebc91deb19a2b42710150361b08958e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8d23aad485a31e434afa128d656202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-414a580eb00a7d0d58696314c2aa7dfe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786421957</data>
</node>
<node id="Hemoptysis">
  <data key="d0">Hemoptysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemoptysis is coughing up blood, a possible symptom of pulmonary aspergillosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoptysis is the coughing up of blood or bloody sputum from the lungs or airway, which may be self‑limiting or recurrent and can range from small amounts to life‑threatening volumes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404943</data>
</node>
<node id="Bronchial Lavage">
  <data key="d0">Bronchial Lavage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bronchial lavage is a medical procedure used to collect samples for diagnosing aspergillosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-976f1e53f9085499934de45456b8e026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390045</data>
</node>
<node id="Ascites">
  <data key="d0">Ascites</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ascites is an abnormal accumulation of fluid in the abdomen, described as a disease/condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Ascites is a medical condition listed as a key term related to biliary and liver disorders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c5e751c6db20a49f7ca0a341eadc654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419484</data>
</node>
<node id="Chylous Ascites">
  <data key="d0">Chylous Ascites</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Chylous Ascites is a form of ascites with a milky appearance caused by lymph leaking into the abdominal cavity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390194</data>
</node>
<node id="Chronic Liver Disease">
  <data key="d0">Chronic Liver Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Chronic liver disease is a long-lasting condition of the liver that is frequently associated with ascites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390194</data>
</node>
<node id="Portal Hypertension">
  <data key="d0">Portal Hypertension</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Portal hypertension is increased pressure in the portal vein branches caused by cirrhosis and leads to fluid leakage into the abdomen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390194</data>
</node>
<node id="Low Albumin">
  <data key="d0">Low Albumin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low albumin refers to reduced blood albumin levels that lower osmotic pressure and promote fluid accumulation in ascites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390194</data>
</node>
<node id="Osmotic Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Osmotic Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Osmotic pressure is the pressure needed to prevent fluid exchange across membranes, affected by albumin levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390194</data>
</node>
<node id="Peritoneum">
  <data key="d0">Peritoneum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Peritoneum is the smooth, transparent membrane lining the inside of the abdominal cavity.&lt;SEP&gt;Peritoneum is the membrane lining the abdominal cavity, mentioned as a key term related to hernia repair.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e12a604aa907a1e42740edfcfafe2583</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405644</data>
</node>
<node id="Perforated Ulcer">
  <data key="d0">Perforated Ulcer</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Perforated ulcer is a gastrointestinal condition that can cause acute ascites as a complication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390195</data>
</node>
<node id="Appendicitis">
  <data key="d0">Appendicitis</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Appendicitis is inflammation of the appendix that can lead to acute ascites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390195</data>
</node>
<node id="Diverticulitis">
  <data key="d0">Diverticulitis</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Diverticulitis is inflammation of diverticula in the colon that can result in acute ascites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390195</data>
</node>
<node id="Dandelion (Taraxacum Officinale)">
  <data key="d0">Dandelion (Taraxacum Officinale)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Dandelion (Taraxacum officinale) is an herbal plant used as a diuretic to help eliminate excess fluid in ascites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390195</data>
</node>
<node id="Paracentesis">
  <data key="d0">Paracentesis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Paracentesis is a medical procedure used to sample or remove ascitic fluid from the abdomen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390196</data>
</node>
<node id="Interferon">
  <data key="d0">Interferon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Interferon is a therapeutic agent listed as a key term related to ascites.&lt;SEP&gt;Interferon is an injectable drug used in the treatment of hepatitis B.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edba73be60673b1668775ee43b5d8dd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405095</data>
</node>
<node id="Portal Vein">
  <data key="d0">Portal Vein</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Portal vein is the blood vessel whose branches experience increased pressure in portal hypertension.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390196</data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatic Juices">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Juices</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic juices are digestive secretions that can invade the peritoneum and contribute to ascites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390196</data>
</node>
<node id="Lymph">
  <data key="d0">Lymph</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lymph is the fluid of the lymphatic system that, when leaked into the abdominal cavity, causes chylous ascites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390196</data>
</node>
<node id="Abdominal Cavity">
  <data key="d0">Abdominal Cavity</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Abdominal cavity is the space within the abdomen that can fill with fluid in ascites.&lt;SEP&gt;The cavity below the diaphragm that houses abdominal organs.&lt;SEP&gt;The abdominal cavity is a body space that commonly serves as the drainage site for a hydrocephalus shunt.&lt;SEP&gt;Abdominal Cavity is the space within the abdomen where ascitic fluid accumulates and from which Paracentesis removes fluid.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-414a580eb00a7d0d58696314c2aa7dfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bcaad1542ea8e041fd9f427e13e25c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-405f3438c94303b670da4ac7ad2e23a8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786418410</data>
</node>
<node id="Azotemia">
  <data key="d0">Azotemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Azotemia is an abnormally high blood level of nitrogen-bearing materials noted as a monitoring concern during diuretic treatment for ascites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390197</data>
</node>
<node id="Hypovolemia">
  <data key="d0">Hypovolemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypovolemia is massive loss of blood or fluid flagged as a potential side effect of diuretic therapy for ascites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390197</data>
</node>
<node id="Potassium Imbalance">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Imbalance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium imbalance is a possible electrolyte disturbance monitored during diuretic treatment for ascites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390197</data>
</node>
<node id="High Sodium Concentration">
  <data key="d0">High Sodium Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High sodium concentration is a condition noted when patients consume more salt than kidneys excrete, affecting ascites management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05c379dcf013630337bc48911a2ab86</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390197</data>
</node>
<node id="Asperger Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Asperger Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Asperger syndrome (AS), also called Asperger disorder or autistic psychopathy, is a childhood disorder belonging to pervasive developmental disorders and autistic spectrum disorders, characterized by problems with social interaction, nonverbal communication difficulties, peculiar speech habits, lack of common sense, intense interests, clumsy movements, and eccentric behaviors.&lt;SEP&gt;Asperger syndrome is characterized by difficulties in social relationships and communication, lack of eye contact, reduced response to social cues, normal language and cognition, clumsy motor coordination, and intense focus on few interests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e02da87d46351e723d1298ee7642793&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08cfa0cda6c4260819924908fa77810e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420019</data>
</node>
<node id="Arthroscopy">
  <data key="d0">Arthroscopy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Arthroscopy is a surgical method that examines the interior of a joint by inserting an illuminated instrument through a small incision, primarily for diagnosis and occasionally for repair.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390372</data>
</node>
<node id="Arthroscope">
  <data key="d0">Arthroscope</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Arthroscope is an illuminated surgical instrument inserted through a small incision to view inside a joint during arthroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390372</data>
</node>
<node id="Joint">
  <data key="d0">Joint</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Joint is a body structure whose interior is examined and treated during arthroscopy.&lt;SEP&gt;A joint is a bodily structure where infectious arthritis can occur, leading to pain and impaired function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7a69ca28e7676455bc1dd105b09f56c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786411979</data>
</node>
<node id="Camera">
  <data key="d0">Camera</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Camera attached to the arthroscope captures images of the joint for the surgeon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390372</data>
</node>
<node id="Monitor">
  <data key="d0">Monitor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitor displays the live video feed from the arthroscope camera in the operating room.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390372</data>
</node>
<node id="Video Technology">
  <data key="d0">Video Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Video technology records the arthroscopic procedure for documentation and review.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390372</data>
</node>
<node id="Cannula">
  <data key="d0">Cannula</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cannula is a tube through which solution may be delivered during arthroscopy, with outflow optionally through the arthroscope.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390372</data>
</node>
<node id="Portal">
  <data key="d0">Portal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Portal is an entry point created in the joint capsule to insert the arthroscope for visualization.&lt;SEP&gt;Portal is a term listed among key terms in General surgery (context unclear).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9b86e7fa3cdc49102c86215baa6da67</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400878</data>
</node>
<node id="Hemarthrosis">
  <data key="d0">Hemarthrosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemarthrosis is bleeding into a joint and listed as a potential complication of arthroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786390373</data>
</node>
<node id="Pulmonary Embolus">
  <data key="d0">Pulmonary Embolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pulmonary embolus is a blood clot that can travel to the lungs and is noted as a possible arthroscopy complication.&lt;SEP&gt;Pulmonary embolus is a blockage of a pulmonary artery by a blood clot.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edfaa9dba99a768f9ffcf5c77b2d0525&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cafce0045c17d2c21616a392f69f22</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786424793</data>
</node>
<node id="Craniotomy">
  <data key="d0">Craniotomy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Craniotomy is a surgical method involving removal of part of the skull to expose the brain and is the most commonly performed surgery for brain tumor removal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396259</data>
</node>
<node id="Z‑Codes">
  <data key="d0">Z‑Codes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Z‑Codes are the ICD classification category referenced for the craniotomy entry.&lt;SEP&gt;Z‑codes are a classification category referenced for cosmetic surgery entries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5972068248f50904396788f92782210f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786421540</data>
</node>
<node id="Brain Tumor">
  <data key="d0">Brain Tumor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Brain Tumor is the medical condition for which craniotomy is most commonly performed.&lt;SEP&gt;Brain tumor is referenced as a condition related to glioma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-627b1597e2ff9fd7f303859f27a292f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786401216</data>
</node>
<node id="Codeine">
  <data key="d0">Codeine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Codeine is an opioid medication that may be given after craniotomy to relieve headache caused by scalp nerve irritation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396260</data>
</node>
<node id="Drainage">
  <data key="d0">Drainage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Drainage refers to the removal of excess fluid from the head after a craniotomy, typically using a surgical drain.&lt;SEP&gt;Drainage refers to". Need to complete description.&lt;SEP&gt;Drainage is a therapeutic method used to remove infected fluid from a joint in infectious arthritis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7a69ca28e7676455bc1dd105b09f56c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786411980</data>
</node>
<node id="Seizures">
  <data key="d0">Seizures</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Seizures are a possible post‑operative complication of craniotomy, controlled with medication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396261</data>
</node>
<node id="Infection">
  <data key="d0">Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infection is a potential post‑operative complication of craniotomy, prevented with prophylactic drugs.&lt;SEP&gt;Infection is listed as one of the possible conditions that can cause degeneration leading to parkinsonism.&lt;SEP&gt;Complication involving signs such as redness and swelling at the puncture site.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d5922b682f2c38e37dd9bd7f8f614180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2887ebc17d5fa167b3627fd14696de82</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419726</data>
</node>
<node id="Scalp Nerves">
  <data key="d0">Scalp Nerves</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Scalp Nerves are the nerves in the scalp that can be irritated during craniotomy, causing headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396261</data>
</node>
<node id="Craniotome">
  <data key="d0">Craniotome</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Craniotome is a surgical instrument used to cut bone during a craniotomy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396261</data>
</node>
<node id="Atherosclerosis">
  <data key="d0">Atherosclerosis</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Atherosclerosis is a disease listed as a key term associated with the craniotomy entry.&lt;SEP&gt;Condition related to hardening of the arteries, referenced in complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Atherosclerosis is the buildup of plaque in artery walls that can narrow and block blood flow.&lt;SEP&gt;Atherosclerosis is a vascular disease whose risk is increased by dyslipidemia and hyperlipoproteinemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6dcc52e74701dc594a5093895fbb8763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-895c5e07d9ff1dcdf835a5d197d6cf8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edba93ae4e0e61889c3b13cfe47b1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ac7fad90c3ef5bbb1366ea8a473928</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409943</data>
</node>
<node id="Cryotherapy">
  <data key="d0">Cryotherapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cryotherapy is a technique that uses an extremely cold liquid or instrument to freeze and destroy abnormal skin cells, widely available to dermatologists and primary care doctors, and also called cryosurgery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb3f69c0e24f7808954b601ab37de0ac</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396401</data>
</node>
<node id="Cryosurgery">
  <data key="d0">Cryosurgery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cryosurgery is an alternative name for the cryotherapy technique that freezes and destroys abnormal skin cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb3f69c0e24f7808954b601ab37de0ac</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396401</data>
</node>
<node id="Liquid Nitrogen">
  <data key="d0">Liquid Nitrogen</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Liquid nitrogen is a cryogen, the coldest cryogen available at –320 °F (–196 °C), used in cryotherapy to freeze skin growths.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb3f69c0e24f7808954b601ab37de0ac</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396401</data>
</node>
<node id="Cotton Swab">
  <data key="d0">Cotton Swab</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A cotton swab is an applicator dipped into liquid nitrogen and applied directly to skin growths during cryotherapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb3f69c0e24f7808954b601ab37de0ac</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396401</data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Cell Cancer">
  <data key="d0">Basal Cell Cancer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal cell cancer is a type of skin cancer that can be destroyed by cryotherapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb3f69c0e24f7808954b601ab37de0ac</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396401</data>
</node>
<node id="Primary Care Doctors">
  <data key="d0">Primary Care Doctors</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Primary care doctors are medical professionals who can also use cryotherapy for skin conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb3f69c0e24f7808954b601ab37de0ac</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396402</data>
</node>
<node id="Cryogen">
  <data key="d0">Cryogen</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cryogen is a term referring to substances like liquid nitrogen used in cryotherapy to freeze tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb3f69c0e24f7808954b601ab37de0ac</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396402</data>
</node>
<node id="Cutaneous T-Cell Lymphoma">
  <data key="d0">Cutaneous T-Cell Lymphoma</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cutaneous T-Cell Lymphoma (CTCL) is a malignancy of CD4+ T‑helper cells that primarily affects the skin and can secondarily involve other body sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396553</data>
</node>
<node id="Mycosis Fungoides">
  <data key="d0">Mycosis Fungoides</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mycosis Fungoides is an alternative name for Cutaneous T-Cell Lymphoma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396553</data>
</node>
<node id="T-Helper Cells">
  <data key="d0">T-Helper Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">T‑Helper Cells are CD4+ T‑lymphocytes that coordinate immune responses and are the malignant cell type in CTCL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396553</data>
</node>
<node id="T-Lymphocytes">
  <data key="d0">T-Lymphocytes</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">T‑Lymphocytes are a class of white blood cells that include CD4+ T‑helper cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396553</data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Severity Level">
  <data key="d0">Critical Severity Level</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical Severity Level describes the high seriousness assigned to CTCL.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification indicating the highest level of seriousness for a disease or condition, identified for pneumonia.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical severity level denotes the most serious classification of protein-energy malnutrition as indicated in the entry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ebc91deb19a2b42710150361b08958e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afbff98c4c1d63870e1df4480f9167fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786424860</data>
</node>
<node id="ICD Category C00-D49">
  <data key="d0">ICD Category C00-D49</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">ICD Category C00-D49 is the International Classification of Diseases code range covering CTCL.&lt;SEP&gt;ICD Category C00-D49 is the coding range under which Hodgkin’s lymphoma is classified.&lt;SEP&gt;ICD Category C00-D49 is the classification range that includes endocrine pancreatic cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;ICD classification code for cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;ICD Category C00-D49 is the classification code range that includes rectal cancer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad7165a537192620d6a93befeffa64e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c9e6467acd0c81d0621428aab938849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ccba52c964c301daf559927d7d7c5e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88b3e0c879cd2c524008f697f6859f7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426767</data>
</node>
<node id="International Consensus Conference on CTCL">
  <data key="d0">International Consensus Conference on CTCL</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The International Consensus Conference on CTCL in 1997 presented the current staging system for the disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396554</data>
</node>
<node id="Stage IA">
  <data key="d0">Stage IA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stage IA is an early stage of CTCL associated with very good prognosis and mean survival of 20+ years.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396554</data>
</node>
<node id="1997">
  <data key="d0">1997</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">1997 is the year when the International Consensus Conference on CTCL presented the disease staging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db342ca6f9a76a46729e0e30b5cde75c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786396554</data>
</node>
