  <data key="d5">1786400473</data>
</node>
<node id="Human Papillomavirus">
  <data key="d0">Human Papillomavirus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Human papillomavirus is a virus that produces papillomas and includes multiple types that cause genital warts.&lt;SEP&gt;Human Papillomavirus (HPV) is a virus that infects humans and some animals, comprising about 130 known strains, some of which are sexually transmitted and can cause warts and various cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;..." etc? Actually earlier answer hasn't been shown fully. The assistant gave final answer partial and then was cut. The content we have shows the assistant prepared some but not all.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3e49cac7d8a89a06ea2ab78d39b9e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3c3c73e1fc719b81a2fc054715a4c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409037</data>
</node>
<node id="Papillomas">
  <data key="d0">Papillomas</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Papillomas are benign growths on the skin and mucous membranes produced by papillomavirus infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3e49cac7d8a89a06ea2ab78d39b9e33</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400473</data>
</node>
<node id="HPV Types 1, 2, 6, 11, 16, and 18">
  <data key="d0">HPV Types 1, 2, 6, 11, 16, and 18</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">These specific HPV types are responsible for causing genital warts and are transmitted by sexual contact.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3e49cac7d8a89a06ea2ab78d39b9e33</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400473</data>
</node>
<node id="PCR Testing">
  <data key="d0">PCR Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PCR testing is a molecular method that detects the presence of HPV in individuals, indicating prevalence rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3e49cac7d8a89a06ea2ab78d39b9e33</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400473</data>
</node>
<node id="Women">
  <data key="d0">Women</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Women infected with certain HPV types are at increased risk of cervical cancer and require screening.&lt;SEP&gt;Women are a gender group in which hypochondriasis is reported to be equally common.&lt;SEP&gt;Women are the population affected by pelvic relaxation and are advised on preventive measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Women are a gender group noted for higher response to certain antidepressants due to lower serotonin levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Women, particularly childbearing women, are the primary population impacted by postpartum depression.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-684465558da6f22c66a6b34b82cea78c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9102756028539b9228bf8362c3e96772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3e49cac7d8a89a06ea2ab78d39b9e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32995d0e87b6ef1faa098707755b406f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8fe6834775c118dee9d1addc0b895c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422994</data>
</node>
<node id="Cervical Cancer">
  <data key="d0">Cervical Cancer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cervical cancer is a potential later disease associated with repeated HPV infection in women.&lt;SEP&gt;Cervical Cancer is a malignant tumor of the cervix linked to infection with high‑risk Human Papillomavirus strains.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer developing in the cervix, which the Pap test is designed to detect at an early stage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3e49cac7d8a89a06ea2ab78d39b9e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d126a4f2dfaa975afdfed278c2386bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3c3c73e1fc719b81a2fc054715a4c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786416503</data>
</node>
<node id="Cervical Smears">
  <data key="d0">Cervical Smears</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cervical smears are a screening method performed yearly for women infected with HPV types 16 and 18.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3e49cac7d8a89a06ea2ab78d39b9e33</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400473</data>
</node>
<node id="Incubation Period">
  <data key="d0">Incubation Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The incubation period for HPV infection varies from one to six months.&lt;SEP&gt;The incubation period for hepatitis E is two to eight weeks between infection and symptom onset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3e49cac7d8a89a06ea2ab78d39b9e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b14c26a47ca283ef7a5696f26a6c99c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405172</data>
</node>
<node id="Symptoms of Genital Warts">
  <data key="d0">Symptoms of Genital Warts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Symptoms of genital warts include bleeding, pain, odor, and visible warts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3e49cac7d8a89a06ea2ab78d39b9e33</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400473</data>
</node>
<node id="Condoms">
  <data key="d0">Condoms</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Condoms are protective artifacts that minimize but do not eliminate the risk of HPV transmission.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3e49cac7d8a89a06ea2ab78d39b9e33</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400473</data>
</node>
<node id="Sexual Abstinence">
  <data key="d0">Sexual Abstinence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sexual abstinence is a reliable prevention method that eliminates the risk of acquiring genital warts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3e49cac7d8a89a06ea2ab78d39b9e33</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400473</data>
