<node id="Gastritis">
  <data key="d0">Gastritis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gastritis is an inflammation of the stomach lining, encompassing various symptoms such as burning or discomfort and includes several forms diagnosed by tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b7c972c3cf8fccfda43764fbd8415a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400576</data>
</node>
<node id="Helicobacter pylori">
  <data key="d0">Helicobacter pylori</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Helicobacter pylori is a bacterium identified as the primary cause of true gastritis, causing infections that lead to various gastric conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b7c972c3cf8fccfda43764fbd8415a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400576</data>
</node>
<node id="Nonerosive H. pylori Gastritis">
  <data key="d0">Nonerosive H. pylori Gastritis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nonerosive H. pylori gastritis is a form of gastritis caused by infection with Helicobacter pylori.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b7c972c3cf8fccfda43764fbd8415a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400576</data>
</node>
<node id="Chronic Superficial Gastritis">
  <data key="d0">Chronic Superficial Gastritis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chronic superficial gastritis is a type of gastritis frequently associated with infection by Helicobacter pylori.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b7c972c3cf8fccfda43764fbd8415a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400576</data>
</node>
<node id="Peptic Ulcers">
  <data key="d0">Peptic Ulcers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Peptic ulcers are lesions in the stomach lining that may be linked to Helicobacter pylori infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b7c972c3cf8fccfda43764fbd8415a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400576</data>
</node>
<node id="Scientists">
  <data key="d0">Scientists</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Scientists are researchers who identified the role of Helicobacter pylori in causing gastritis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b7c972c3cf8fccfda43764fbd8415a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400576</data>
</node>
<node id="1990s">
  <data key="d0">1990s</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The 1990s is the decade during which scientists discovered Helicobacter pylori as the main cause of true gastritis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3b7c972c3cf8fccfda43764fbd8415a3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400576</data>
</node>
<node id="Herpes Virus">
  <data key="d0">Herpes Virus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Herpes virus is the pathogen responsible for genital herpes that can enter cells, hide in neurons, and reactivate to cause active infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400647</data>
</node>
<node id="Latency">
  <data key="d0">Latency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Latency is the period during which a latent virus resides silently inside neurons for days, months, or years.&lt;SEP&gt;Latency is defined...</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afe775e3de6a2ede3813b294c2d7085</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786421099</data>
</node>
<node id="Latent Virus">
  <data key="d0">Latent Virus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Latent virus refers to the dormant herpes virus that persists in neurons until reactivation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400647</data>
</node>
<node id="Active Infection">
  <data key="d0">Active Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active infection is the phase when the reactivated virus forces cells to produce new viruses, leading to symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400647</data>
</node>
<node id="Difficult Urination">
  <data key="d0">Difficult Urination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Difficult urination is a clinical symptom that can occur during recurrent genital herpes infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400647</data>
</node>
<node id="Lymphadenopathy">
  <data key="d0">Lymphadenopathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lymphadenopathy is swelling of lymph nodes that may develop in men and women with genital herpes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400648</data>
</node>
<node id="Nurse Practitioner">
  <data key="d0">Nurse Practitioner</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nurse practitioner is a healthcare provider who can diagnose and treat genital herpes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400648</data>
</node>
<node id="Urologists">
  <data key="d0">Urologists</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Urologists are doctors specializing in urinary tract and male genital diseases who can diagnose and treat genital herpes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400648</data>
</node>
<node id="Gynecologists">
  <data key="d0">Gynecologists</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gynecologists are doctors specializing in female genital diseases who can diagnose and treat genital herpes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400648</data>
</node>
<node id="Infectious Disease Specialists">
  <data key="d0">Infectious Disease Specialists</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infectious disease specialists are physicians who can diagnose and treat genital herpes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400648</data>
</node>
<node id="Prodrome Stage">
  <data key="d0">Prodrome Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prodrome stage is the early phase of a herpes outbreak before blisters become visible, during which drug treatment is most effective.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400648</data>
</node>
<node id="Primary Infection">
  <data key="d0">Primary Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Primary infection is the initial severe episode of genital herpes that can lead to complications and may require hospitalization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400648</data>
</node>
<node id="Urinary System">
  <data key="d0">Urinary System</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Urinary system comprises organs involved in urine production and excretion, which may be compromised during severe genital herpes infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400648</data>
</node>
<node id="Anal Opening">
  <data key="d0">Anal Opening</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Anal opening is the exterior part of the digestive tract that can be involved in complications of primary genital herpes infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786400648</data>
</node>
<node id="Nervous System">
  <data key="d0">Nervous System</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nervous system includes neurons where the herpes virus can reside latently and reactivate.&lt;SEP&gt;Body system that can be involved in severe cases of pneumococcal pneumonia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8ebc91deb19a2b42710150361b08958e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786421955</data>
</node>
<node id="Symptoms">
  <data key="d0">Symptoms</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Symptoms are clinical signs such as lesions and pain that arise during an active herpes infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Symptoms are clinical manifestations that may be absent or mild in early Hepatitis C infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Symptoms are clinical manifestations such as nausea, vomiting, headache, anorexia, jaundice, clay‑colored stools, dark urine, and hepatomegily.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-784ba38e8bfe9ffbf875f5ee96725a4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c</data>
