<node id="Gestational Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Gestational Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gestational diabetes is an abnormal increase in blood sugar levels that occurs during pregnancy, appears first during pregnancy and disappears after birth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786401051</data>
</node>
<node id="Pregnancy Hormones">
  <data key="d0">Pregnancy Hormones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pregnancy hormones increase in late pregnancy and limit glucose entry into cells, contributing to gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786401051</data>
</node>
<node id="Placenta">
  <data key="d0">Placenta</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The placenta is an organ attached to the uterine wall that produces hormones affecting glucose metabolism and transfers excess glucose to the fetus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786401051</data>
</node>
<node id="Maternal Pancreas">
  <data key="d0">Maternal Pancreas</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The mother's pancreas produces insulin to counteract rising blood glucose levels during gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786401051</data>
</node>
<node id="Fetal Pancreas">
  <data key="d0">Fetal Pancreas</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The baby's pancreas responds to excess glucose by producing additional insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786401051</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin is a hormone that enables cells to take in glucose and is produced by the pancreas.&lt;SEP&gt;hormone that lowers blood glucose, regulating glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;A hormone used in the insulin tolerance test to stimulate growth hormone secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is a hormone whose absorption is slowed by Hyperbaric Oxygen Therapy, requiring glucose and insulin balance adjustment.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is a hormone secreted by the pancreas that regulates the level of glucose in the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4bfe90135432788559f3dd95da898ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e04fc4d9139221a4e00a150baf448e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9afb199a3e40198055fdd9a325ecd1aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25a42943ad0f93e6631565dc2c851d36</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412241</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose is the concentration of glucose in the blood, elevated in gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786401051</data>
</node>
<node id="Dietary Management">
  <data key="d0">Dietary Management</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dietary management involves strict, detailed diets with controlled calorie intake to lower blood glucose in gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f65898fb0918e956817b050a5bb5580</data>
