<node id="Physical Examination">
  <data key="d0">Physical Examination</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c54bf8feacba012d420dc1bafe3e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ee6af5422b0bedd83a764af83874c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c10fb15c165fb1c6b20b0aa8847da7ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adcf683ab3aafdf4309bc219710636d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7a69ca28e7676455bc1dd105b09f56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-910d4bcf6932bd29fd1d161e11852b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e534c2f61dae08dd6e4ae98c00c82c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a882c73a80d91bc942b5ef3432982d9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5f246a7b970683961e9b1aba02b38a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b63fc7d102b55c2843666075d6ad7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical Examination is a clinical assessment procedure employed across a wide range of medical specialties to gather objective signs that aid in diagnosis and management. In rheumatology and musculoskeletal medicine, inspection and palpation of an affected joint are integral to identifying infectious arthritis, while in metabolic and systemic disorders the same hands‑on approach helps detect gout by revealing characteristic joint swelling, tenderness, and tophi. Cardiovascular evaluation relies on physical examination to uncover signs of heart failure—such as peripheral edema, jugular venous distension, and abnormal heart sounds—and to recognize structural abnormalities like hypertrophic cardiomyopathy through murmurs, systolic ejection clicks, and dynamic outflow obstruction.

In obstetrics, a focused physical examination contributes to the diagnosis of hyperemesis gravidarum by assessing dehydration, weight loss, and electrolyte imbalance. Psychiatric assessment may incorporate a physical examination to rule out organic contributors and to observe behavioral cues relevant to conditions such as paranoia. Otolaryngology and oncology use a targeted inspection of the oral and nasal cavities, often with a mirror, as a standard step in screening for head and neck cancers, allowing clinicians to detect mucosal lesions, asymmetry, or abnormal masses. Urology includes a specific physical examination of the genitalia to identify penile curvature and palpable plaques, findings characteristic of Peyronie’s disease.

Across these diverse applications, physical examination remains a foundational, non‑invasive diagnostic tool that complements laboratory testing and imaging, providing immediate, bedside information essential for forming differential diagnoses and guiding further investigative or therapeutic steps.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical examination is a clinical assessment used to diagnose the allergic reaction based on symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical examination is a clinical assessment performed during diagnosis of priapism.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical examination of skin, nails, and scalp is used by dermatologists to diagnose psoriasis.</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786425489</data>
</node>
