<node id="Hammertoe">
  <data key="d0">Hammertoe</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hammertoe is a deformity where one or more toes bend downward into a claw-like position, most commonly the second toe, with joint enlargement, skin callus, and involvement of blood vessels and nerves.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403122</data>
</node>
<node id="American Psychological Association">
  <data key="d0">American Psychological Association</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">American Psychological Association is referenced via its website www.apa.org and contact phone number in the entry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403122</data>
</node>
<node id="Tendons">
  <data key="d0">Tendons</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tendons whose shortening causes hammertoe by reducing control and movement of the affected toe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403122</data>
</node>
<node id="Callus">
  <data key="d0">Callus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Callus formation on the top portions of toes results from friction against shoes and is associated with hammertoe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403122</data>
</node>
<node id="Improperly Fitted Footwear">
  <data key="d0">Improperly Fitted Footwear</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Footwear that does not fit properly is cited as a common cause of hammertoe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403122</data>
</node>
<node id="High-Heeled Shoes">
  <data key="d0">High-Heeled Shoes</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">High-heeled shoes place pressure on the front part of the foot, compressing smaller toes and contributing to hammertoe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403122</data>
</node>
<node id="Muscle Imbalance">
  <data key="d0">Muscle Imbalance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Muscle imbalance is mentioned as a frequent underlying factor leading to hammertoe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403122</data>
</node>
<node id="Proper Footwear">
  <data key="d0">Proper Footwear</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Proper footwear with ample toe room is recommended as a conservative treatment for hammertoe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403122</data>
</node>
<node id="Stockings">
  <data key="d0">Stockings</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Stockings with plenty of room in the toe region are suggested as part of conservative treatment for hammertoe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403122</data>
</node>
<node id="Stretching Exercises">
  <data key="d0">Stretching Exercises</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stretching exercises may help lengthen excessively tight tendons as a treatment for hammertoe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca82475bbfe64d98c513d42669176ff3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403122</data>
</node>
