<node id="Hartnup Disease">
  <data key="d0">Hartnup Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hartnup disease is a genetic metabolic disorder characterized by defective absorption of amino acids, leading to symptoms similar to pellagra and requiring niacin supplementation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403289</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Transfusion Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Blood Transfusion Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A blood transfusion reaction is an adverse response to transfused blood that can cause red cell destruction and reduced haptoglobin levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403289</data>
</node>
<node id="Mechanical Heart Valve">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Heart Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A mechanical heart valve is a prosthetic device that can cause red blood cell damage leading to decreased haptoglobin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403289</data>
</node>
<node id="Abnormally Shaped Red Cells">
  <data key="d0">Abnormally Shaped Red Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Abnormally shaped red cells are misshapen erythrocytes that can lead to reduced haptoglobin levels due to increased destruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403289</data>
</node>
<node id="Thalassemia">
  <data key="d0">Thalassemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thalassemia is a hereditary blood disorder involving abnormal hemoglobin production, contributing to red cell destruction and low haptoglobin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403289</data>
</node>
<node id="Sickle Cell Anemia">
  <data key="d0">Sickle Cell Anemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sickle cell anemia is a genetic disease causing misshapen red blood cells, leading to hemolysis and decreased haptoglobin.&lt;SEP&gt;Autosomal recessive hemoglobinopathy caused by a specific beta-globin mutation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19e4810245f812dff5d4b92e29c6f847&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405020</data>
</node>
<node id="Inherited Lack of Haptoglobin">
  <data key="d0">Inherited Lack of Haptoglobin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inherited lack of haptoglobin is a genetic condition causing persistently low haptoglobin levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403290</data>
</node>
<node id="Hartnup Family">
  <data key="d0">Hartnup Family</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The Hartnup family is the family in which Hartnup disease was first identified, located in London.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403290</data>
</node>
<node id="London">
  <data key="d0">London</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">London is the city in the United Kingdom where the Hartnup family resides.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403290</data>
</node>
<node id="Pellagra">
  <data key="d0">Pellagra</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pellagra is a disease caused by niacin deficiency, presenting symptoms similar to those of Hartnup disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403290</data>
</node>
<node id="Niacin Deficiency">
  <data key="d0">Niacin Deficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Niacin deficiency is a lack of vitamin B3 that leads to pellagra-like symptoms and is linked to Hartnup disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403290</data>
</node>
<node id="Niacin">
  <data key="d0">Niacin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Niacin is a B vitamin used to treat Hartnup disease and prevent pellagra-like symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403291</data>
</node>
<node id="Nicotinamide">
  <data key="d0">Nicotinamide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nicotinamide is a form of niacin administered as a treatment for Hartnup disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403291</data>
</node>
<node id="Tryptophan">
  <data key="d0">Tryptophan</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Tryptophan is an amino acid that may be supplemented in the diet of patients with Hartnup disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403291</data>
</node>
<node id="Aminoaciduria">
  <data key="d0">Aminoaciduria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Aminoaciduria is the presence of excess amino acids in the urine, used as a diagnostic marker for Hartnup disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403291</data>
</node>
<node id="Diet History">
  <data key="d0">Diet History</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A diet history is an assessment method to evaluate protein and vitamin intake for diagnosing Hartnup disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403291</data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Testing">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic testing identifies carriers of Hartnup disease genes for prevention and family counseling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403291</data>
</node>
<node id="High Protein Diet">
  <data key="d0">High Protein Diet</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A high protein diet is a nutritional approach used to control symptoms of Hartnup disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403291</data>
</node>
<node id="Vitamin Supplements">
  <data key="d0">Vitamin Supplements</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Vitamin supplements, such as niacin, are used to manage Hartnup disease symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403291</data>
</node>
<node id="National Organization for Rare Disorders">
  <data key="d0">National Organization for Rare Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Organization for Rare Disorders provides information and resources related to Hartnup disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786403291</data>
</node>
<node id="Hatha Yoga">
  <data key="d0">Hatha Yoga</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hatha yoga is mentioned as a cause, though its relevance to Hartnup disease is unclear.&lt;SEP&gt;Hatha Yoga is the most widely practiced form of yoga in the United States, focusing on physical health and mental wellbeing through postures, breathing, and meditation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2cac3b15cf6eb4edf007b3be55fb814e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a5fe7cfd2eb995bee47dc8e7a28fbbf</data>
