<node id="Heart Failure">
  <data key="d0">Heart Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Heart Failure is a medical condition characterized by the heart’s inability to pump sufficient blood, classified as a disease/disorder with moderate severity, affecting cardiovascular, musculoskeletal, and hematological systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A possible progression of hypertrophic cardiomyopathy.&lt;SEP&gt;Heart failure is a medical condition that can cause death in severe cases of protein-energy malnutrition.&lt;SEP&gt;Heart failure is a condition evaluated by pulmonary artery catheterization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-910d4bcf6932bd29fd1d161e11852b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afbff98c4c1d63870e1df4480f9167fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e534c2f61dae08dd6e4ae98c00c82c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b7e1ff6aefba50b9ab4cb48e8298cf0</data>
