</node>
<node id="Coronary Artery Disease">
  <data key="d0">Coronary Artery Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Coronary Artery Disease is a condition where coronary arteries narrow or become blocked, identified as the most common cause of heart failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Coronary artery disease (CAD) is the most common heart disease condition, occurring when blood vessels in the heart become blocked or narrowed.&lt;SEP&gt;Coronary Artery Disease is a heart condition mentioned among key terms that can be associated with patients considered for Heart Transplantation.&lt;SEP&gt;Coronary Artery Disease is a condition in</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-895c5e07d9ff1dcdf835a5d197d6cf8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f36c10fba48ed73bf1306763cd71ea5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-910d4bcf6932bd29fd1d161e11852b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99d14117824aa2b5637825772676446</data>
