<node id="Plaque">
  <data key="d0">Plaque</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Plaque is a fatty substance composed of cholesterol and other materials that accumulates on artery walls during atherosclerosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Plaque is a sticky bacterial film that forms on teeth and can harden into tartar if not removed.&lt;SEP&gt;Plaque is a hard lump of scar tissue that forms in the tunica albuginea and prevents stretching of the penis during erection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c98e85575a0fbf6c6f4d4ea25dc15ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b63fc7d102b55c2843666075d6ad7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-895c5e07d9ff1dcdf835a5d197d6cf8c</data>
