<node id="Hellerwork">
  <data key="d0">Hellerwork</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hellerwork is a system of bodywork that combines deep tissue massage, body movement education, and verbal dialogue to realign the body’s structure for health, posture improvement, and stress reduction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9357c3975c61fb3fb97582bf3597bed2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404324</data>
</node>
<node id="Deep Tissue Massage">
  <data key="d0">Deep Tissue Massage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deep Tissue Massage is a massage technique incorporated in Hellerwork, designed to release muscular tension.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9357c3975c61fb3fb97582bf3597bed2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404324</data>
</node>
<node id="Body Movement Education">
  <data key="d0">Body Movement Education</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Body Movement Education is an educational component of Hellerwork that teaches body movement to aid structural alignment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9357c3975c61fb3fb97582bf3597bed2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404324</data>
</node>
<node id="Verbal Dialogue">
  <data key="d0">Verbal Dialogue</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Verbal Dialogue is a conversational component of Hellerwork used to facilitate awareness and realignment of the body’s structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9357c3975c61fb3fb97582bf3597bed2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404324</data>
</node>
<node id="Posture">
  <data key="d0">Posture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Posture refers to the alignment of the body, which Hellerwork aims to improve.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9357c3975c61fb3fb97582bf3597bed2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404324</data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Stress">
  <data key="d0">Physical Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical stress denotes bodily tension that Hellerwork seeks to reduce.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9357c3975c61fb3fb97582bf3597bed2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404324</data>
</node>
<node id="Mental Stress">
  <data key="d0">Mental Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mental stress denotes psychological tension that Hellerwork seeks to reduce.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9357c3975c61fb3fb97582bf3597bed2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404324</data>
</node>
<node id="Overall Health">
  <data key="d0">Overall Health</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Overall health is the general state of physical and mental well‑being that Hellerwork aims to enhance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9357c3975c61fb3fb97582bf3597bed2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404324</data>
</node>
<node id="Heel Spurs">
  <data key="d0">Heel Spurs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Heel Spurs are a severe foot condition characterized by a bony projection on the sole (plantar) region of the calcaneus, often associated with pain and inflammation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Calcaneus">
  <data key="d0">Calcaneus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The calcaneus is the heel bone on which heel spurs form as bony projections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Plantar Fascia">
  <data key="d0">Plantar Fascia</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Plantar fascia is a fibrous band of connective tissue on the sole of the foot that extends from the heel to the toes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Plantar Fascitis">
  <data key="d0">Plantar Fascitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Plantar fascitis is the medical term for inflammation of the plantar fascia, which can lead to heel pain and spur formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Pronation">
  <data key="d0">Pronation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pronation is the normal inward motion of the foot with dropping of the inside arch during walking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Excessive Pronation">
  <data key="d0">Excessive Pronation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Excessive pronation is an extreme form of pronation where the foot turns inward and the arch drops beyond normal limits, creating mechanical stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Arch of the Foot">
  <data key="d0">Arch of the Foot</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The arch of the foot is the curved structure on the sole whose decrease is correlated with higher prevalence of heel spurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Calf Muscles">
  <data key="d0">Calf Muscles</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calf muscles are the muscles at the back of the lower leg that are stretched as part of conservative treatment for heel spurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Foot Orthotics">
  <data key="d0">Foot Orthotics</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Foot orthotics are specially designed shoe inserts recommended by healthcare professionals to support the foot and alleviate heel spur pain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Conservative Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Conservative Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Conservative Treatment refers to non‑surgical management of heel spurs and plantar fasciitis, including calf‑muscle stretching, activity modification, weight management, and footwear adjustments such as raised‑heel shoes and orthotics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Raised Heel Shoes">
  <data key="d0">Raised Heel Shoes</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Raised heel shoes are footwear designed with an elevated heel to reduce strain on the plantar fascia and alleviate heel spur pain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Weight Management">
  <data key="d0">Weight Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Weight management involves maintaining or reducing body weight to lessen stress on the foot structures and help prevent or treat heel spurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404420</data>
</node>
<node id="Calf Muscle Stretching">
  <data key="d0">Calf Muscle Stretching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Calf muscle stretching is a therapeutic exercise aimed at lengthening the calf muscles to reduce tension on the plantar fascia in heel‑spur treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404421</data>
</node>
<node id="Activity Modification">
  <data key="d0">Activity Modification</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Activity modification entails adjusting or reducing physical activities that aggravate heel pain, thereby aiding recovery from heel spurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404421</data>
</node>
<node id="Children Age 6-8 Years">
  <data key="d0">Children Age 6-8 Years</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Children Age 6-8 Years denotes the developmental stage when the foot arch is fully formed, after which heel spurs become more prevalent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4c57ef53ddb01cbbf235608d43c7612</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404421</data>
