<node id="Mitral Valve">
  <data key="d0">Mitral Valve</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Mitral Valve is one of the four heart valves that direct blood flow and may malfunction, requiring replacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67802df86489f08c4cf899e4cdd599e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404586</data>
</node>
<node id="Anticoagulants">
  <data key="d0">Anticoagulants</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anticoagulants are medications commonly used after heart valve replacement to prevent blood clots.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67802df86489f08c4cf899e4cdd599e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404586</data>
</node>
<node id="Echocardiography">
  <data key="d0">Echocardiography</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Echocardiography is an imaging method listed as a key term related to heart valve procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Echocardiography is an imaging technique used to assess heart enlargement or pulmonary hypertension in patients with complications from piercing and tattoos.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8db2289714a65b14031455c87d3fc259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67802df86489f08c4cf899e4cdd599e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420899</data>
</node>
<node id="Electrocardiography">
  <data key="d0">Electrocardiography</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Electrocardiography is an electrical monitoring method listed as a key term related to heart valve procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67802df86489f08c4cf899e4cdd599e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404586</data>
</node>
<node id="Heart Palpitations">
  <data key="d0">Heart Palpitations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Heart Palpitations are a symptom that can occur when a heart valve malfunction severely interferes with blood flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67802df86489f08c4cf899e4cdd599e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404587</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Flow">
  <data key="d0">Blood Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Flow refers to the circulation of blood through the heart and vessels, which can be disrupted by valve malfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Flow is the movement of blood through vessels, whose volume influences electrical impedance measured by the test.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood flow refers to the circulation of blood, which may be impaired in priapism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f69c2450b3e8a6ce90d873db565dfb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67802df86489f08c4cf899e4cdd599e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c10fb15c165fb1c6b20b0aa8847da7ef</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786423958</data>
</node>
<node id="Breastbone">
  <data key="d0">Breastbone</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Breastbone is a bone cut during heart valve replacement surgery to access the heart.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67802df86489f08c4cf899e4cdd599e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404587</data>
</node>
<node id="Ribs">
  <data key="d0">Ribs</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ribs are bones separated during heart valve replacement surgery to allow opening of the chest.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67802df86489f08c4cf899e4cdd599e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404587</data>
</node>
<node id="Neurological Examination">
  <data key="d0">Neurological Examination</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Neurological Examination</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67802df86489f08c4cf899e4cdd599e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404587</data>
</node>
<node id="Echocardiography...&quot; that is fine. The incomplete line is after that; there is a dangling &quot;relation">
  <data key="d0">Echocardiography..." that is fine. The incomplete line is after that; there is a dangling "relation</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67802df86489f08c4cf899e4cdd599e</data>
  <data key="d2">" (no fields). So we need to discard that incomplete line and not output it. No need to re-output the correct Echocardiography line unless we think it's correct as is. Probably fine.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404593</data>
</node>
<node id="Heimlich Maneuver">
  <data key="d0">Heimlich Maneuver</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An emergency procedure, also called abdominal thrusts, used to remove a foreign object lodged in the airway by applying upward pressure on a conscious adult.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed5025da8263f838bf3c6848afbffd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404597</data>
</node>
<node id="Abdominal Thrusts">
  <data key="d0">Abdominal Thrusts</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A synonym for the Heimlich maneuver that describes the upward thrusts applied to the abdomen to expel an airway obstruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed5025da8263f838bf3c6848afbffd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404597</data>
</node>
<node id="Foreign Object">
  <data key="d0">Foreign Object</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An object that becomes lodged in the airway and can cause choking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed5025da8263f838bf3c6848afbffd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404597</data>
</node>
<node id="Airway Obstruction">
  <data key="d0">Airway Obstruction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A blockage of the airway caused by a foreign object that prevents normal breathing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed5025da8263f838bf3c6848afbffd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404597</data>
</node>
<node id="Airway">
  <data key="d0">Airway</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The passage through which air moves to the lungs, which can become obstructed during choking.&lt;SEP&gt;The airway is the passage through which air (and blood or sputum in hemoptysis) moves.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5025da8263f838bf3c6848afbffd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404943</data>
</node>
<node id="Rescuer">
  <data key="d0">Rescuer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The individual who stands behind the victim, encircles the waist, and applies pressure to perform the Heimlich maneuver.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed5025da8263f838bf3c6848afbffd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404597</data>
</node>
<node id="Victim">
  <data key="d0">Victim</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The conscious adult who is choking and on whom the Heimlich maneuver is performed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed5025da8263f838bf3c6848afbffd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404597</data>
</node>
<node id="Trained Volunteer">
  <data key="d0">Trained Volunteer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A person who can be trained to successfully apply the Heimlich maneuver.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed5025da8263f838bf3c6848afbffd2d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404598</data>
</node>
<node id="Hemophilus Infections">
  <data key="d0">Hemophilus Infections</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemophilus infections are a group of contagious gram‑negative bacterial diseases affecting humans, potentially fatal, affecting multiple body systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404687</data>
</node>
<node id="Haemophilus Influenzae">
  <data key="d0">Haemophilus Influenzae</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Haemophilus influenzae is a gram‑negative bacterium commonly found in nasal secretions and the primary cause of hemophilus infections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404687</data>
</node>
<node id="Haemophilus Influenzae B (Hib)">
  <data key="d0">Haemophilus Influenzae B (Hib)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Haemophilus influenzae b is a strain of H. influenzae that was historically the most common cause of bacterial meningitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404687</data>
</node>
<node id="PRP‑D Vaccine">
  <data key="d0">PRP‑D Vaccine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">PRP‑D is a vaccine used in children older than 15 months to prevent hemophilus infections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404687</data>
</node>
<node id="HBOC Vaccine">
  <data key="d0">HBOC Vaccine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HBOC is a vaccine administered to infants at two, four, and six months to prevent hemophilus infections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404687</data>
</node>
<node id="PRP‑OMP Vaccine">
  <data key="d0">PRP‑OMP Vaccine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">PRP‑OMP is a vaccine used to immunize children against hemophilus infections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404687</data>
</node>
<node id="Bacterial Sepsis">
  <data key="d0">Bacterial Sepsis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bacterial sepsis is a potentially fatal bloodstream infection that can result from hemophilus infection, especially in newborns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404688</data>
</node>
<node id="Conjunctivitis">
  <data key="d0">Conjunctivitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Conjunctivitis is inflammation of the eye caused by H. influenzae infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404688</data>
</node>
<node id="Cellulitis">
  <data key="d0">Cellulitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cellulitis is a bacterial skin infection that can result from H. influenzae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404688</data>
</node>
<node id="Infectious Arthritis">
  <data key="d0">Infectious Arthritis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infectious arthritis is joint inflammation caused by bacterial infection such as H. influenzae.&lt;SEP&gt;Infectious arthritis is a serious joint infection characterized by pain, fever, inflammation, swelling, and loss of function, considered a medical emergency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7a69ca28e7676455bc1dd105b09f56c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786411979</data>
</node>
<node id="Sinusitis">
  <data key="d0">Sinusitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sinusitis is inflammation of the sinuses associated with H. influenzae infection, featuring fever, pain, bad breath, and coughing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404688</data>
</node>
<node id="Empyema">
  <data key="d0">Empyema</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Empyema is a collection of pus in the pleural space that can occur during H. influenzae infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404688</data>
</node>
<node id="Respiratory Tract">
  <data key="d0">Respiratory Tract</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The respiratory tract is the body system most commonly affected by hemophilus infections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404688</data>
</node>
<node id="Late Winter">
  <data key="d0">Late Winter</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Late winter is a seasonal period during which hemophilus infections in the United States are most likely to spread.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404689</data>
</node>
<node id="Early Spring">
  <data key="d0">Early Spring</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Early spring is a seasonal period associated with increased spread of hemophilus infections in the United States.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404689</data>
</node>
<node id="Person‑to‑Person Contact">
  <data key="d0">Person‑to‑Person Contact</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Person‑to‑person contact is a transmission route for hemophilus infections through close interaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404689</data>
</node>
<node id="Nasal Discharges">
  <data key="d0">Nasal Discharges</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nasal discharges are bodily fluids that can carry H. influenzae and facilitate transmission of hemophilus infections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404689</data>
</node>
<node id="Newborn Infants">
  <data key="d0">Newborn Infants</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Newborn infants are a vulnerable population that can acquire hemophilus infection leading to bacterial sepsis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbc235c34c37663eef619f2c8affbe76</data>
