<node id="Hemochromatosis">
  <data key="d0">Hemochromatosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemochromatosis is an inherited blood disorder that causes excessive iron retention in the body and is classified as severe.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemochromatosis is a blood disorder that may be treated with therapeutic phlebotomy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d89439564ae2dc33beae4237976b40b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d78fea89c4fad7d739948de01e91d4a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420560</data>
</node>
<node id="Iron Overload">
  <data key="d0">Iron Overload</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Iron overload is the condition of retaining excessive amounts of iron and is an alternate name for hemochromatosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d78fea89c4fad7d739948de01e91d4a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404755</data>
</node>
<node id="Bronze Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Bronze Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bronze diabetes is an alternate name for hemochromatosis mentioned in the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d78fea89c4fad7d739948de01e91d4a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404755</data>
</node>
<node id="Hereditary Hemochromatosis">
  <data key="d0">Hereditary Hemochromatosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hereditary hemochromatosis is an alternate name for hemochromatosis indicated in the description.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d78fea89c4fad7d739948de01e91d4a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404755</data>
</node>
<node id="Familial Hemochromatosis">
  <data key="d0">Familial Hemochromatosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Familial hemochromatosis is another synonym for hemochromatosis noted in the entry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d78fea89c4fad7d739948de01e91d4a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404755</data>
