<node id="Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI)">
  <data key="d0">Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) is a diagnostic imaging method used to assess hemochromatosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) is a diagnostic imaging method used to investigate complications associated with piercing and tattoos.&lt;SEP&gt;Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) is an imaging technique that uses a magnetic field and radio waves to generate internal body images, employed in diagnosing Progressive Supranuclear Palsy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d78fea89c4fad7d739948de01e91d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8db2289714a65b14031455c87d3fc259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2408b24dbbf82011285a46aaece84afd</data>
