<node id="Polycythemia Vera">
  <data key="d0">Polycythemia Vera</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Polycythemia vera is a blood disorder marked by excessive production of red blood cells and high hemoglobin levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Polycythemia Vera is a chronic blood disorder characterized by an abnormal increase in red blood</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf22957a0e865e34a0996f2ddcc2608</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422600</data>
</node>
<node id="General Physical Examination">
  <data key="d0">General Physical Examination</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">General physical examination is a routine medical assessment during which a hemoglobin test may be performed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404823</data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure Application">
  <data key="d0">Pressure Application</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pressure application is a technique of applying force to a puncture site to stop bleeding and reduce bruising.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80e03e36082a52818b6740d8905c8a42</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404824</data>
</node>
<node id="Massive Hemoptysis">
  <data key="d0">Massive Hemoptysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Massive hemoptysis is a life‑threatening emergency characterized by severe bleeding from the lungs.&lt;SEP&gt;Massive hemoptysis is defined as 200–600 mL of blood coughed up within 24 hours or less, representing a severe form of hemoptysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-145bdf1ac68f0b5798dcddc645b482c1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404943</data>
</node>
<node id="Hemolytic-Uremic Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Hemolytic-Uremic Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemolytic-Uremic Syndrome is a severe disease characterized by red blood cell destruction, vascular damage, and possible kidney failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-434d8d551fe8baa35b0eb7738c2dec25</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404893</data>
</node>
<node id="Escherichia Coli">
  <data key="d0">Escherichia Coli</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Escherichia coli is a bacterium whose infection can lead to Hemolytic-Uremic Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-434d8d551fe8baa35b0eb7738c2dec25</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404893</data>
</node>
<node id="Stool Culture">
  <data key="d0">Stool Culture</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stool culture is a diagnostic method used within 48 hours of bloody diarrhea to detect Escherichia coli infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-434d8d551fe8baa35b0eb7738c2dec25</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404893</data>
</node>
<node id="Antimotility Agents">
  <data key="d0">Antimotility Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Antimotility agents are drugs that reduce intestinal movement and may worsen an Escherichia coli infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-434d8d551fe8baa35b0eb7738c2dec25</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404893</data>
</node>
<node id="Day Care">
  <data key="d0">Day Care</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Day care facilities are child‑care settings that children with suspected infection should avoid until stool cultures are negative.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-434d8d551fe8baa35b0eb7738c2dec25</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404894</data>
</node>
<node id="Bloody Diarrhea">
  <data key="d0">Bloody Diarrhea</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bloody diarrhea is a symptom described as bloody stool that prompts stool culture testing within 48 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-434d8d551fe8baa35b0eb7738c2dec25</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404894</data>
</node>
<node id="Red Blood Cell Destruction">
  <data key="d0">Red Blood Cell Destruction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Destruction of red blood cells is a hallmark pathological feature of Hemolytic-Uremic Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-434d8d551fe8baa35b0eb7738c2dec25</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404894</data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Vessel Wall Damage">
  <data key="d0">Blood Vessel Wall Damage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Damage to the lining of blood vessel walls is a characteristic complication of Hemolytic-Uremic Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-434d8d551fe8baa35b0eb7738c2dec25</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404894</data>
</node>
<node id="Supportive Care">
  <data key="d0">Supportive Care</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Supportive care involves fluid and electrolyte management and is the primary treatment approach for Hemolytic-Uremic Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-434d8d551fe8baa35b0eb7738c2dec25</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404894</data>
</node>
<node id="Sputum">
  <data key="d0">Sputum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sputum is the mucus expelled from the respiratory tract, which may be bloody in hemoptysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786404943</data>
</node>
<node id="Chest Pain">
  <data key="d0">Chest Pain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chest pain is a possible symptom that may accompany hemoptysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Chest Pain is a symptom associated with pleural effusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-448825a5baf21347c5a8fd84c362669b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bc0e87b467a3072004e86dd7a21ec8c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786422150</data>
</node>
<node id="Heart Abnormalities">
  <data key="d0">Heart Abnormalities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
