<node id="Hepatitis C">
  <data key="d0">Hepatitis C</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatitis C is an inflammatory disease of the liver caused by infection with the Hepatitis C Virus.&lt;SEP&gt;Hepatitis C is another type of viral hepatitis referenced as distinct from hepatitis B.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edba73be60673b1668775ee43b5d8dd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405094</data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatitis C Virus">
  <data key="d0">Hepatitis C Virus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatitis C Virus is a spherical, single-stranded RNA virus belonging to the Flaviviridae family that causes Hepatitis C.&lt;SEP&gt;HCV, one of the three most common hepatitis viruses causing liver disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af13d6b5d2273ae3dfeff4d407f3bf78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405234</data>
</node>
<node id="Acute Phase">
  <data key="d0">Acute Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The acute phase is the first six months of Hepatitis C infection, during which some individuals may clear the virus.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute phase refers to the early stage of drug‑induced hepatitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405308</data>
</node>
<node id="Chronic Phase">
  <data key="d0">Chronic Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The chronic phase follows the acute phase and can persist long-term in Hepatitis C infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405022</data>
</node>
<node id="Doctors">
  <data key="d0">Doctors</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Doctors are medical professionals who manage diagnosis and treatment of Hepatitis C patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctors are medical professionals who are familiar with preventing drug‑induced hepatitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctors are clinicians who have recognized that humans can continue to grow and that most patients with personality disorders are treatable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b20a7bdac3dcdeae955d7f5fcff8809</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420001</data>
</node>
<node id="Researchers">
  <data key="d0">Researchers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Researchers invented a new test in 1992 to detect Hepatitis C Virus in blood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405022</data>
</node>
<node id="HCV Test">
  <data key="d0">HCV Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The HCV Test is a diagnostic method developed in 1992 to check blood for Hepatitis C Virus RNA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405023</data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatitis C Vaccine">
  <data key="d0">Hepatitis C Vaccine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Hepatitis C Vaccine is an experimental vaccine that entered an early clinical trial in 2012 to prevent infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405023</data>
</node>
<node id="New Drugs">
  <data key="d0">New Drugs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">New drugs are therapeutic agents that improve prognosis for chronic Hepatitis C by reducing viral load and liver damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405023</data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Trial">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Clinical Trial in 2012 evaluated the safety and efficacy of the Hepatitis C Vaccine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405023</data>
</node>
<node id="Flu-like Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Flu-like Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Flu-like syndrome is a collection of mild symptoms such as fatigue, poor appetite, and nausea observed in some Hepatitis C patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405023</data>
</node>
<node id="Liver Cancer">
  <data key="d0">Liver Cancer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Liver cancer is a malignant tumor that may develop as a complication of chronic Hepatitis C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405024</data>
</node>
<node id="Liver Transplant">
  <data key="d0">Liver Transplant</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Liver transplant is a surgical procedure considered when liver failure occurs due to chronic Hepatitis C.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver transplant is a surgical procedure referenced in the prognosis of Primary Biliary Cirrhosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eff6cb4281c913c830bd641c706365c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb339d7a28b5edfc594d9ad14afee5c</data>
