<node id="Hepatitis B">
  <data key="d0">Hepatitis B</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatitis B is a viral infection of the liver transmitted through blood or body fluids, classified as a severe disease/condition.&lt;SEP&gt;A contagious virus that can be transmitted from mother to baby and cause perinatal infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2679367b0beba9113c18be86c1ebf3c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edba73be60673b1668775ee43b5d8dd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420096</data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatitis A">
  <data key="d0">Hepatitis A</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatitis A is a viral hepatitis disease mentioned as being preventable by vaccination.&lt;SEP&gt;Hepatitis A is an infectious disease of the liver caused by the HAV virus, transmitted through contaminated food, water, or close human contact.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97bc31370eb8948b543aaf5f06eb9116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edba73be60673b1668775ee43b5d8dd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405386</data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatitis B Virus">
  <data key="d0">Hepatitis B Virus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">HBV is the DNA virus that causes hepatitis B and contains antigens that trigger immune responses.&lt;SEP&gt;HBV, known as serum hepatitis, one of the most common hepatitis viruses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af13d6b5d2273ae3dfeff4d407f3bf78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edba73be60673b1668775ee43b5d8dd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405234</data>
</node>
<node id="DNA Virus">
  <data key="d0">DNA Virus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DNA virus denotes a class of viruses with deoxyribonucleic acid as genetic material, exemplified by HBV.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8edba73be60673b1668775ee43b5d8dd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405094</data>
</node>
<node id="RNA Viruses">
  <data key="d0">RNA Viruses</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RNA viruses are viruses with ribonucleic acid genomes, including other hepatitis-causing viruses besides HBV.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8edba73be60673b1668775ee43b5d8dd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405094</data>
</node>
<node id="Antigen">
  <data key="d0">Antigen</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antigen refers to fragments of HBV that stimulate the immune system to produce antibodies.&lt;SEP&gt;An antigen is a substance that elicits an immune response, such as HLA molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;An antigen is a foreign substance that induces an immune response, leading to antibody production in hypersensitivity pneumonitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Antigen is any protein that triggers the immune system to produce antibodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Antigen is a key term related to the immune system.&lt;SEP&gt;Antigen is a key term associated with Provenge, indicating its target in immunotherapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59ae7c2e485dd251483e45f48ced8031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6007bd886198fad2e92df82e7baf0b56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8edba73be60673b1668775ee43b5d8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8049c6dc0f71e37cbd8d3611d0687a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3519af09df48250c19cedc50f317f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeb4dffb5ad505f4839faaa747910b3c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786425689</data>
