<node id="Liver Cells">
  <data key="d0">Liver Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Liver cells are the cellular components destroyed by HBV and HDV infection and later replaced by scar tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f6deb35c161bfdda7d3d14623d9a411</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405261</data>
</node>
<node id="Drug-Induced Hepatitis">
  <data key="d0">Drug-Induced Hepatitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Drug-Induced Hepatitis is a disease characterized by liver inflammation caused by an adverse reaction to a drug.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405306</data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatotoxins">
  <data key="d0">Hepatotoxins</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatotoxins are harmful substances that can cause liver damage when present in certain drugs, leading to drug-induced hepatitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405306</data>
</node>
<node id="Toxic Hepatitis">
  <data key="d0">Toxic Hepatitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Toxic hepatitis is a type of drug-induced hepatitis that occurs when hepatotoxins cause liver damage in anyone who takes the offending drug.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405306</data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic Idiosyncrasy">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic Idiosyncrasy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic idiosyncrasy is a form of drug-induced hepatitis that occurs only in individuals who metabolize a drug differently, producing harmful by‑products that damage the liver.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405306</data>
</node>
<node id="Immunologic Idiosyncrasy">
  <data key="d0">Immunologic Idiosyncrasy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Immunologic idiosyncrasy is a form of drug-induced hepatitis that occurs only in individuals with an immune‑mediated response to a drug, leading to liver damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405306</data>
</node>
<node id="HDV Infection">
  <data key="d0">HDV Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HDV infection is a type of hepatitis that commonly causes cirrhosis in children with viral hepatitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405306</data>
</node>
<node id="Delta Hepatitis">
  <data key="d0">Delta Hepatitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Delta hepatitis is a form of hepatitis that can develop in a pregnant woman.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405307</data>
</node>
<node id="Child">
  <data key="d0">Child</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A child is a young patient who may develop cirrhosis when viral hepatitis is complicated by HDV infection.&lt;SEP&gt;A child is the patient described with impetigo, for whom prognosis is excellent and treatment considerations are discussed.&lt;SEP&gt;Child is a minor who may be evaluated for inhalant intoxication or dependence.&lt;SEP&gt;Child denotes a young patient whose eyes are photographed during Photoscreening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5212ecff28a486ed3ab5e22a14c8388f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db6c2b2025b59f4b58a91f35ae965a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57c6e499d18c8c0449bb5da48fdad5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f9159512d902b809ff6ebeca7cf146</data>
