<node id="Hiccups">
  <data key="d0">Hiccups</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hiccups is a disease/condition characterized by involuntary spasmodic contraction of the diaphragm followed by closure of the throat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9098e6c377264351e34498ab20d1d2b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405751</data>
</node>
<node id="Phrenic Nerve">
  <data key="d0">Phrenic Nerve</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The phrenic nerve carries sensory signals from the diaphragm to the spinal cord and transmits motor commands to control diaphragm contraction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9098e6c377264351e34498ab20d1d2b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405751</data>
</node>
<node id="Vagus Nerve">
  <data key="d0">Vagus Nerve</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The vagus nerve transmits sensory information from the diaphragm and throat to the spinal cord and brain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9098e6c377264351e34498ab20d1d2b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786405751</data>
</node>
<node id="Spinal Cord">
  <data key="d0">Spinal Cord</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The spinal cord relays sensory information from the diaphragm via the phrenic and vagus nerves to the brain.&lt;SEP&gt;Spinal cord is the part of the central nervous system from which CSF is collected.&lt;SEP&gt;Spinal cord is a part of the nervous system that can be involved in decompression sickness, leading to partial paralysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9098e6c377264351e34498ab20d1d2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a89a85dc3be8d37412b0c61ebf99cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93e4004c7edfa4a3c9a928142916ec61</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426683</data>
</node>
