<node id="Human Leukocyte Antigen Gene Products">
  <data key="d0">Human Leukocyte Antigen Gene Products</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HLA gene products are antigens classified into Class I, II, and III, located on various loci and expressed on nucleated cells and immune cells.&lt;SEP&gt;HLA gene products are antigens classified into Class I, Class II, and Class III groups and are expressed on various cell types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59ae7c2e485dd251483e45f48ced8031</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409380</data>
</node>
<node id="Class I Molecules">
  <data key="d0">Class I Molecules</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Class I molecules are HLA antigens encoded by the HLA-A, HLA-B, and HLA-C loci and are found on all nucleated cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Class I molecules are HLA antigens encoded by HLA-A, HLA-B, and HLA-C loci and are found on all nucleated cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59ae7c2e485dd251483e45f48ced8031</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409380</data>
</node>
<node id="Class II Molecules">
  <data key="d0">Class II Molecules</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Class II molecules are HLA antigens encoded by HLA-DR, HLA-DQ, and HLA-DP loci and are normally expressed on B-lymphocytes, macrophages, monocytes, dendritic cells, endothelial cells, and activated T-lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;Class II molecules are HLA antigens encoded by the HLA-DR, HLA-DQ, and HLA-DP loci and are normally found on B‑lymphocytes, macrophages, monocytes, dendritic cells, endothelial cells, and activated T‑lymphocytes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59ae7c2e485dd251483e45f48ced8031</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409380</data>
</node>
<node id="Class III Molecules">
  <data key="d0">Class III Molecules</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Class III molecules are HLA-related proteins that are not evaluated in histocompatibility testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Class III molecules are HLA‑related proteins that are not evaluated in histocompatibility testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59ae7c2e485dd251483e45f48ced8031</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
