  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inactivity is a lifestyle factor that contributes to hyperlipoproteinemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09ac7fad90c3ef5bbb1366ea8a473928</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409944</data>
</node>
<node id="LDL Cholesterol">
  <data key="d0">LDL Cholesterol</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">LDL cholesterol is a measured blood lipid value whose acceptable limit is 130 mg/dL and recommended goal is less than 100 mg/dL by NCEP ATP III.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3cd4e9159e066f72729a8b0e6c804cc7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409958</data>
</node>
<node id="HDL Cholesterol">
  <data key="d0">HDL Cholesterol</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">HDL cholesterol is a measured blood lipid value obtained accurately after a fasting blood test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3cd4e9159e066f72729a8b0e6c804cc7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409959</data>
</node>
<node id="Total Cholesterol">
  <data key="d0">Total Cholesterol</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Total cholesterol represents the overall cholesterol concentration measured from a fasting blood specimen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3cd4e9159e066f72729a8b0e6c804cc7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786409959</data>
</node>
<node id="Fasting">
  <data key="d0">Fasting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fasting is a 12‑hour abstention from food and drink required before a blood test to accurately measure LDL and HDL cholesterol.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting is the state of not eating or drinking, recommended from midnight before the PRA test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3cd4e9159e066f72729a8b0e6c804cc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35c30232e67a5a9d2bf59484035c1a03</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786421623</data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperemesis Gravidarum">
  <data key="d0">Hyperemesis Gravidarum</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperemesis gravidarum is a severe disease/condition characterized by excessive vomiting during pregnancy, leading to dehydration and weight loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410001</data>
</node>
<node id="Morning Sickness">
  <data key="d0">Morning Sickness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Morning sickness refers to common nausea and vomiting experienced by up to 80% of pregnancies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410001</data>
</node>
<node id="First Pregnancy">
  <data key="d0">First Pregnancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">First pregnancy denotes a woman's initial gestation, which is associated with a higher incidence of hyperemesis gravidarum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410001</data>
</node>
<node id="Multiple Pregnancy">
  <data key="d0">Multiple Pregnancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multiple pregnancy involves carrying more than one fetus, such as twins or triplets, and is linked to higher risk of hyperemesis gravidarum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410001</data>
</node>
<node id="Severe Vomiting">
  <data key="d0">Severe Vomiting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Severe vomiting is an extreme, uncontrollable vomiting symptom seen in hyperemesis gravidarum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410001</data>
</node>
<node id="Unborn Baby">
  <data key="d0">Unborn Baby</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The unborn baby is the fetus that is generally not harmed by hyperemesis gravidarum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410002</data>
</node>
<node id="Electrolytes">
  <data key="d0">Electrolytes</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Electrolytes are substances in intravenous fluids that help conduct nerve signals and correct acid-base balance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410002</data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-Nausea Medication">
  <data key="d0">Anti-Nausea Medication</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti-nausea medication is a drug given by injection to stop vomiting in hyperemesis gravidarum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410002</data>
</node>
<node id="Sedative Medication">
  <data key="d0">Sedative Medication</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sedative medication is a drug administered to calm patients and reduce vomiting in hyperemesis gravidarum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410002</data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Medication">
  <data key="d0">Oral Medication</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral medication is a drug taken by mouth to control nausea and vomiting while reintroducing food.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410002</data>
</node>
<node id="Urine Sample">
  <data key="d0">Urine Sample</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Urine sample is a specimen collected for laboratory analysis to aid diagnosis of hyperemesis gravidarum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410002</data>
</node>
<node id="Healthy Baby">
  <data key="d0">Healthy Baby</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Healthy baby refers to a newborn that is typically not adversely affected by maternal hyperemesis gravidarum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410002</data>
</node>
<node id="Adequate Sleep">
  <data key="d0">Adequate Sleep</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adequate sleep is sufficient rest that may contribute to symptom improvement in hyperemesis gravidarum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cea23812b7285588a42ea7c6a323d1b6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410003</data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperopia">
  <data key="d0">Hyperopia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperopia (farsightedness) is a moderate ophthalmological condition where incoming light focuses behind the retina, causing difficulty seeing near objects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f54ec7015ee2d6dc6b93427b653bc6f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410054</data>
</node>
<node id="Lens">
  <data key="d0">Lens</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The lens is a transparent dense component of the eye’s lens system that refracts light to focus images onto the retina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f54ec7015ee2d6dc6b93427b653bc6f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410054</data>
</node>
<node id="Diopter">
  <data key="d0">Diopter</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Diopter is the unit used to quantify refractive error, including hyperopia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f54ec7015ee2d6dc6b93427b653bc6f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410054</data>
</node>
<node id="Corrective Lenses">
  <data key="d0">Corrective Lenses</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Corrective lenses, such as spectacles or contact lenses, are used to</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f54ec7015ee2d6dc6b93427b653bc6f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410054</data>
</node>
<node id="Coumadin">
  <data key="d0">Coumadin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Coumadin is a brand name alias for the anticoagulant Warfarin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-62a73fa69c77f67bef562f4f893763be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410071</data>
</node>
<node id="Lovenox">
  <data key="d0">Lovenox</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lovenox is a brand name alias for the low-molecular weight heparin Enoxaparin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-62a73fa69c77f67bef562f4f893763be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410071</data>
</node>
<node id="Obstruction of Veins and Arteries">
  <data key="d0">Obstruction of Veins and Arteries</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Obstruction of veins and arteries refers to blockage of blood vessels, noted as a risk associated with hypercoagulation disorders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-62a73fa69c77f67bef562f4f893763be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410071</data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Hemostasis">
  <data key="d0">Normal Hemostasis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Normal hemostasis is the physiological process that stops bleeding by forming clots at injury sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-62a73fa69c77f67bef562f4f893763be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410071</data>
</node>
<node id="Clot">
  <data key="d0">Clot</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A clot is a mass of blood components that forms to stop bleeding; increased clotting is characteristic of hypercoagulation disorders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-62a73fa69c77f67bef562f4f893763be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410071</data>
</node>
<node id="Recurrent Thrombosis">
  <data key="d0">Recurrent Thrombosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recurrent thrombosis denotes repeated formation of clots within vessels, a possible outcome of untreated hypercoagulation disorders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-62a73fa69c77f67bef562f4f893763be</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786410071</data>
</node>
<node id="Hypercoagulation Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Hypercoagulation Disorders</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-62a73fa69c77f67bef562f4f893763be</data>
