</node>
<node id="Influenza">
  <data key="d0">Influenza</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Influenza, also known as the flu or grippe, is a highly infectious respiratory disease caused by certain strains of the influenza virus, affecting respiratory and gastrointestinal systems and leading to severe symptoms and potential secondary infections.&lt;SEP&gt;A viral infection also called the flu, caused by viruses targeted by influenza vaccination.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f49c33435524f5d8ed6badce93b4057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc626b00afed53316810372730831c40</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412404</data>
</node>
<node id="Influenza Virus">
  <data key="d0">Influenza Virus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Influenza virus refers to the strains of virus that cause influenza when inhaled, attacking cells of the upper respiratory tract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc626b00afed53316810372730831c40</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412317</data>
</node>
<node id="Secondary Infections">
  <data key="d0">Secondary Infections</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Secondary infections are potentially life‑threatening infections that influenza victims become susceptible to following the primary illness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc626b00afed53316810372730831c40</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412317</data>
</node>
<node id="Spanish Flu Pandemic">
  <data key="d0">Spanish Flu Pandemic</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Spanish flu pandemic of 1918‑1919 was a global influenza outbreak that resulted in a very high death toll.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc626b00afed53316810372730831c40</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412317</data>
</node>
<node id="Annual Death Toll">
  <data key="d0">Annual Death Toll</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The annual death toll attributable to influenza and its complications averages 20,000 deaths in the United States.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc626b00afed53316810372730831c40</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412317</data>
