  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412424</data>
</node>
<node id="Internet">
  <data key="d0">Internet</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Internet is the global network of computers and services that is the primary object of addictive use in Internet addiction disorder.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4542d461496cd18b5417df49b1f50690</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412468</data>
</node>
<node id="Problematic Computer Use">
  <data key="d0">Problematic Computer Use</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Problematic computer use is an alternate name for Internet addiction disorder, describing excessive and dysfunctional use of computers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4542d461496cd18b5417df49b1f50690</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412468</data>
</node>
<node id="Pathological Computer Use">
  <data key="d0">Pathological Computer Use</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pathological computer use is another synonym for Internet addiction disorder, emphasizing maladaptive patterns of computer usage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4542d461496cd18b5417df49b1f50690</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412468</data>
</node>
<node id="Internet Overuse">
  <data key="d0">Internet Overuse</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Internet overuse refers to excessive use of the Internet that leads to functional impairment, used as an alternate term for Internet addiction disorder.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4542d461496cd18b5417df49b1f50690</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412468</data>
</node>
<node id="Intestinal Obstructions">
  <data key="d0">Intestinal Obstructions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intestinal obstructions, also called bowel obstructions, are partial or complete mechanical or non‑mechanical blockages of fluids or food in the small or large intestine, affecting people of all ages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Mechanical Intestinal Obstruction">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Intestinal Obstruction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mechanical intestinal obstruction is a type of obstruction where the bowel is physically blocked, preventing contents from passing, caused by volvulus, intussusception, hernias, impacted feces, abnormal tissue growth, foreign bodies, gallstones, or inflammatory bowel disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Non‑Mechanical Intestinal Obstruction">
  <data key="d0">Non‑Mechanical Intestinal Obstruction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Non‑mechanical intestinal obstruction is a type of obstruction not caused by physical blockage, often related to functional disorders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Volvulus">
  <data key="d0">Volvulus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Volvulus is a condition where the bowel twists on itself, causing a mechanical intestinal obstruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Intussusception">
  <data key="d0">Intussusception</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intussusception is a condition where a segment of the intestine telescopes into itself, leading to a mechanical obstruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Impacted Feces">
  <data key="d0">Impacted Feces</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Impacted feces are hardened stool trapped in the intestine, which can cause mechanical obstruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Abnormal Tissue Growth">
  <data key="d0">Abnormal Tissue Growth</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Abnormal tissue growth refers to tumors or other proliferative lesions that can block the intestines mechanically.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Foreign Bodies">
  <data key="d0">Foreign Bodies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Foreign bodies are external objects that enter the intestines, such as gallstones, and can cause mechanical obstruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Gallstones">
  <data key="d0">Gallstones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gallstones are crystalline formations that may enter the intestines and act as foreign bodies causing obstruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Inflammatory Bowel Disease">
  <data key="d0">Inflammatory Bowel Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inflammatory bowel disease, including Crohn’s disease, is a chronic condition that can lead to mechanical intestinal obstruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Barium Enema">
  <data key="d0">Barium Enema</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Barium enema is a diagnostic procedure where a suspension of barium sulfate is inserted rectally to visualize the intestinal tract on imaging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Barium Sulfate">
  <data key="d0">Barium Sulfate</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Barium sulfate is a white powder used as a contrast material in imaging studies such as barium enema.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="X‑ray">
  <data key="d0">X‑ray</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">X‑ray imaging is a radiographic technique used to detect intestinal obstruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412491</data>
</node>
<node id="Ultrasound Evaluation">
  <data key="d0">Ultrasound Evaluation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultrasound evaluation of the abdomen is a non‑invasive imaging method used to assess intestinal obstruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412492</data>
</node>
<node id="Z‑codes">
  <data key="d0">Z‑codes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Z‑codes are a category of ICD codes used for classification of conditions such as intestinal obstructions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-09934893a08d3cab96095297ececeeb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786412492</data>
