<node id="Surgical Procedures">
  <data key="d0">Surgical Procedures</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Surgical Procedures are medical operations that may cause blood clot formation and require monitoring of coagulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ec14d30df69d510d9dcaa9c0f8a32fd9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419126</data>
</node>
<node id="Patau Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Patau Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Patau Syndrome is a genetic disorder causing severe and variable internal and external abnormalities, including brain malformations, microcephaly, and organ defects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419190</data>
</node>
<node id="Trisomy 13">
  <data key="d0">Trisomy 13</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Trisomy 13 is a chromosomal anomaly involving an extra copy of chromosome 13, commonly underlying Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419190</data>
</node>
<node id="Full Trisomy 13">
  <data key="d0">Full Trisomy 13</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Full Trisomy 13 denotes the presence of three complete copies of chromosome 13 in all cells, leading to the most severe manifestations of Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419190</data>
</node>
<node id="Chromosomal Anomaly">
  <data key="d0">Chromosomal Anomaly</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A chromosomal anomaly is any deviation from the normal chromosome number or structure, influencing the severity and symptoms of Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419190</data>
</node>
<node id="Holoprosencephaly">
  <data key="d0">Holoprosencephaly</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Holoprosencephaly is a forebrain malformation where the brain fails to divide into lobes or hemispheres, observed in Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419190</data>
</node>
<node id="Microcephaly">
  <data key="d0">Microcephaly</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Microcephaly is an abnormally small head resulting from impaired brain development, present in many cases of Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419190</data>
</node>
<node id="Myelomeningocele">
  <data key="d0">Myelomeningocele</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Myelomeningocele is a defect in which the spinal cord protrudes through an opening in the vertebrae, occurring in Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419190</data>
</node>
<node id="Ultrasound Imaging">
  <data key="d0">Ultrasound Imaging</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultrasound imaging is a prenatal diagnostic technique used to detect structural abnormalities indicative of Patau Syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultrasound imaging is a diagnostic technique used to observe fetal development and determine gestational age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c63f65bb800d3d7fae8a0864fc3cdf3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786423566</data>
</node>
<node id="Karyotyping">
  <data key="d0">Karyotyping</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Karyotyping is a laboratory method that separates and visualizes chromosomes to confirm trisomy 13 in suspected Patau Syndrome cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419191</data>
</node>
<node id="Cleft Lip">
  <data key="d0">Cleft Lip</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cleft lip is a structural facial abnormality that can be surgically corrected in children with Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419191</data>
</node>
<node id="Cleft Palate">
  <data key="d0">Cleft Palate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cleft palate is a structural oral abnormality that may be surgically repaired in individuals with Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419191</data>
</node>
<node id="Special Formulas">
  <data key="d0">Special Formulas</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Special formulas are tailored nutritional preparations used to manage feeding difficulties in children with Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419191</data>
</node>
<node id="Vision Aids">
  <data key="d0">Vision Aids</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Vision aids are assistive devices used to support visual function in individuals affected by Patau Syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96db15f8221b080d39a0f8664e928222</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786419191</data>
</node>
