  <data key="d5">1786420560</data>
</node>
<node id="Finger Stick">
  <data key="d0">Finger Stick</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Finger stick is a method of obtaining a small blood sample by pricking the finger.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d89439564ae2dc33beae4237976b40b1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420560</data>
</node>
<node id="Thrombocytosis">
  <data key="d0">Thrombocytosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thrombocytosis is a blood disorder that may be treated with therapeutic phlebotomy.&lt;SEP&gt;Thrombocytosis is a condition characterized by high platelet count.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d89439564ae2dc33beae4237976b40b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c07ccd2ac226d52ffc3c4068cddb090e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786421632</data>
</node>
<node id="Arterial Collection">
  <data key="d0">Arterial Collection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Arterial collection is a method of obtaining blood from an artery, mentioned as possibly performed by a physician.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d89439564ae2dc33beae4237976b40b1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420561</data>
</node>
<node id="Phenylketonuria">
  <data key="d0">Phenylketonuria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phenylketonuria (PKU) is a rare metabolic disorder caused by deficiency of the hepatic enzyme phenylalanine hydroxylase, leading to toxic buildup of phenylalanine in blood and brain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167f22f2d8b7871f48b0a587c85a9186</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420664</data>
</node>
<node id="Phenylalanine Hydroxylase">
  <data key="d0">Phenylalanine Hydroxylase</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Phenylalanine hydroxylase (PAH) is a liver enzyme that normally converts the amino acid phenylalanine into tyrosine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167f22f2d8b7871f48b0a587c85a9186</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420664</data>
</node>
<node id="PAH Gene">
  <data key="d0">PAH Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The PAH gene encodes the phenylalanine hydroxylase enzyme; mutations in this gene cause phenylketonuria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167f22f2d8b7871f48b0a587c85a9186</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420664</data>
</node>
<node id="Chromosome 12">
  <data key="d0">Chromosome 12</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Chromosome 12 is the chromosome on which the PAH gene and its PKU‑related mutations are located in the human genome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167f22f2d8b7871f48b0a587c85a9186</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420664</data>
</node>
<node id="Guthrie Test">
  <data key="d0">Guthrie Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guthrie test (Guthrie bacterial inhibition assay) is a newborn screening method that measures phenylalanine levels in a blood spot to diagnose PKU.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167f22f2d8b7871f48b0a587c85a9186</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420664</data>
</node>
<node id="Dietary Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Dietary Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dietary therapy, also called nutrition therapy, is the primary treatment for PKU that restricts phenylalanine intake to prevent toxicity and support normal development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167f22f2d8b7871f48b0a587c85a9186</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420664</data>
</node>
<node id="Phenylalanine">
  <data key="d0">Phenylalanine</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phenylalanine is an amino acid that, when not properly metabolized due to PAH deficiency, accumulates to toxic levels in blood and brain of PKU patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167f22f2d8b7871f48b0a587c85a9186</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420664</data>
</node>
<node id="Tyrosine">
  <data key="d0">Tyrosine</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Tyrosine is the amino acid produced from phenylalanine by the action of phenylalanine hydroxylase.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167f22f2d8b7871f48b0a587c85a9186</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420664</data>
</node>
<node id="Autosomal Recessive Disorder">
  <data key="d0">Autosomal Recessive Disorder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An autosomal recessive disorder is a genetic condition, like PKU, that requires two copies of a mutated gene for the disease to manifest.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167f22f2d8b7871f48b0a587c85a9186</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420665</data>
</node>
<node id="Newborn Screening">
  <data key="d0">Newborn Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Newborn screening is a public health program that tests newborns for conditions such as PKU, often using the Guthrie test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167f22f2d8b7871f48b0a587c85a9186</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420665</data>
</node>
<node id="Nervous System Cells">
  <data key="d0">Nervous System Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nervous system cells are brain cells that are damaged by high phenylalanine levels in PKU patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167f22f2d8b7871f48b0a587c85a9186</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420665</data>
</node>
<node id="Phobias">
  <data key="d0">Phobias</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phobias are intense but unrealistic fears that can interfere with social, work, or daily activities and are classified as a disease/condition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-af3b4b939a2aeb8a2dffe85570c09b57</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786420674</data>
</node>
<node id="Social Phobia">
  <data key="d0">Social Phobia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Social Phobia is a type of phobia characterized by deep fear of being watched, judged, or embarrassed in social situations.</data>
