<node id="Pyloroplasty">
  <data key="d0">Pyloroplasty</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pyloroplasty is a surgical procedure that cuts and resutures the pylorus valve, relaxing and widening its muscular opening into the duodenum, used to treat high‑risk gastric or peptic". This is truncated and missing description, also missing many entities like "Gastrointestinal system", "Musculoskeletal system", "Infectious", "Peptic Ulcer Disease", "Gastric Ulcer", "Duodenal Ulcer", "Pyloric Sphincter", "Stomach", "Duodenum", "Small Intestine", "Ulcer", "ICD Category Z-codes", "Severity Level Moderate", "Entry Type Surgical Procedure", "Complications", "Recovery Area", "Anesthesia", "Patient", "Diagnosis", "Prognosis", "Prevention", "Key Terms: The presence of ulcer". Also relationships: Pyloroplasty treats Peptic Ulcer Disease, etc.&lt;SEP&gt;Pyloroplasty is a surgical procedure that cuts and resutures the pylorus valve, relaxing and widening its muscular opening (pyloric sphincter) into the duodenum, and is used to treat patients at high risk for gastric or peptic ulcer disease.</data>
