<node id="Zone Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Zone Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Zone therapy is a key term associated with reflexology, referring to the concept of treating the body through specific zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e261bddabf1598318602d5ab776f60c1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426920</data>
</node>
<node id="Full Thickness of Rectum">
  <data key="d0">Full Thickness of Rectum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The full thickness of the rectum refers to all layers of the rectal wall that protrude outward in complete prolapse (procidentia).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0caa0df876843ee924756d881922e0a8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426920</data>
</node>
<node id="Reflexologists">
  <data key="d0">Reflexologists</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Reflexologists are practitioners who work from maps of predefined pressure points on the hands and feet to perform reflexology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e261bddabf1598318602d5ab776f60c1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1786426921</data>
</node>
<node id="Illness">
  <data key="d0">Illness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Illness denotes a state of poor health that reflexology may help alleviate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e261bddabf1598318602d5ab776f60c1</data>
